window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 103","paragraphs":["Territory (2)","The oven was a cooking appliance with a remarkably long history.","One didn’t need to look far to understand its importance. Without ovens, Western civilization couldn’t even have produced bread, its staple food.","The oven was created to take fire-roasting to the next level.","Well, the true next step was probably putting food in a pot and boiling it, but that was beside the point.","What mattered was that possessing an oven had an enormous effect on my quality of life.","\"Wow.\"","I exclaimed in admiration as I looked at the deliciously cooked fish.","Even though it was a makeshift oven, it had cooked the fish evenly.","Whenever I grilled fish on the cast-iron pan, some parts ended up undercooked while others burned.","An oven, however, surrounded the food with heat from every direction, so it naturally cooked everything evenly.","’I might even be able to bake bread if I ever get the opportunity.’","I carefully carried the grilled fish, which made my mouth water just by looking at it.","I didn’t forget to wear gloves since I could easily burn myself.","I had even purchased a new pair of kitchen gloves from the auction house specifically for today.","Munch, munch.","\"Mm!\"","It tasted exactly as I had expected.","That was precisely why it was so delicious.","Even when I grilled it normally, the fish had tasted somewhat like meat. Now it tasted like actual meat.","It reminded me of the pork belly I used to splurge on while living alone and desperately saving every penny.","Of course, it wasn’t exactly the same. The texture was especially different.","Even so, its flavor was every bit as good as pork belly.","’Even the parts that look burned are tender inside.’","I would probably be using the oven often from now on.","I happily enjoyed my meal.","I didn’t forget to send a piece to each of the registered users who had helped me. This time, the recipients were Heavenly Demon and Passing Dwarf.","They also tasted the oven-roasted fish and praised it highly.","It was objectively delicious.","’How did people invent the oven?’","I gazed at the oven while eating the fish.","The firewood had burned away and was turning into charcoal, while thin wisps of smoke rose from the chimney.","The oven had made an enormous contribution to human cuisine.","Without ovens, there would be no bread.","’Could I make pizza with that?’","No.","That would be a luxury.","Unless I cultivated my own wheat and obtained eggs as well, it was nothing more than a pointless fantasy.","For now, I should be satisfied with oven-roasted fish.","The oven would be useful not only for cooking fish but also for reheating smoked meat.","\"La-la-la~\"","As my quality of life improved, my morale naturally rose with it.","An increase in morale also meant an increase in combat effectiveness.","While singing the oven’s praises, I planned my afternoon schedule.","’I should determine where the gorilla troop’s territory is.’","Rice Kraone, the final chronicler of the Kingdom of Balkan, had died by suicide.","However, the infection had already left him without hope of survival, meaning the gorilla troop was effectively responsible for his death.","I needed to determine the precise boundaries of the gorillas’ territory so they wouldn’t pose a threat to my safety.","’I’ll have to learn about gorilla behavior first...’","I didn’t know how gorillas had adapted to the Forest of Four Seasons.","In other words, I needed to consider the possibility that the behavior I already knew about had changed.","Still, knowing something was better than knowing nothing.","I sent a message to the person best suited to answer my questions.","[Allfather: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: I wanted to ask you about gorilla behavior.]","[Allfather: Gorillas? Ah. It seems you discovered how the book’s owner died.]","Apparently, the information NecromancyIsLove had given me was genuine.","Did that mean I accepted his claim that he was the Immortal King?","No.","I could simply assume that an intelligent person was engaging in elaborate role-play.","Even if he truly was the Immortal King, it didn’t particularly matter.","[Wild Grylls: Allfather? Are you still there?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. I heard there’s a gorilla territory nearby. I also have a vague idea of where it is.]","[Allfather: Among primates, including humans, gorillas are exceptionally unaggressive and nonconfrontational. Naturally, this varies by subspecies, but that is generally the case.]","[Wild Grylls: Does that mean they’re safe?]","[Allfather: Not necessarily. If a gorilla reveals itself, it generally means you have intruded upon its territory. Furthermore, considering how the book’s owner died, you cannot afford to let your guard down.]","So I ultimately had no choice but to be careful.","I should avoid entering their territory if at all possible.","However, I had no idea where their territory began or ended.","Animals commonly marked their territory with excrement.","It seemed I would have to search carefully for their droppings.","’I’ll have to bring Wonmo.’","Wonmo possessed an excellent sense of smell, so finding the droppings should be easy.","He happened to be bouncing around energetically instead of taking a nap, so I could bring him along.","I began composing a message to thank Allfather.","[Wild Grylls: Like humans? What did they do, specifically?]","[Allfather: First, they reportedly used \"tools.\" They carried animal bones in their hands and wielded them like clubs.]","[Wild Grylls: ...]","[Allfather: Incidentally, there is one aspect of these gorillas that concerns me.]","[Wild Grylls: Something that concerns you?]","[Allfather: According to the book, the gorillas behaved almost like humans.]","What was this, Planet of the Apes ?","Could gorillas really be that intelligent?","It was a terrifying thought.","One careless mistake, and they could smash my skull open with those bones.","What if they were also aggressive?","The entire gorilla troop might gang up on me and beat me senseless.","’...Should I just not go?’","Allfather’s warning dampened my enthusiasm.","My resolve faltered briefly, but I soon shook my head vigorously.","This was precisely when taking a risk was necessary.","There was an enormous difference between possessing information and remaining ignorant.","’I’ll only determine the boundaries of their territory.’","For now, that would be my sole objective.","I would do exactly that and nothing more.","Even if the territory contained a legendary medicinal herb, I intended to ignore it.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you for the advice. I’ll have to be careful.]","[Allfather: I don’t think you should enter their territory, even out of curiosity.]","[Wild Grylls: I only intend to determine where the boundary lies and then return.]","[Allfather: I see. Understood.]","After ending my conversation with Allfather, I prepared for the expedition.","It would be wise to prepare for the possibility that I might accidentally enter the gorillas’ territory.","’Gorillas are herbivores, right?’","Allfather had told me that gorillas survived by eating things such as tree bark.","Despite living on tree bark, they possessed the greatest physical strength among all primates.","I felt an irrational stab of envy but quickly dismissed it.","Humans possessed far greater intelligence than they did.","I packed a few fasting pills as a gesture of goodwill.","If the situation became tense, I planned to offer them the pills and earn their favor.","’Namu-Ppareumbo eats them without any trouble, so gorillas should too, right?’","Or perhaps I should purchase a banana.","When people thought of gorillas, bananas were the first fruit that came to mind.","Entertaining such pointless thoughts, I completed my preparations.","Namu-Ppareumbo climbed onto my back, while Wonmo eagerly urged me to get moving.","All that remained was to depart, but...","Grrrrumble!","\"Ah.\"","It seemed I would have to delay my departure for a moment.","***","Grylls set out to explore only after thoroughly relieving himself.","The cave he left behind was silent, with no presence to be felt anywhere.","Only the occasional crackling of the campfire broke the stillness.","Rustle! Rustle!","Then it happened.","The bushes lining the path toward the river—the opposite direction from the one Grylls had taken—began to shake.","At first, they trembled only slightly, but the movement soon became noticeable.","Swish—","Eventually, something emerged through the bushes.","It did not fully reveal itself, instead cautiously poking out only its face.","Its overall features resembled a human’s, but it had a flat nose and pitch-black skin.","Most tellingly, the hair covering parts of its face revealed that it was an ape.","\"...Ooh! Ooh!\"","After surveying Grylls’s shelter for some time, the ape let out a quiet call.","In response, the bushes shook even more violently than before.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","A troop of apes emerged—the very gorillas Grylls had been wary of.","The gorillas appeared to communicate through their distinctive calls before cautiously entering the shelter.","At first glance, they looked like ordinary gorillas. Upon closer inspection, however, several details set them apart.","The gorilla presumed to be their leader carried nothing, but the gorillas following him were armed with clubs.","Their weapons varied considerably. Some wielded bones, others pieces of wood, and a few even carried crudely fashioned stone axes.","It was clear that these creatures were fundamentally different from ordinary apes.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh.\"","\"Ooh-ooh.\"","The apes meticulously inspected Grylls’s shelter.","They examined the iron container holding the fish, the container filled with charcoal, and finally the oven.","\"Oookyaaagh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh?!\"","Suddenly, one of the gorillas screamed.","The others hurried toward him at the sound.","The gorilla was rolling on the ground while clutching his hand. In front of him stood the oven Grylls had recently constructed.","Apparently, he had put his hand inside before it had fully cooled and burned himself.","It was an accident caused by curiosity.","The leader hurried over and examined his condition.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","After assessing the injury, the leader pointed toward the iron container holding the fish.","It was as though he were telling the injured gorilla that the container held water and that he should quickly cool his hand.","The burned gorilla immediately plunged his hand into it.","Splash!","As soon as his hand entered the water, the gorilla’s face filled with relief.","The fish inside were startled and began splashing wildly, but he didn’t seem to care.","After briefly showing his relief, the leader carefully examined the oven.","Perhaps he noticed the appetizing scent lingering inside.","He brought his nose close to the opening and sniffed repeatedly.","However, he apparently couldn’t determine the oven’s purpose and merely tilted his head.","Eventually, he lost interest and turned his attention elsewhere.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","One of the gorillas pointed toward the iron container holding the fish.","It was an important source of food for Grylls.","However, the leader shook his head in refusal.","He appeared to be indicating that it would be difficult to carry.","Although disappointed, the other gorilla accepted his decision.","The leader turned away and continued surveying the shelter.","He soon discovered the laundry hanging from the clothesline.","\"Ooh.\"","The leader stared at the laundry before slowly pulling on it.","The makeshift clothesline couldn’t withstand the gorilla’s immense strength and collapsed helplessly.","The leader carefully examined the uniform PrincessCheonggu had given Grylls, then tossed it onto the ground.","He didn’t seem particularly interested in it.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","Just then, the gorillas exploring the cave rushed outside.","Unlike the burned gorilla’s earlier scream, these were cries of celebration.","When the leader showed interest in what they had found, the gorillas placed their discovery on the ground.","They had brought out the sack of fasting pills that currently served as Namu-Ppareumbo’s staple food.","\"Hmm...\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The gorillas urged their leader to make a decision.","However, the leader remained cautious.","He took one fasting pill from the sack and placed it in his mouth.","Before long, he began chewing it thoroughly.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh?! Ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","The leader’s eyes widened as he cried out in astonishment.","Anyone could tell that his reaction meant, \"Delicious.\"","His expression made it seem as though he had discovered the greatest delicacy in the world.","The other gorillas each placed a fasting pill in their mouths.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh?!\"","\"Oooook!\"","Like their leader, the other gorillas reacted with tremendous excitement.","To some, the pills were unbearably bitter emergency rations, but the gorillas apparently considered them an exquisite delicacy.","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","After eating several more pills, the gorillas quietly lifted the sack.","We can’t keep something this delicious to ourselves. Let’s share it with the rest of our troop.","The leader apparently agreed, as he picked up the sack without hesitation.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The gorilla troop then departed Grylls’s shelter.","They had not stolen the elixir, inner core, or any of the other treasures Grylls cherished, but the loss was still devastating.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Oblivious to that fact, the gorilla troop happily returned home."]},{"title":"Chapter 104","paragraphs":["Territory (3)","Territory was an extremely sensitive matter, whether for animals or humans.","In the broadest sense, a human’s territory was their country and its borders. On a smaller scale, it was their home.","Food, clothing, and shelter were all essential, but shelter was the element responsible for providing safety.","Without a home, people could never be safe from natural disasters and all manner of other dangers.","Therefore, both humans and animals required territory to live safely.","Even humans became wary or confrontational when strangers entered their homes. Animals would naturally react even more strongly.","I hadn’t set out to explore the forest and identify the gorillas’ territory for no reason.","’But considering the Owlbear and Mad Dog, there must be territorial conflicts between the animals too.’","Although I had set out confidently, there were more than a few things that concerned me.","First, what would happen to the territories that had belonged to the now-deceased Owlbear and Mad Dog?","I had considered that question several times, but nothing noteworthy had happened so far.","There had been a kangaroo inside the Owlbear’s cave, but it had fled upon seeing me.","Only now was I truly beginning to understand that other animals might move in to claim the vacant territories.","The saber-toothed tiger was a monster I had barely defeated with Namu-Ppareumbo’s assistance.","Had I fought it alone, I would have died several times over.","’If something is powerful enough to force its way into a saber-toothed tiger’s territory...’","It might have challenged the saber-toothed tiger even while it was alive.","Alternatively, it might already have become the dominant predator of this entire region.","’I’ve been consistently marking my territory too.’","Of course, I wasn’t being entirely serious.","I had simply been relieving myself wherever I pleased.","Even so, I believed it must have served as a territorial marker to some extent.","’This is the Owlbear’s cave.’","Retracing yesterday’s route, I arrived at the Owlbear’s cave.","I had originally planned to use this location as the starting point of my search.","That was before Wonmo dashed inside.","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuu!\"","I urgently called out to him, but he had already disappeared into the cave.","Shaking my head, I followed him inside.","\"Кkyaaagh! Kkyaagh!\"","However, Wonmo came racing back out before I had gone very far.","Judging by his terrified expression, something was inside.","After barely managing to calm the trembling Wonmo, I cautiously peered into the cave.","\"Oh.\"","I could understand why Wonmo was frightened.","The creatures inside were anything but ordinary.","It was the kangaroo I had seen yesterday.","It was hopping around inside the cave.","The problem was that there wasn’t just one. There were several of them.","Apparently, they had claimed this place as their territory.","Exactly what I had feared had happened.","A mob of kangaroos had taken over after the Owlbear’s death.","’But can kangaroos even survive in this kind of environment?’","Perhaps it was merely a preconception, but on Earth, kangaroos usually lived in Australia.","As long as they had grass, trees, and other sources of food, there was no reason they couldn’t survive here.","Even so, their presence felt oddly out of place.","Regardless of how I felt about it, I decided to withdraw quietly.","Fighting them now would only disadvantage me, and there were still many places I needed to investigate.","’If I want to escape, I’ll have to pass through other animals’ territories...’","That also bothered me.","I would inevitably have to trespass into territories belonging to other animals.","If I was unlucky, I might be forced to fight a series of battles against the creatures ruling those territories.","That was precisely why I needed more information.","’Wait. Come to think of it...’","I turned and looked back at the entrance to the former Owlbear nest.","I was thinking about Rice Kraone, the owner of the book I had found there.","’How was he able to live inside the Owlbear’s nest? Did he live there before the Owlbear arrived?’","Allfather would probably be able to tell me later.","After one last look at what had now become the kangaroos’ cave, I continued onward.","I still had no way of estimating where the gorillas’ territory might be.","It would have been convenient to use the area upriver as a reference, but even that was uncertain.","’The river itself could be part of their territory.’","It would be easier to treat this as both exploration and an attempt to determine territorial boundaries.","If I discovered any droppings along the way, I could stop immediately.","After all, I had an excellent detection dog—no, a detection bear—with me, so finding them should be easy.","Sniff, sniff.","\"Hey, Wonmo. That’s dirty. Don’t touch it.\"","That didn’t mean I wanted him to search for mushrooms.","Worried that Wonmo might eat one, I hurriedly stopped him.","Afterward, I continued exploring while carefully marking my route so I wouldn’t get lost.","As I proceeded, I suddenly realized that the terrain was gradually changing.","’This is practically a jungle rather than a forest.’","The leaves were becoming a deeper shade of green, and moss was growing increasingly abundant.","Moreover, while the forest floor had often consisted of stone rather than soil, at some point it had become covered entirely in tree roots.","Even the air had changed noticeably, particularly the humidity.","It had been somewhat dry moments ago, but at some point, it had become humid.","’I didn’t feel myself crossing into a different space.’","It wasn’t anything like the alien sensation I had experienced when crossing the river.","It merely felt as though I had gradually entered a jungle without noticing.","I considered turning back but decided to explore just a little farther.","\"Good lord. What the fuck?\"","Not long after making that decision, I discovered a new species.","A creature of unknown origin was steadily crawling forward.","Its appearance was unmistakably that of a snail.","The problem was its size.","Its shell alone was much larger than I was, to say nothing of its actual body.","’Is this what the snails from Maple World would look like?’","The sight of a human-sized snail crawling along was utterly horrifying.","At the same time, however, it puzzled me.","Wouldn’t a creature that large be quickly devoured?","’There must be a reason it survives.’","I shouldn’t touch it merely to satisfy my curiosity.","The wisest course was to let it continue on its way.","I passed the snail, which was crawling even more slowly than a sloth.","Not long afterward, I discovered exactly how it had managed to survive.","Hissssss—","The grass along the snail’s trail had completely melted.","As if that weren’t enough, even the soil appeared to have dissolved, with smoke rising from the ground.","The substance was probably poisonous like the Golden Poison Frog’s toxin, or perhaps acidic.","Considering the nature of snails, its entire body might be poisonous or acidic.","Anything that tried to eat it would probably melt into liquid.","’...I should name it the Acid Snail.’","Surely it couldn’t spit acid from its mouth like the frog, could it?","Just in case, I moved far away from the snail.","I continued exploring various parts of the jungle, but after finding nothing unusual, I eventually turned back.","’Do the gorillas not live here?’","Either they lived deeper inside, or I had searched in the wrong direction.","Wonmo hadn’t found anything either, so it felt like the entire excursion had been a waste.","’There’s...still plenty of time.’","When I checked the Gallery clock, it was only two thirty.","I had planned to continue exploring until five at the latest, so I could afford to search a little longer.","However, as a precaution, I decided not to reenter the jungle.","It would be disastrous if I encountered the gorillas.","\"Hmm?\"","Just as I resolved to return, I discovered something strange.","It was a tree with a deep depression in the center of its trunk.","Since fights constantly broke out in the Forest of Four Seasons, finding a damaged tree wasn’t unusual.","However, the mark carved into this particular tree stood out.","’Could this be...a handprint?’","A distinct handprint had been imprinted on the trunk.","I couldn’t tell much about it, but it certainly didn’t appear to belong to a human.","I didn’t know what kind of ape had made it. I wasn’t an expert.","There were only two things I could determine.","It was much larger than my hand, and its proportions differed from those of a human hand.","The palm was much larger than the fingers, while the hand itself was more than twice the size of mine.","’...This might be a territorial marker.’","I examined the impression, which was large enough to engulf my entire hand.","If a gorilla had truly made this mark, it would be best to leave immediately.","If I wandered around unnecessarily, I might be ambushed.","’Are there any other marks?’","However, I felt the urge to determine the territorial boundary more precisely.","I couldn’t allow a single handprint to frighten me into doing nothing.","Just as I was about to turn my head—","\"Huh?\"","My fingertips brushed against another indentation.","There was a second mark beside the large handprint.","The tree was so thick that I had nearly overlooked it.","However, there was another reason I was surprised.","’This one...really looks like a human handprint.’","A much smaller handprint had been carved beside the larger one.","Although it was still bigger than mine, its size was within the limits of an ordinarily large human hand.","I wondered if it belonged to an adolescent gorilla, but that didn’t seem right either.","’The fingers are long.’","Its fingers were unusually long.","The difference became obvious when the two prints were compared.","Could it have belonged to Rice, who had been attacked by the gorilla troop?","That didn’t seem right either.","I didn’t know why, but the prints gave me a sense of companionship.","It was almost as though the two owners had made them to display their bond.","After carefully examining both handprints, I took a photograph.","I intended to upload it to the Gallery later.","\"They seem pretty old...but I don’t know.\"","I couldn’t tell whether the smaller print had been left by a survivor or a mutant.","Still pondering the mystery, I headed out of the jungle.","I couldn’t remain there any longer.","’I have something to think about, so I should return to the shelter.’","I wanted to continue exploring, but I changed my plans.","After all, I had discovered a mark that might have belonged to a survivor.","Furthermore, it belonged to a survivor other than Rice.","’Why would someone leave a handprint? And why beside a gorilla’s?’","Still contemplating that baffling question, I returned to the shelter.","The moment I arrived, all the tension drained from my body.","\"Hmm?\"","Something was strange.","I sensed an inexplicable incongruity.","What was causing it?","I couldn’t identify it at all.","Everything was familiar, yet something felt wrong. The positions of various objects seemed to have changed slightly.","\"Why has the laundry rack fallen over? Did I fail to secure it properly?\"","The first oddity was the laundry I had hung up, which was now scattered across the ground.","The iron container’s position seemed to have changed slightly, and something about the charcoal container also looked strange.","There were signs throughout the shelter that someone had visited, putting me on guard.","’There’s no one inside, though.’","I cautiously peered into the cave, but no one was there.","For a moment, I had thought an intruder might still be hiding inside.","I rubbed the back of my neck before lowering my weapons and entering the cave.","The instant I stepped inside, the feeling that something was wrong became far stronger.","No.","It wasn’t merely a feeling.","One of my belongings had completely disappeared.","\"Huh?\"","I usually kept everything neatly organized so that it would be easy to find.","Therefore, I immediately realized what was missing.","\"What the hell? Where are the fasting pills?\"","The fasting pills were gone.","The entire sack had disappeared.","Since Namu-Ppareumbo was the one who primarily ate them, I always kept them in one specific place.","If they had vanished, there could be only one explanation.","Someone had broken into my shelter and taken them.","The idea of a thief living in the forest seemed absurd, but it wasn’t unprecedented.","Hadn’t a raccoon stolen some fasting pills during the last torrential downpour?","Of course, Namu-Ppareumbo had taught that raccoon a painful lesson before it ended up inside Wonmo’s stomach.","\"...\"","Perhaps it was deeply shocked to hear that the fasting pills were gone.","Namu-Ppareumbo scrambled off my back at the fastest speed it could achieve outside combat.","It then stared blankly at the spot where the fasting pills had been.","I could vividly sense the devastation and fury radiating from it.","Who could have stolen the fasting pills?","Stranger still, the thief hadn’t touched anything else.","’Maybe they left footprints.’","Criminals always left traces behind.","Leaving the silently furious Namu-Ppareumbo inside, I stepped out of the cave.","When I carefully examined the ground, I discovered footprints that hadn’t been there before.","’I should upload these to the Gallery.’","I didn’t know who the culprit was, but...","’I’ve never seen Ppareumbo this angry before.’","It seemed the thief had nothing left to look forward to but death.","Meanwhile, somewhere in the jungle—","\"Ooh-ho-ho! Ooh-ho!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh! Ooh-hoo-hoo!\"","An impromptu gorilla feast was underway."]},{"title":"Chapter 105","paragraphs":["Hostage (1)","Whoever they were, they had seriously gotten on Namu-Ppareumbo’s bad side.","With that thought, I made a post on the gallery. This time, it wasn’t a handprint but footprints.","The handprint could wait. The urgent matter right now was identifying the culprit.","Aside from Namu-Ppareumbo’s staple food disappearing in its entirety, this was also a serious problem for me.","Whether they had deliberately waited until we were gone or it had simply been unfortunate timing, the incident had occurred during that brief window.","’At this rate, I won’t even be able to leave home whenever I want.’","Should I have installed an iron fence as well, knowing this might happen? I wasn’t sure.","Perhaps I should have built an actual door instead of a fence. It was something I needed to start considering.","Title: Anyone Know What Made These Footprints?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of animal footprints)","(Photo of animal footprints)","(Photo of Namu-Ppareumbo’s back, radiating emptiness and rage)","(Photo of Wonmo beside him, nervously watching his mood)","I went exploring today, and my fasting pills were gone when I returned.","These footprints seem to belong to the culprits. Does anyone recognize them? I’m asking because there seem to be several different kinds.","└ Heavenly Demon: They look more like handprints than footprints. More importantly, I can feel Namu-Ppareumbo’s fury through the photograph alone.","└ SwordMaster: I know, right? Wonmo cautiously watching him from the side is adorable too. Does he realize something terrible has happened?","└ Wild Grylls: Wonmo is surprisingly good at reading the room. By the way, Heavenly Demon, if it isn’t too much trouble, could I ask you for some more fasting pills?","└ Heavenly Demon: That itself is no problem, but it will take some time. The pills require rare medicinal herbs, so our supply is limited.","The moment I read that comment, I checked on Namu-Ppareumbo. He was still staring at the spot where the fasting pills had been.","For a person, would it feel like discovering that an entire pile of meat dishes had vanished?","And now he would have to eat nothing but vegetables and wild greens.","Thinking about it that way, I would be pissed too. Besides, this problem wasn’t limited to Namu-Ppareumbo.","’They trespassed into my territory and even stole my belongings.’","It was embarrassing to admit, but whenever nature called, I usually relieved myself nearby.","I wanted to mark my territory at least a little. Before that, I had always buried it with dirt.","However, since I would have to stay here for a long time, establishing territory of my own was unavoidable.","└ Starlight Princess: Stealing someone else’s food... What terrible creatures. What will you do if you find them?","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t have enough time to search for them today. I’ll have to look tomorrow.","└ Cheonggu Princess: The uniform is safe, right?","└ Wild Grylls: It was lying on the ground.","└ Cheonggu Princess: ...","└ Even animals rejected it, hahahahaha.","└ Animals won’t even touch Cheonggu’s uniform, lololol.","└ The design is admittedly a little lame, lol.","└ Forget the design, that deer emblem is just... hahaha.","└ Allfather: Hmm. Judging from the prints alone, they appear to belong to primates.","└ Wild Grylls: Primates?","└ Allfather: Yes. I cannot determine the exact species, but they are definitely primate prints.","└ Wild Grylls: Then there’s a high chance they’re gorillas. Do gorillas invade other creatures’ territories?","└ Allfather: That rarely happens. As I mentioned before, they possess low aggression and seldom fight outsiders unless there is internal conflict among their own group.","In other words, there was a high probability that the gorillas had undergone some kind of change.","Whether it involved increased aggression or something else, it wasn’t good news for me.","’And it looks like there was more than one...’","There were many footprints. Looking at them closely, each had a slightly different shape.","After roughly distinguishing them, I estimated that there had been four or five.","Even one would have been overwhelming, yet an entire group had invaded.","This was not something I could overlook. I absolutely had to make an example of them.","’But how?’","I didn’t even know exactly where the gorillas lived, let alone when they would return.","They could raid the place every time my animal companions and I were away.","It seemed my only choice was to set a trap and wait. Entering their territory would be far too dangerous.","’I never expected them to strike first like this.’","I had imagined myself trespassing into other animals’ territories, but I had never dreamed that other animals would raid my home.","As I had said earlier, I should have realized it when that raccoon blatantly stole my fasting pills.","The animals in this forest seemed to be evolving in ways far beyond anything I could predict.","└ Praise the Sun: What are you going to do when you catch the thieves? Just kill them?","└ Wild Grylls: If they do it again, I won’t have any choice but to kill them. This is where I live.","└ Praise the Sun: You’ve gotten ruthless. Didn’t you agonize over Namu-Ppareumbo for ages?","└ Wild Grylls: It wasn’t that I spared him. I couldn’t kill him;;","└ Praise the Sun: Oh, right. I’d forgotten about that.","└ Looks like Ppareumbo is seriously pissed this time.","└ Whoever did it is definitely dead, hahaha.","└ Gorilla vs. Namu-Ppareumbo. My heart is already swelling with anticipation.","└ Passing Dwarf: What happened? Something got stolen?","└ Wild Grylls: My fasting pills. Ppareumbo eats them, but they’re also my emergency rations.","└ Passing Dwarf: Oh, really? You should install a door from now on, lol.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m seriously considering it.","└ Passing Dwarf: Actually, forget it. Even if you install a door, they’ll just smash it apart.","└ Wild Grylls: You have a point. Ha. Damn it.","└ Destined to be robbed;;","└ Guess you have no choice but to keep it wide open, lol.","└ Grylls’s home gives everything away for free.","└ Wild Grylls: Shut up, you bastards.","└ Grylls, criminals always return to the scene of the crime.","└ The comment above is right. They might come back tomorrow.","└ Wild Grylls: So in the end, I just have to wait until tomorrow. Fine, okay.","After chatting about various things on the gallery, I looked around the shelter.","Aside from the cave, the surrounding area was generally wide open.","Although I had blocked it off with barricades, small animals could still enter easily.","’And like the dwarf said, they’d just destroy any door I built.’","An iron fence could keep out small animals, but even a door wouldn’t stop larger ones.","There were so many extreme creatures here that I couldn’t think of a suitable solution.","My best option was to claim the surrounding area as my territory and make sure nothing dared to enter without permission.","’Should I comfort Ppareumbo first?’","Namu-Ppareumbo was still staring blankly into space. He seemed more devastated than angry now.","I started to place a hand on his shoulder, then stopped.","Come to think of it, this bastard still hadn’t washed himself.","I quietly lowered my hand and offered him some words of comfort instead.","\"I’m angry too, Ppareumbo.\"","\"....\"","\"We still have something to eat today, so don’t worry too much. But I can’t promise that we’ll recover the stolen fasting pills.\"","I could obtain another supply through the Heavenly Demon.","However, it would be best to consider the stolen pills gone for good.","As Allfather had said, gorillas were herbivores. They might have already eaten all of them.","\"For now, just be patient. Those bastards might come back tomorrow. We can teach them a lesson then, okay?\"","\"Try to lighten up a little. Wonmo is scared of you.\"","Only then did Namu-Ppareumbo turn his head to the side, toward Wonmo.","Wonmo flinched when their eyes met, but soon began rubbing his cheek against him.","\"Kyuu. Kyuuu.\"","\"....\"","Had adorable Wonmo’s nuzzling softened his heart?","Namu-Ppareumbo slowly raised his hand and placed it atop Wonmo’s head.","It seemed that he also regarded Wonmo as either a pet or a member of the family.","I smiled warmly at the sight, but only briefly before considering how to handle the situation going forward.","’A trap... would be pointless. I wonder if there’s anything like CCTV?’","There was even an orichalcum vein nearby, so I wondered whether a similar type of magic existed.","If relay magic existed, there was no way they didn’t have something like CCTV.","If I couldn’t prevent my home from being robbed, I at least wanted to identify the culprits.","’Or I could scare them away with an alarm.’","It was a fairly decent idea. Wouldn’t Cheonggu Princess know something about that?","Just as I was about to log into the gallery with that thought—","Rustle—","\"....\"","I clearly heard something brushing against the grass outside.","The moment I heard it, I stopped trying to access the gallery.","Wonmo, who had been acting affectionate, seemed to sense something too. His eyes widened, and he froze in place.","As for Namu-Ppareumbo...","Swoosh—","He turned his head toward the cave entrance.","I did the same.","Silently and stealthily, I reached into my subspace bag.","What I pulled out was my crossbow. I always carried it with me, just in case.","Picking it up from the ground would have made at least some noise, but taking it from the subspace bag was completely silent.","Drawing the string wasn’t difficult either. I had grown stronger than before, so this much was a piece of cake.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Primate cries came from outside the cave.","I couldn’t tell whether they came from small monkeys or gorillas.","I would have to see them with my own eyes to find out.","Suppressing every trace of my presence, I crept forward.","And perhaps the anonymous commenter had been right when they said criminals always returned to the scene of the crime.","\"Ooh! Ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh.\"","Two monkeys—no, two gorillas—were talking to each other outside.","One of them beat its chest and gestured in apparent frustration, while the other made gestures as though trying to restrain it.","As expected of creatures that understood the concept of theft, they seemed more intelligent than ordinary gorillas.","Even so, to Namu-Ppareumbo and me, they were nothing more than thieves.","Bastards who stole food in the wild deserved to die.","They had stolen it knowing that could happen in the first place, hadn’t they?","Swoosh—","I slowly raised my crossbow and aimed it at the gorillas.","They were still chattering among themselves, apparently unaware that we had returned.","I wanted to pull the trigger immediately, but I suppressed the urge with superhuman patience.","My chances of hitting them would increase if they came a little closer. It was still too soon.","Splash!","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Had the fasting pills not been enough?","One of the gorillas pulled out the fish stored inside the metal barrel.","The fish was so enormous that even the gorilla had to wrap both arms around it.","The sight made me feel as though my rage meter had risen another notch.","The otters had all died after attempting to steal my fish.","That gorilla would meet the same fate.","Slowly—","As I silently took aim, Namu-Ppareumbo positioned himself beside me.","He wasn’t trying to charge forward. He stood right by my side.","He almost resembled a spotter assisting a sniper.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh.\"","Before long, the jubilant gorillas turned around and began to leave.","I aimed at the one that had greedily taken my fish.","Then, I stopped breathing altogether. Just as my sights settled perfectly on the target—","Shoot.","Perhaps it was my imagination, but a voice that seemed to belong to Namu-Ppareumbo echoed inside my head.","The instant I heard it, I pulled the trigger without hesitation.","Twang!","The moment the string was released, the bolt tore through the air.","Its tip flew directly toward the gorilla’s broad back.","Thud!","\"Gwooooooh!\"","\"Uooh?!\"","Flap-flap—","The bolt buried itself squarely in the gorilla’s back.","The gorilla immediately screamed in pain and let out a tremendous roar.","At the same time, the fish it had been carrying flew into the air and thrashed violently.","Creak—","I didn’t stop there. I immediately took out another bolt and loaded the crossbow.","Then I aimed at the gorilla once again. The other one had already fled into the undergrowth.","The gorilla struck by the bolt was also desperately trying to escape.","It apparently had no presence of mind to retrieve the fish that had fallen to the ground.","A human would have collapsed after taking a shot like that, but a beast was still a beast.","Yet even beasts could be deprived of their mobility.","Thud!","\"Uoooooh!\"","By targeting their legs.","The bolt lodged squarely in the gorilla’s calf.","I had fired immediately after loading, so I had been rather lucky.","Or perhaps my skill had improved. Either way, the situation was favorable.","The moment the gorilla collapsed, I took up my sword and shield and stepped outside.","Namu-Ppareumbo climbed onto my back as well, ready to join the fight at any moment.","\"Uooh....\"","The gorilla reached toward the bushes, desperately trying to escape.","But its companion had already abandoned it. There was no one left to help it.","I approached the gorilla as it clawed frantically along the ground.","The gorilla seemed to notice the shadow looming over it and slowly turned to look at me.","\"U... uoooh....\"","It stared at me with a terror-stricken expression.","Then it noticed Namu-Ppareumbo clinging to my back, and its eyes widened in shock.","Its reaction seemed to say, What are you doing here? It looked unable to believe the situation before it.","Whatever the circumstances were, the gorilla clearly knew Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Uh... ugh....\"","The gorilla pointed at Namu-Ppareumbo, then fainted.","Foam gathered around its mouth, as though it had been unable to withstand the physical and psychological shock.","The only difference was that it couldn’t speak. Its reactions otherwise seemed remarkably human.","Had its intelligence truly increased?","More importantly, however, its reaction puzzled me.","\"Ppareumbo.\"","’Judging by its behavior, it seems pretty similar to you.’","The fact that it had extorted food from me only made that possibility strangely more convincing.","\"What did you do to these guys?\"","Had he been the local bully around here?","I had no idea."]},{"title":"Chapter 106","paragraphs":["Hostage (2)","Two gorillas had broken into Grylls’s home again.","One of them had been subdued after Grylls shot it with a crossbow, but the other fled for its life.","It forced its way through dense bushes and thick trees, climbing trunks and leaping from branch to branch.","Its speed was remarkably agile for such a heavily built gorilla. That showed just how desperate it was.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","Before long, the fleeing gorilla reached the place where its troop lived.","The gorillas were currently enjoying an unexpected fasting-pill feast.","However, when their companion approached with such an urgent expression, they had no choice but to put the feast on hold.","\"Ooh?\"","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","Sensing that something serious had happened, the leader stepped forward.","The fleeing gorilla then explained everything that had happened.","After hearing the full story, the leader adopted a grave expression and issued an order.","\"Ooh-ooh. Ooh!\"","\"Ooh!\"","First, they would send out scouts and observe the situation. They had been the ones to trespass into another’s territory.","If the owner of that territory had killed their fellow gorilla, they could retaliate afterward.","When the leader conveyed something along those lines, the other gorillas nodded.","\"Ooh-hoo.\"","\"Hoo....\"","The leader handed the gorilla a fasting pill to calm it down.","It seemed a fight would break out before long.","That was the feeling they had.","***","After completely subduing the gorilla, what I did next was kill it...","No, I tied it up.","I wanted to cut off its head and put it on display, but that didn’t suit my nature.","More importantly, since these creatures possessed considerable intelligence, there were many factors I needed to consider.","’If they have any sense of camaraderie, they’ll definitely come back. It would be better to keep this one alive for then.’","Seeing their companion dead might only enrage them further.","One gorilla would be manageable, but if several of them attacked at once, it would be a difficult fight.","Even with Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo here, I had no idea how powerful the gorilla troop was.","What I needed was information.","It would be best to use the gorilla I had captured as a hostage and extract information from them.","’Let’s see. Tie its arms behind its back, then tie its legs... It must be incredibly strong, so I need to bind it tightly.’","Gorillas possessed tremendous strength even among primates.","And this was the Forest of Four Seasons.","It was a place where even ordinary-sized animals were terrifying.","Therefore, I thoroughly bound the unconscious gorilla with rope.","I tied it so securely that it would never be able to escape through brute strength alone.","What did I do about the bolts lodged in its body?","I administered some rough first aid.","The bolts had gone in so cleanly that I simply snapped off both ends.","An elixir?","I didn’t have any elixirs to waste on thieves.","I merely purchased the cheapest potion available at the auction house and wrapped the wounds in bandages.","└ Heavenly Demon: You have bound it securely. Since ancient times, those who stole food have been punished with flogging.","└ Wild Grylls: Food is directly tied to my survival, so I’m thinking of giving it an even harsher punishment.","└ Heavenly Demon: Cutting off its hands so that it can never steal again would not be a bad idea.","└ Wild Grylls: Whoa;; I’ll just stick with flogging.","└ SwordMaster: Just cut off its hands. As far as I know, repeat offenders have their hands cut off in my country too.","└ Wild Grylls: ;:;","Title: Captured the Thief Alive","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a gorilla tightly bound with rope)","Some anonymous commenter said that criminals always return to the scene of the crime.","Apparently, the fasting pills weren’t enough for these gorilla bastards, because they tried to steal my fish too.","There were two of them. I subdued one with my crossbow, but the other escaped.","For now, I’m planning to use this bastard as a hostage to obtain information.","It was the kind of extreme punishment that suited the era.","It seemed barbaric, yet also strangely reasonable.","└ Allfather: You have certainly bound it tightly. Judging from its appearance, it is definitely a gorilla.","└ Wild Grylls: Right? I thought these creatures were herbivores, but they tried to steal my fish too.","└ Allfather: It appears their diet has changed. Be careful. Its companions will certainly come.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve already taken that into account. I’m waiting for them.","└ Suspiciously: Is that one male or female?","└ Why are you asking?","└ Suspiciously: I heard gorillas live in matriarchal societies.","└ Aren’t you thinking of orangutans?","└ I heard male orangutans travel alone too.","└ What kind of beastkin doesn’t even know that? Lol.","└ Suspiciously: There are things even beastkin don’t know, damn it.","Lunatics were bound to appear on the gallery sooner or later.","I chuckled but didn’t respond. I simply let them entertain themselves.","If they crossed the line, the moderators would deal with them. There was no need for me to interfere.","’More importantly, when is this guy going to wake up?’","I stared at the still-unconscious gorilla.","It had foamed at the mouth and fainted the moment it saw Namu-Ppareumbo.","That made me curious about Namu-Ppareumbo’s past, but it wasn’t something I needed to worry about right now.","The important thing was obtaining information. It seemed best to leave the gorilla alone for the time being.","’It would be so convenient if I could talk to animals.’","The ability to communicate with animals.","In other words, the power of a druid.","Since this was a fantasy world, I had searched for such an ability, but apparently none existed.","There were occasionally people who claimed they could understand animals, but most of them were lying.","’Even humans speak different languages. How much worse must it be for animals?’","While entertaining those pointless thoughts, I carefully examined the gorilla.","It was much larger than me.","Aside from that, however, it seemed completely ordinary. I couldn’t find anything unusual about it.","\"Sniff, sniff.\"","\"Wonmo, that’s not food.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","I warned Wonmo in case he tried to eat the unconscious gorilla.","My job was to wait until this creature’s companions arrived.","If they didn’t come...","There was nothing else I could do. I would have to kill it.","Disposing of the body wouldn’t be a problem either. I could bury it or throw it into the river.","’Should I dig the hole in advance, just in case?’","I was thinking about that as I casually picked up a shovel.","\"Ugh....\"","The unconscious gorilla gradually began to regain its senses.","Seeing it wake up, I quietly put down the shovel.","\"Hey. You awake?\"","\"Uuugh...?\"","The gorilla stared at me in confusion, apparently still dazed.","It didn’t seem to recognize my face yet.","\"Ooh... ooh? Ooh?!\"","Then the gorilla suddenly began thrashing violently.","Judging by its bewildered expression, it had realized that its body was completely bound.","It was a good thing I had used several lengths of rope. Otherwise, it probably would have broken free in no time.","\"Awooh....\"","Of course, struggling wouldn’t make the wounds from the crossbow bolts disappear.","Unable to endure the pain, the thrashing gorilla soon became still.","Now that it had calmed down, it was time for us to have a conversation of sorts.","\"Hey. Look at me.\"","At my words, the gorilla slowly raised its head.","Its face had been twisted in pain moments ago, but now it looked stern and unyielding.","It seemed determined not to answer me, regardless of what I did.","It really was like a person.","’You couldn’t understand me anyway.’","There was no particular reason I had called out to it.","I merely wanted to observe its reaction.","I had intended to decide how to treat it based on that reaction, but it appeared to be remarkably stubborn.","’Then how will it react when it sees Namu-Ppareumbo?’","I brought over Namu-Ppareumbo, who had been standing silently and staring into the forest.","Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t resist at all, even as I carried him over.","I then placed him in front of the gorilla’s face where it could see him.","\"Do you know this—\"","\"Ookyaaaaak!\"","The instant it saw Namu-Ppareumbo, the gorilla reacted as though it were having a seizure.","Its violent force could be felt even though it was bound with rope. That was how terrified it was.","I stared blankly at the rampaging gorilla before turning toward Namu-Ppareumbo.","Namu-Ppareumbo looked at the thrashing gorilla and slowly raised his hand.","Just as I was about to stop him, thinking he might kill it—","Smack!","Ppareumbo delivered a resounding slap across its face.","The gorilla immediately became docile. Its dejected expression was an added bonus.","No. Rather than dejected, it seemed to have lost the will to live.","’What the hell has this bastard been doing?’","I knew what Namu-Ppareumbo was capable of. He possessed speed that the eye couldn’t follow and razor-sharp claws.","I couldn’t tell whether he was infamous among all the gorillas or if only this particular one feared him.","Either way, he had made it behave, so it was fine.","I rummaged through my bag and took out a fasting pill.","It was one of the pills I had brought as emergency food and as a gesture of goodwill.","I intended to show it to the gorilla.","\"Hey. Look at this.\"","\"...?\"","\"You know what this is, right?\"","The moment I showed it the fasting pill, the gorilla’s eyes trembled violently.","It clearly recognized the pill, which was practically a confession that they were the culprits.","There was nothing more to verify. I snorted and slowly conveyed my meaning.","\"Fasting pill.\"","First, the fasting pill.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","Next, Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Staple food. Okay?\"","Finally, I mimed eating it, and the gorilla’s face seemingly turned pale.","You might ask how I could tell when its entire body was covered in black skin and fur.","Would you believe me if I said that was simply how it felt?","Anyway, let’s just leave it at that.","’In the end, I’ll have to wait for this guy’s companions to arrive.’","I asked Namu-Ppareumbo to watch the gorilla.","Since I didn’t know when the troop would appear, I planned to inspect my weapons.","First was the crossbow that had proven so useful. I drew the string so it would be ready to fire at any moment.","Rustle, rustle—","\"Kyuu?\"","\"....\"","Speak of the tiger and it appears.","No, in this case, was it speak of the gorilla?","Holding the loaded crossbow, I turned toward the source of the noise.","Rustle!","Apparently having no intention of concealing themselves, gorillas began emerging from the bushes.","There weren’t just one or two, but exactly five.","An exceptionally large gorilla stood in the center.","Since it stood ahead of the others, it appeared to be their leader. More importantly, there was also a difference in their equipment.","’Just as Allfather said.’","The leader was barehanded, but each of the other gorillas held something.","One of them was even holding a stone axe. I couldn’t describe how shocked I was when I saw it.","The fact that they had made a stone axe meant that they understood the concept of crafting.","They seemed more intelligent than I had expected.","I needed to remain vigilant.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ugh...!\"","Upon seeing that its companions had arrived, the hostage gorilla cried out frantically.","But as I had mentioned, it had been shot with crossbow bolts. The movement made it grimace in pain.","The presumed leader glanced at the hostage before focusing its gaze on me.","I raised my sword and shield, prepared to fight if necessary.","\"Ooh! Ooh!\"","\"Uooh! Uooh!\"","Then the gorillas beside their leader began making a commotion.","Rather than a commotion, it was more like they had seen something horrifying.","\"....\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo.","At some point, Ppareumbo had approached my side.","Most of the gorillas began trembling in fear when they saw him.","The leader managed to remain calm, but its expression had stiffened considerably.","That meant Namu-Ppareumbo’s infamy among the gorillas was truly terrifying.","Thanks to that, the negotiation might be a little easier.","I immediately began communicating with them.","First, I showed them one of the fasting pills they had taken.","I was asking whether they had stolen something containing these.","The leader seemed to understand my intention and nodded.","\"Ooh.\"","The leader issued an order with a short grunt.","At its command, one of the gorillas brought over an object.","The leader took it and threw it toward me.","Flop—","However, apparently containing nothing, the object lost momentum and fell midway.","It was a pouch.","The pouch that had contained the fasting pills.","But there were no fasting pills left inside.","’They already ate all of them.’","I had suspected as much, but they had eaten everything in such a short time.","All I could do was sigh.","Would those bastards apologize?","Or would they shamelessly refuse to take responsibility?","Considering Namu-Ppareumbo’s infamy, they would probably apologize, but who knew?","First, it seemed best to observe Namu-Ppareumbo’s reaction.","\"What do you want to do?\"","\"....\"","Namu-Ppareumbo had been staring blankly at the empty pouch. At my question, he slowly began walking.","The gorilla troop made no move in response. They merely watched him with tense expressions.","Before long, Namu-Ppareumbo approached the fully restrained gorilla.","For a moment, I wondered whether he had partially given up and intended to release it.","Slash!","I was wrong.","Namu-Ppareumbo’s actions exceeded my imagination.","With his sharp claws, he sliced straight through the gorilla’s neck.","These were the same claws that had cut through a metal barrel—the claws I had personally maintained for him.","They could effortlessly sever the fragile flesh and bones of an animal.","Spurt!","Ignoring the blood gushing from the severed neck, Namu-Ppareumbo did what he intended to do.","He drove his claws into the gorilla’s head as it rolled across the ground like a ball.","It looked as though he had stabbed it with a fork.","Then, holding it that way, he slowly raised his arm and hurled the head toward the gorillas.","Thud! Bounce! Roll—","The severed gorilla head landed in front of the leader.","He hadn’t thrown it at me, but had tossed it upward instead.","What exactly was he trying to do?","Just in case, I placed my left foot forward so I could defend myself at any moment.","Whoosh—","As the gorilla’s head descended, the leader pulled back its right arm.","The moment the head reached eye level, the leader thrust its drawn-back fist forward.","Booooom!","A deafening impact erupted.","Whoooooosh!","The gorilla’s head flew toward us like a cannonball."]},{"title":"Chapter 107","paragraphs":["The Way of the Wild (1)","The wild is harsh.","And savage.","It would be foolish to demand \"reason\" from animals living in the wild.","It was a world governed by the law of the jungle, where the strong took everything from the weak.","At the same time, it was a world where those who survived were the strong.","Even if I wanted to treat them rationally, animals were not rational creatures.","Their instincts took precedence over reason, and that wouldn’t change even if their intelligence increased.","Those who invaded your territory were enemies.","Those who stole your food were enemies.","Those who went beyond stealing it and actually ate it were enemies too.","Either you killed your enemies, or they killed you.","That was the way of the wild and the law of nature.","Whoosh!","The gorilla’s head had been punched away by the leader.","It flew toward Namu-Ppareumbo like a cannonball, but who was Namu-Ppareumbo?","He could effortlessly dodge an arrow fired from point-blank range.","Avoiding a mere head propelled by a punch was nothing to him.","’But that thing was launched with a punch?’","Even so, I was astonished.","The punch I had just witnessed from the gorilla leader wasn’t merely powerful. What made it even more astonishing was the perfect control behind that strength.","If the leader had simply forced it forward with brute strength, the gorilla’s head would have exploded.","Yet through some unknown principle, it had been launched like a cannonball without bursting apart.","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","Namu-Ppareumbo’s provocation had been answered by the leader’s attack.","When the leader began beating its chest, the other gorillas followed suit.","A gorilla beating its chest was unmistakably a threat.","In other words, this was a declaration of war.","\"Ha....\"","\"Grrrr...!\"","Unlike me, who let out a sigh, Namu-Ppareumbo wore his usual relaxed expression.","Wonmo seemed to sense the atmosphere too. His fur stood on end as he became alert.","’They were the ones in the wrong, though.’","The gorillas had poured the fuel, and Namu-Ppareumbo had thrown a match onto it.","The problem was that it was my house now going up in flames.","What a rotten situation.","Unless we dealt with those gorillas, there would be no extinguishing the fire consuming my home.","I steeled myself and prepared for an attack that could come at any moment.","’They’ll be incomparably stronger than those otters.’","These weren’t just any animals. They were gorillas, the primates with the greatest physical strength.","Moreover, as the clubs in their hands demonstrated, they could even use tools.","This would undoubtedly be a difficult fight.","Above all, the gorilla leader bothered me.","’What is that thing that it doesn’t need to carry anything?’","It had no weapon, yet somehow seemed even stronger.","It was a strange intuition.","While I narrowed my eyes and glared at the leader, the other gorillas began charging.","As expected of gorillas, they rushed forward with their long arms planted against the ground.","The leader, however, merely stood behind them and watched. It made no move to join the battle itself.","\"Ppareumbo, get on Wonmo’s back.\"","\"....\"","\"Wonmo, don’t start running yet. Stay close behind me.\"","After giving Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo their instructions, I slowly retreated.","My chances of victory would be low if I charged at the gorillas like this.","I had been able to defeat the otters because they were small and their tactics were simple.","But look at these bastards.","They weren’t merely charging blindly.","’They’re surrounding us.’","Instead of running straight at us, they scattered in every direction.","They spread out to the front, rear, and both sides, forming an encirclement.","They executed the maneuver the moment the battle began, suggesting they had done it many times before.","’As expected, these bastards know how to use their heads.’","Intelligence was the reason humanity had risen to the top of the food chain.","Even if their intellect fell far short of a human’s, that didn’t make them any less threatening.","\"Kwaaaaah!\"","Once the encirclement was complete, the gorilla whose gaze met mine swung down its weapon.","Of the three wielding a bone, a stone axe, and a wooden club, it was the one holding the stone axe.","I urgently raised my shield to defend myself.","Just in case, I even reinforced it with mana.","Claaaaang!","The stone axe collided with my shield, producing a deafening crash.","As expected of gorillas, reputed to be the strongest primates, the impact felt tremendously heavy.","If this had been before I ate the eel, every one of their attacks would have been lethal.","But I had no time to worry about the noise.","The gorilla wielding the wooden club was already approaching.","Without even thinking of counterattacking, I hurriedly pulled back my shield.","Whoosh!","The club narrowly swept past my face.","At the same time, the stone-axe-wielding gorilla roared and charged at me.","Its vicious teeth were slightly frightening, but I forced the fear aside.","Clang!","The stone axe struck my shield again.","However, counterattacking was difficult.","Just as before, the club-wielding gorilla immediately launched another attack.","Their attacks were wild and indiscriminate, yet that very recklessness allowed them to cover one another’s openings.","’At this rate, I’ll be at a disadvantage.’","I didn’t even have the freedom to check on Wonmo and Namu-Ppareumbo.","I was somehow managing to block and evade their attacks with the skills I had honed until now, but I was hopelessly outnumbered.","Unless I attacked, I would never escape the gorillas’ endless assault.","’Their attacks themselves are simple.’","After exchanging several rounds of attacks and defenses, I began to understand their pattern.","No, perhaps calling it a pattern was giving them too much credit.","Their attacks were closer to wild swings.","However, they were using \"tools.\"","They were trying to strike me with those tools.","I was looking for the inevitable openings created whenever someone grew careless while trying to use a weapon.","How ironic.","They had picked up weapons to become stronger, yet those weapons were instead creating openings.","Whoosh!","The stone axe narrowly passed in front of me.","I had watched the timing of its downward swing and stepped back.","’Now the other one will swing its club.’","I glanced to the side.","Just as I had expected, the gorilla was preparing to swing its club.","It wasn’t bringing the weapon straight down from above. It was swinging diagonally.","Having roughly predicted the direction of the attack, I raised my shield.","And the sword in my right hand—","Stab!","I thrust my sword toward the collarbone of the stone-axe-wielding gorilla.","Since it was the Heavenly Demon’s sword and was even enveloped in aura, the blade penetrated easily.","Moreover, given the gorilla’s posture, stabbing it in the shoulder was extremely easy.","\"Kuaaaaaah!\"","Booom!","Clutching the wounded area, the gorilla stumbled backward.","Meanwhile, my shield blocked the wooden club.","Now was my chance.","While one gorilla was reeling, I decided to eliminate the other one first.","’If it’s only one...’","The remaining gorilla continued attacking despite what had happened to its companion.","That was the mistake that would cost it the fight.","Its physical strength might have been immense, but it was slow.","Furthermore, this one’s weapon wasn’t a stone axe. It was merely a wooden club.","Crack!","No matter how sturdy the wood was, it would still break after colliding with an iron shield.","The instant I heard the club snap, I swung my sword diagonally.","Slash!","Rather than trying to cleave through the gorilla’s entire body, I focused on cutting only as deeply as necessary.","That was something SwordMaster had taught me.","Trying to cleave completely through a body inevitably required putting more strength into the attack.","Doing so significantly reduced stability.","A sword depended more on stability than strength.","SwordMaster had even advised me to use an axe instead if I wanted to rely on greater force.","’He also said that striking something too hard could damage my shoulder.’","Following his advice, I had slightly changed the way I fought.","Even when a perfect opportunity presented itself, I wouldn’t put excessive strength into my attack.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was so exceptional that I didn’t have to worry about its cutting power for the time being.","\"Krraaaaaah!\"","A diagonal wound appeared across the gorilla’s upper body, sending it crashing backward.","Blood didn’t spray immediately, but the wound was clearly deep.","\"Kuaaaaah! Kua! Kuaaaaah!\"","The gorilla thrashed and rolled across the ground.","Blood began gushing from the wound carved by my sword.","It wasn’t only blood. Its organs began spilling from its split abdomen.","Even though I had swung lightly, the power of the attack seemed to have torn open more than half its abdomen.","That took care of one.","The other was still clutching its shoulder.","When our eyes met, it looked at me in terror.","Perhaps the greater one’s intelligence became, the harder it was to escape the fear of death.","Stab!","\"Kuh... kua....\"","I immediately finished it by stabbing it through the heart.","Cutting its throat didn’t suit my nature, and more importantly, it would make cleaning up afterward troublesome.","Having killed both gorillas, I turned around to check on Wonmo and Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Kyuu... kyuu....\"","\"Wonmo?\"","As expected, the two gorillas they had faced had become cold corpses.","However, Wonmo was whimpering as though he had been injured.","I glanced at the gorilla leader before approaching Wonmo.","\"Kyuuu....\"","\"You broke a claw.\"","One of Wonmo’s claws had broken.","Fortunately, it wasn’t a serious injury.","It didn’t look as though a gorilla had struck him. He seemed to have made a mistake on his own.","I stroked Wonmo’s head and spoke to Namu-Ppareumbo, who was riding on his back.","\"Go to the cave and give Wonmo some elixir. You can do that, right?\"","\"....\"","Namu-Ppareumbo nodded.","He then patted Wonmo’s side a couple of times.","Wonmo glanced at me once before lumbering back into the cave.","’Now, all that remains is...’","The gorilla leader.","I turned and faced it.","The creature had continued observing from behind even as all its companions were killed.","Was it confident?","Or did it have some other reason?","’The fact that it isn’t carrying a weapon bothers me most.’","Unlike the other gorillas, which had wielded weapons, it stood completely barehanded.","What did it possess that allowed it to fight without a weapon?","I couldn’t help wondering.","But that didn’t change the fact that it was my enemy.","I spoke to the gorilla leader.","\"Do you still want to continue?\"","The gorilla leader didn’t answer.","Instead, it responded by slowly rising upright.","As it straightened its back, it lifted both hands from the ground.","Its two legs were short compared to its arms, like a sloth’s, but they were as thick as logs.","’So it intends to fight...’","Just as I thought that, the gorilla slowly began moving.","It placed its left foot forward and drew its right foot back.","It extended its left hand with its palm facing forward and positioned its right hand beside its waist.","Finally...","It slightly twisted its body.","When all those movements came together, they formed a complete stance.","’What the fuck am I looking at?’","No matter how I looked at it, that was a stance for performing martial arts.","And a gorilla was displaying it?","A martial art that could never be learned without a master’s instruction?","I wanted to deny everything I was seeing.","Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, this was...","This was going too far.","\"...Who taught you?\"","\"Who the hell taught you...?!\"","My voice was unconsciously beginning to rise when the gorilla leader leaned its upper body forward, as though it didn’t consider my question worth answering.","It was an obvious signal that it was about to charge.","I suppressed my agitation and assumed my stance.","Swoosh!","Its movements differed from those of the other gorillas.","The others had simply charged at me.","The leader, however, approached me as though it were gliding across the ground.","Whooom!","That wasn’t all.","The moment it arrived in front of me, the gorilla leader attacked.","Its enormous palm flew directly toward my face.","If that attack landed properly, my head would burst like a watermelon.","Bang!","I barely turned my head in time to evade the palm strike.","But I hadn’t avoided it completely.","The palm narrowly grazed my cheek.","I felt a stinging pain, as though my skin had been torn.","’Th-this is...’","As though time itself had slowed, I found myself staring directly at the gorilla leader.","Its eyes were perfectly calm, yet a faint anger smoldered within them.","Despite that anger, it maintained complete composure.","Seeing those eyes reminded me of the palmprints I had discovered during today’s exploration.","One palmprint that I had assumed belonged to a gorilla.","And beside it, another that appeared to belong to a human.","’Just who...?!’","There was only one possible explanation.","’Just who the hell taught it...?!’","Someone had taught this gorilla martial arts."]},{"title":"Chapter 108","paragraphs":["The Way of the Wild (3)","Martial arts had contributed greatly to human history.","From ancient times to the modern era, more than half of humanity’s history had been defined by war.","And martial arts had played a significant role in those wars.","Particularly in ancient times, the course of a war could often change depending on an individual’s skill.","As technology advanced, the greatest cheat item in history—the gun—eventually appeared. Even so, the importance of martial arts never diminished.","That was because martial arts weren’t limited to any particular tool.","They were techniques for wielding martial force more effectively.","That was the essence of martial arts, and even the accuracy and stability of a gun varied drastically depending on the person using it.","Furthermore, martial arts were difficult to master without someone teaching you directly. Learning them alone might technically be possible, but it was close to impossible.","The length of a person’s limbs, height, weight, and many other attributes were different. Even talent varied tremendously between individuals.","Someone needed to watch the learner in real time and correct them accordingly.","’Just who...?!’","I couldn’t hide my astonishment as I faced the gorilla leader that had launched the palm strike.","It had approached as though gliding across the ground, followed by an attack that flowed as naturally as water.","Every individual movement was astonishing.","But I had no time to think.","What mattered was that this gorilla leader was my enemy.","I had to defeat it at all costs.","Swoosh!","The moment I evaded the palm strike, I counterattacked.","Because it felt as though time were moving slowly, my counterattack was equally swift.","My sword descended from above.","At this rate, the blade would bury itself in the gorilla leader’s collarbone.","Yet the gorilla leader’s expression remained perfectly calm.","Instead of retreating, it moved even closer to me.","Grab!","Then it seized my arm with both hands.","Not only that, but it also turned its back toward me.","Just as before, every movement flowed seamlessly into the next.","And as that sequence of movements continued, something happened to my body.","Whoosh!","Without my consent, both my legs left the ground.","Booom!","The world spun once, and a tremendous impact struck my back.","My breath was violently knocked from my lungs, and my eyes widened in pain.","What the hell had it just done to me?","’Was that a shoulder throw...?!’","I had only a moment to be shocked that the gorilla leader could even use grappling techniques.","The sole of its foot appeared directly above my head.","If that stomp landed, I would die.","Booooom!","I narrowly avoided it by rolling aside.","Hurriedly steadying my breathing, I rose to my feet.","During the brief time it took me to stand, the gorilla leader approached.","It had no intention of giving me even a moment to recover.","One mistake and I would genuinely die.","I rapidly accelerated the mana flowing through my body.","If even one of its attacks struck me properly, it would undoubtedly inflict catastrophic damage.","Claaaang!","Another palm strike flew toward me.","I blocked it with my shield.","It was powerful, but not powerful enough to break through my shield.","If I could exploit an opening, this fight was manageable.","If my opponent had been an ordinary human, I could have created some distance, but...","’Its arms are so long that the difference in reach is meaningless.’","Since it was a gorilla, the length of its arms rendered distance management far less effective.","That meant I had to engage it in a battle of tactics on equal ground.","This was completely different from my previous fights.","Unlike the battles I had survived through improvisation, this was a contest of pure skill.","In other words, it might turn into the kind of prolonged battle of endurance I hated so much.","Booom!","Once again, the gorilla leader’s hand collided with my shield.","This time, it used a fist rather than its palm.","The impact transmitted through the shield made my shoulder tingle.","Its physical strength was on an entirely different level from the other gorillas.","Grimacing, I swung the sword in my right hand diagonally.","I didn’t forget to be careful so it couldn’t throw me over its shoulder again.","However, it evaded my attack with a simple backstep.","Its control of distance was exceptional too.","Who the hell had taught this creature martial arts?","Whoever it was, they had taught it something truly obnoxious.","’A weakness. I need to find a weakness.’","Its short legs?","Its much longer arms compensated for them.","Counterattack by exploiting its sluggish movements?","If it threw me again, I would die.","The difference between bare hands and a weapon?","That bastard’s entire body was a weapon.","No matter how hard I tried, I couldn’t find a weakness.","As I had said, this was a contest of pure skill.","’No. I do have an advantage.’","After thinking carefully, I realized I wasn’t entirely without an advantage.","That creature couldn’t defend against my attacks.","Its only option was to evade them.","The instant it tried to block, the Heavenly Demon’s sword would cut through it.","I decided to exploit that fact.","I would create a situation where it had no choice but to defend.","Then an opportunity would inevitably appear.","Swoosh!","I thrust into an opening, aiming for its shoulder.","However, the gorilla leader not only evaded effortlessly but also responded by lightly tapping the flat of my sword.","The tap diverted my blade to the side and slightly disrupted my balance.","In other words, it was now the gorilla leader’s turn.","Realizing that, it extended its palm toward me.","That was precisely what I had been waiting for.","I charged directly at the gorilla.","\"?!\"","The gorilla leader’s eyes widened, apparently not expecting me to charge.","But it was already too late to retract its outstretched arm.","Even if it somehow managed to pull it back, its posture would become awkward.","While the gorilla leader was caught off guard, I thrust my shield forward as though throwing a punch instead of swinging my sword.","My target was its face.","Startled, the gorilla leader hurriedly raised an arm to protect itself, but—","Cr-r-rack!","Its arm wasn’t enough to stop my mana-enhanced body or the shield surging with aura.","The unmistakable sound of breaking bones entered my ears.","The moment I heard it, I became certain of my victory.","Cr-runch!","\"Keugh?!\"","But perhaps that was the price of letting my guard down.","I felt something burst around my ribs.","It was accompanied by an ominous noise.","Not the sound of bones merely breaking, but of them being crushed into fragments.","At first, I felt nothing.","There was only a tingling sensation, as though lightning had passed through me.","Then, in an instant, excruciating pain struck and my vision went black.","I couldn’t breathe.","\"Kuh... kuh....\"","\"Kuaaaaah!\"","The gorilla leader and I both staggered backward.","We had each delivered a devastating blow to the other.","My ribs had been struck, while its arm had been destroyed.","When it came to continuing the fight, I still had the advantage.","The arm that had blocked my shield hung limply.","Its bones had been completely shattered.","’My ribs, though...’","Of course, I wasn’t unscathed either.","For one thing, I couldn’t breathe.","It was even worse than when I had been thrown over its shoulder.","As I remained unable to draw breath, my vision gradually began to fade.","\"Uuugh... Hah! Ugh!\"","Fortunately, I finally managed to suck in a breath.","Then an overwhelming wave of pain surged through me.","It hurt several times worse than when the orichalcum guardian had struck me.","It had only been one hit.","A single blow had inflicted enough damage to nearly incapacitate me.","I was fortunate it had struck my ribs. If it had hit another vital point, I would have died instantly.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","Perhaps it had decided that it could no longer continue fighting.","Clutching its broken arm with its other hand, the gorilla leader turned and fled.","That was actually fortunate.","I wasn’t in any condition to continue fighting either.","’Elixir... I need to drink an elixir...!’","Clutching my ribs, I stumbled into the cave.","I couldn’t breathe properly.","I was worried that one of my broken ribs might have punctured a lung. Still, an elixir should heal it.","Once inside the cave, I hurriedly drank an elixir.","I emptied the entire bottle.","\"Hoo. Hoo. Hoo.\"","Cold sweat poured from my body as I struggled to steady my breathing.","Thanks to the elixir, I seemed to be doing a little better.","However, the excruciating pain remained, occasionally forcing me to grimace.","\"Haa....\"","Only after approximately five minutes did I finally manage to stabilize myself.","This situation was completely different from when the orichalcum guardian had struck me.","Injuring my ribs had made it difficult even to breathe.","\"Cough! Cough! Keugh!\"","As if that weren’t enough, blood sprayed from my mouth.","That had been dangerous.","I roughly wiped the blood from my hand and sank to the ground.","Things seemed to become more difficult with each passing day.","’Just what was that bastard...?’","A gorilla that used human martial arts.","I couldn’t understand it at all.","I wondered whether a survivor had taught it, but I wasn’t even sure that was possible.","The people on the gallery had said there had never been a case where someone taught martial arts or a breathing technique to a primate and achieved any remarkable results.","’Is the Forest of Four Seasons different?’","Perhaps it would be easier to simply accept that the gorilla had learned martial arts because it possessed enough intelligence to do so.","But I still wanted to know who had taught it.","A gorilla had learned martial arts.","Its teacher not only had to possess a high level of mastery but also needed exceptional teaching ability to pass martial arts on to a gorilla.","Most importantly, this was someone who had survived in the Forest of Four Seasons long enough to teach a gorilla martial arts.","Swoosh—","As my thoughts grew increasingly complicated, someone approached me.","It was Namu-Ppareumbo.","’What was that all about?’","I stared intently at him, then suddenly remembered what he had done.","He had decapitated the gorilla we had taken hostage and thrown its head at the others.","It had truly been the way of the wild.","It was also a side of Namu-Ppareumbo I had never seen before.","\"Hey.\"","\"....\"","\"Why did you spare me?\"","Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t answer.","However, he seemed to be saying:","Because you were so pathetic that there was no need to kill you.","’Hmm. That makes sense.’","I chuckled.","It was fortunate that I had been so weak back then.","If I had posed even the slightest threat to Namu-Ppareumbo, I probably wouldn’t be alive today.","\"Come to think of it, Ppareumbo, what are you going to eat?\"","\"....\"","Separate from everything else, I needed to consider his diet from now on.","Namu-Ppareumbo merely wore his usual relaxed expression.","Of course, it wasn’t difficult to interpret the meaning behind that expression.","\"There won’t be any fasting pills for a while. The Heavenly Demon said you’ll have to wait.\"","\"....\"","The corners of Ppareumbo’s mouth lowered slightly.","So even this guy could make an expression like that.","How fascinating.","***","The gorilla leader ran and continued running.","One of its arms had been completely destroyed, leaving it unable to climb trees.","All it could do was run.","Even so, it moved at an extraordinary speed. The surrounding scenery changed continuously with every stride it took.","Just like the technique it had used to close the distance with Grylls in an instant, even the way it ran differed from that of an ordinary animal.","Rustle!","Before long, the gorilla leader reached its main camp.","The other gorillas were going about their respective tasks.","One gorilla was gathering bananas hanging from a tree.","Another lay sprawled out, sleeping.","Others were splitting stones to make tools.","\"Awoooooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","The leader roared while clutching its limp, dangling arm.","At the sound of that roar, every gorilla stopped what it was doing.","An eerie silence instantly descended over the gorillas’ territory.","What had the leader told them?","Swoosh—","Then someone approached from behind the leader.","The leader turned around the moment it sensed the presence.","The newcomer was similar in size, but its posture was entirely different from that of the other gorillas.","Even the leader planted both hands on the ground when running.","This newly arrived gorilla, however, stood proudly upright on two legs.","More importantly, its appearance was markedly different.","The leader and the other gorillas all had their bodies exposed.","The newcomer, however, wore \"clothes\" like a human.","Although the clothing was worn, tattered, and practically reduced to rags...","It was still clothing.","It wore black garments that Grylls would have described as Eastern in style.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","The moment the leader saw that gorilla, it began explaining everything that had happened.","It even pointed at its broken, dangling arm.","The newly arrived gorilla silently listened to the leader’s account.","\"Ooh-ooh!\"","\"....\"","\"Ooh-ooh! Ooh!\"","The more it heard, the more serious its expression became.","Perhaps it was older than the other gorillas. Its face was lined with wrinkles and bore the unmistakable signs of age and experience.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"....\"","It also had a five-pronged scar slashed across one eye."]},{"title":"Chapter 109","paragraphs":["Welcome To (1)","I had been through a lot of hardships while living in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Whenever that happened, I would rest in my own way—collapsing from exhaustion and spending the entire day holed up in the cave, or occasionally practicing my breathing technique.","However, I rarely smoked.","I had decided only to smoke when both my body and mind were utterly exhausted.","And that perfectly described my current condition.","Sizzle!","I lit the tip of a cigar with a fire-starting stone.","Once smoke began curling from its tip, I placed it between my lips and took a long, refreshing drag.","The cool fragrance—without the slightest trace of harshness—filled my lungs and invigorated me.","\"Phew.\"","With the World Tree tobacco still between my lips, I exhaled. The smoke rose in wisps before gradually dispersing.","Smoking seemed to clear my head, at least a little.","Though my thoughts were still complicated.","I wanted to keep my distance from tobacco whenever possible, but that was difficult right now.","’I have to dispose of the gorilla corpses, and they might come back for revenge... Haah...’","Thanks to the elixir, my broken ribs had mostly healed.","My stamina hadn’t been depleted too severely either, so I still felt relatively energetic. My head, however, was a mess.","I had started smoking because I wanted to untangle those complicated thoughts somehow.","After all, there was simply far too much to consider regarding the gorillas.","’Who the hell taught them martial arts?’","I could overlook the gorillas using tools. Allfather had warned me about that in advance.","Besides, their obsession with using tools had actually made them easier to deal with in some respects.","But the gorilla that had used martial arts was a different matter. It had been an extremely difficult opponent.","The combination of a gorilla’s naturally powerful body and fluid techniques had made every one of its attacks dangerous.","If I hadn’t trained my reaction speed with Namu-Ppareumbo, my skull would have been smashed open.","’Considering the circumstances, the person who left that palm print on the tree must have taught them.’","With the cigar still between my lips, I organized my thoughts.","If I wanted to uncover the truth more precisely, I would need to enter their territory.","Even if I captured the leader gorilla, it wasn’t as though it could speak.","They might be incapable of speech, but they were remarkably intelligent creatures.","The fact that they had gone beyond using tools and learned martial arts was proof enough.","’Just how intelligent do they have to be to use martial arts?’","When it came to martial arts, the person being taught was just as important as the person doing the teaching.","There was a reason the word talent existed. Without talent, a person would simply remain stuck in place.","Perhaps that gorilla possessed more talent for martial arts than I did.","The thought suddenly occurred to me.","’...This forest is seriously insane.’","I couldn’t help but chuckle bitterly.","I took another deep drag of the cigar and exhaled the smoke.","For now, it seemed best to put the gorillas out of my mind and deal with the work in front of me.","\"Wonmo is... asleep.\"","Wonmo had been injured for the first time in his life. After receiving treatment, he was now sleeping soundly on the mat.","He normally slept sprawled out with all four limbs extended, but now he had curled himself into a ball.","Since intruders had entered his territory, he was probably remaining alert so that he could spring into action at any moment.","’Even our home isn’t safe anymore.’","There was no telling when the gorillas might return.","They had even raided our fasting pills. This wasn’t something I could take lightly.","Nor could I leave someone behind to guard this place. Even Namu-Ppareumbo would be in danger.","’In the end, I definitely need to install a door.’","And it would have to be an extremely sturdy one.","A door that even the gorillas couldn’t easily break down.","For that, it would have to be made of steel.","I had no choice but to ask the dwarf to make it. I would assemble it myself afterward.","’Wouldn’t a few lumps of orichalcon be enough?’","I took one final, refreshing drag before opening the wooden box.","Then I tapped the ash into the ashtray and cut off the burnt tip with my dagger.","I could still smoke it several more times. I didn’t have much tobacco left, so I needed to conserve it.","’It really is delicious, though.’","If I started running low later, I would have to ask Let’s Grow Trees for more.","I didn’t know what that person wanted in return, but I could at least hear them out.","I gathered a shovel and various other tools before heading outside.","The moment I stepped out, I was greeted by the sight of the dead gorilla troop.","The most gruesome of them all was the gorilla whose head had been severed—the one Namu-Ppareumbo had killed.","’First, I should take a few pictures to upload to the Gallery.’","I had a mountain of questions to ask, so documenting the scene was essential.","After photographing the tools the gorillas had used, I began cleaning everything up.","Considering the gorillas’ massive size, even disposing of them was inevitably difficult.","’Should I just bury them?’","The easiest method was to dig a hole, throw them inside, and bury them.","There was no need to carry every corpse all the way to the river and dump them there.","If I was attacked while heading toward the river, I would be in serious trouble.","In particular, the leader gorilla that had escaped might return with another troop to take revenge.","’Cutting them... into pieces would feel a little wrong.’","They were primates rather than ordinary beasts like the saber-toothed tiger, so I felt uncomfortable dismembering them.","Besides, some of the corpses were already badly mutilated.","It would be better to simply dig a pit.","I started by gathering all the corpses in one place. Incidentally, I had a hard time finding the severed head belonging to the decapitated corpse.","’I should dig the pit far away from here.’","I wasn’t insane enough to bury them inside my shelter.","I would bury them somewhere reasonably far away.","There was also a chance that other animals might come and dig them up, so I intended to bury them as deeply as possible.","’This should be good enough.’","It was behind the cave, in a reasonably spacious clearing.","The place could easily have been called my backyard, and I dug a deep pit there.","Moving each gorilla individually was tedious, but there was no avoiding it.","It was only after roughly an hour had passed that I finally managed to bury all the gorilla corpses.","If my strength and other physical abilities hadn’t improved, it would have taken me at least two hours.","Title: Gorilla Troop Eliminated","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a dead gorilla)","(Photo of a gorilla lying on the ground)","(Photo of a gorilla lying dead in a spray of blood)","(Photo of a gorilla cleverly positioned so its severed neck isn’t visible)","(Photo of the tools used by the gorillas)","(Photo of the gorilla corpses gathered together)","I wiped out all the gorillas that came to rescue the hostage I captured.","There was a leader gorilla, but it escaped.","Also, the leader gorilla used something resembling martial arts. Is that even possible? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: A gorilla used martial arts? What kind of martial art did it display?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s difficult to explain in detail, but I’ll start with its stance. It extended its left hand forward with the palm facing outward, while its right hand was clenched into a fist and held beside its waist.","└ Heavenly Demon: That alone is insufficient. Could you describe the martial art it demonstrated in a little more detail?","└ Wild Grylls: It used palm strikes frequently. They were incredibly fast too.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. There are far too many martial arts that employ palm strikes. We need a more distinctive feature...","└ SwordMaster: Before that, aren’t you surprised that a gorilla used martial arts? Something completely absurd just happened, you know? ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: That is true. This lady has seen countless fools inferior to monkeys, but never imagined that an actual ape could practice martial arts.","└ SwordMaster: You do know the difference between apes and monkeys, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: Is it not simply the presence or absence of a tail? They are all the same monkeys to this lady.","└ SwordMaster: Fair enough. Anyway, were you injured anywhere?","└ Wild Grylls: I was struck in the ribs and nearly died, but fortunately, I survived. The leader gorilla broke its arm too.","└ Heavenly Demon: What a remarkable occurrence. However, it could not have cultivated martial arts on its own. This lady suspects that someone taught it.","└ Wild Grylls: (Photo of the center of the tree bearing both a gorilla’s palm print and a human palm print) Looking at this, I’m certain someone taught it.","└ Heavenly Demon: That is a reasonable inference.","└ Allfather: There may still be another survivor alive. If someone taught martial arts to an entire gorilla troop, they must have defeated them in battle first.","└ Praise the Sun: I’m more surprised that they used tools. Aren’t they genuinely evolving into humans?","└ Allfather: That is a highly plausible hypothesis. Either they possess abnormally high intelligence, or the Forest of Four Seasons is accelerating their evolution.","└ That sounds terrifying just hearing about it. Shudder ;;","└ So that’s why the place is overflowing with miraculous herbs. Surviving there is just as difficult.","└ Grylls got lucky.","└ Forget all that. Doesn’t this mean Grylls is weaker than a gorilla?","└ Wild Grylls: Shut up. I didn’t lose.","└ If you lose, you’re officially worse than a gorilla. Lmao.","└ Lmao. A bastard inferior to an ape.","└ Wild Grylls: Don’t worry. I’m already a bastard inferior to a sloth.","└ Oh, right. Lmaoooo.","└ I forgot about that. Lmao.","Once I uploaded the post to the Gallery, everyone began chattering in their own way.","It was surprising enough that the gorilla had displayed martial arts, yet they had even used tools.","Why had humans risen to the top of the food chain?","It was precisely because they made extensive use of tools.","Fortunately, the gorillas had only used clubs. I would have struggled if they had wielded spears.","’And the person behind them...’","The \"master\" who had taught martial arts to the gorillas undoubtedly existed.","The question was whether that master was still alive.","The gorillas now recognized me as an enemy.","If they had a human master, that person should have shown at least some curiosity about me.","’Besides...’","I turned my head and looked at Namu-Ppareumbo.","Perhaps it was because his fasting pills had been stolen despite teaching the gorillas a proper lesson, but he seemed unusually dispirited today.","However, I couldn’t immediately produce fasting pills that I didn’t have.","There was also something I wanted to know.","Just what kind of creature was Namu-Ppareumbo for the gorilla troop to fear him?","That fear had allowed us to undermine the gorillas’ morale. That had been the greatest advantage of all.","\"Ppareumbo.\"","\"...\"","\"Just how strong are you for the gorillas to be so afraid of you?\"","I had become curious about Namu-Ppareumbo’s past.","Namu-Ppareumbo was strong—far stronger than I could imagine.","He had treated someone like me as insignificant, and even among the gorillas, he reigned as an object of terror.","What in the world had this creature done before I arrived?","I found myself more curious about it than usual today.","\"...\"","Instead of answering, Namu-Ppareumbo stared intently at me.","His expression seemed to ask whether I truly wanted to know.","I stared back at him for a moment before nodding.","Although it hadn’t even been a month, I could understand Namu-Ppareumbo’s intentions to some extent.","Scritch—scritch—","He began drawing on the ground.","I focused on the picture.","True to the nature of a sloth, he moved painfully slowly, but I waited patiently.","’No. Wait a minute. He’s drawing?’","I glanced at Namu-Ppareumbo.","He only looked like a sloth on the outside. I was beginning to suspect that there might be a human inside him.","Of course, like the evolved gorillas, perhaps he had simply evolved in a different direction.","Nothing that happened in the Forest of Four Seasons could be considered strange.","So I decided to let it go.","Thinking too deeply about every little thing would only give me a headache.","Scritch—scritch—","After ten minutes, the drawing gradually began to take shape.","The first thing Namu-Ppareumbo drew was himself.","Short legs compared to his long arms. Claws at the ends of his hands. Finally, even his perpetually peaceful expression.","Anyone could tell that it was Namu-Ppareumbo.","However, there wasn’t just one.","There were two, then three, then four, eventually reaching ten.","It looked like a picture of Namu-Ppareumbo’s \"family.\"","He pointed with one claw at the smallest Namu-Ppareumbo—or rather, the smallest sloth—among them.","Apparently, that one represented him.","I nodded to show that I understood.","’But there weren’t any other members of his family...’","Just as that thought crossed my mind—","Scrape—","He dragged his claw across one of the sloths in the group.","Anyone could tell that it meant the sloth had died.","Scrape—scrrrape—","One by one, Namu-Ppareumbo crossed out every member of the group except himself.","He didn’t stop until he had scratched out even the sloth standing directly beside him.","Based on this, I could form several hypotheses.","First, Namu-Ppareumbo had once belonged to a group of his own.","Second, that group had been massacred for some reason, leaving him as the sole survivor.","And lastly, the reason they had been massacred was...","\"Was it because of the gorillas?\"","Namu-Ppareumbo gave no answer.","He merely stared at the ground.","But that alone was answer enough.","Namu-Ppareumbo’s group had been defeated by the gorilla troop.","Only Namu-Ppareumbo, the sole survivor, had lived.","’They wiped out the entire group of someone this strong?’","It seemed that the gorilla troop was far stronger than I had imagined.","Either that, or—","’The person who taught them martial arts fought on their behalf.’","Neither possibility was particularly encouraging."]},{"title":"Chapter 110","paragraphs":["Welcome To (2)","The annihilation of an entire group, like what Namu-Ppareumbo had experienced, was a story that could be found not only in the wild but also throughout human civilization.","Foreigners would drive out the indigenous people who had originally occupied the land and claim it for themselves.","History contained many examples of indigenous people resisting to the bitter end, only to be forced to their knees by the foreigners’ overwhelming military power.","’So he really became stronger to survive too.’","After learning about Ppareumbo’s past, I began to see him differently.","He hadn’t been abnormally strong from the beginning. Like me, he had grown stronger in order to survive.","During that process, he must have repeatedly clashed with the gorilla troop that had seized his territory.","’...’","There was a high probability that he had single-handedly caused far more than mere chaos.","He certainly possessed enough strength to do so.","In any case, Namu-Ppareumbo was currently living with me. I couldn’t have asked for a more dependable companion.","Of course, that didn’t mean I could neglect defensive preparations.","An entire horde of gorillas might descend upon us as early as tomorrow.","’Should I move?’","The option of relocating occurred to me, but I quickly discarded it.","That was a last resort.","I would have to abandon the barricade and all the other tools I had prepared.","More importantly, with the river nearby, this base was something I absolutely needed to defend.","’I’m definitely holding this place.’","In that case, how could I defend it easily?","The best method would be to lure them toward the narrow cave entrance.","The gorillas were huge.","Even if they forced their way inside, no more than two could enter at once. That would make it easy to defeat them individually.","’But will they obediently fall for it?’","They were highly intelligent and even knew how to employ tactics.","I didn’t know whether they would behave exactly as I wanted.","Still, doing something was better than doing nothing, so I slowly began designing my defenses.","’If I want to take advantage of a confined space like I did when I killed the owlbear...’","Ultimately, I needed a door—and one sturdier than any wooden door.","The dwarf had once asked why I would bother installing a door when it would only be destroyed.","In that case, why not install a door sturdy enough that it couldn’t be destroyed?","It was an extremely simple solution.","Someone might suggest buying a safe instead, but if I was going to do that, I might as well place the entire safe in front of the entrance.","A small safe was out of the question because the gorillas might simply carry it away.","’There should be something like a CCTV camera, right?’","I would ask the dwarf to make the door and ask Cheonggu Princess about the CCTV.","Cheonggu Princess would probably give me one willingly, but I couldn’t be certain. Someone else might also have one.","Once I had roughly organized my ideas, I immediately uploaded a post to the Gallery.","***","Title: Does Anyone Here Have Something That Can Record Video? Besides the Gallery.","Wild Grylls","I’m thinking about installing a security system after the gorillas robbed my house.","Does anyone have an item that can record video while I’m away? I heard there are broadcast orbs. Can’t something be done with one of those?","I’m also planning to install a door, and I intend to make it extremely sturdy. Anyone have some advice?","└ Heavenly Demon: Would the gorillas not simply destroy the door?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll install a door sturdy enough that they can’t break it.","└ Heavenly Demon: A simple answer, but a reasonably good one.","└ SwordMaster: Why don’t you buy a safe instead? A door would probably break from a single body slam by an animal like an owlbear.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m considering a separate container. Besides, the gorillas might carry away the entire safe.","└ SwordMaster: Are those gorillas really that intelligent?","└ Wild Grylls: I think it would be easier to treat them as slightly dim-witted humans.","└ Passing Dwarf: An item like the one you described does exist. But it’s insanely expensive, so you’ll have trouble buying it.","└ Wild Grylls: How does one kilogram of orichalcon sound?","└ Passing Dwarf: This bastard was filthy rich.","└ Wild Grylls: Heh.","└ A man with an orichalcon vein in the cave outside his house. ;;","└ What if he finds adamantium later?","└ It’s not impossible. But isn’t adamantium found deep underground?","└ Who knows? Maybe Grylls will go mining later.","└ Wild Grylls: Why the hell would I go mining, you bastards?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I have the item you’re talking about, Mr. Grylls. Would you like one?","└ Wild Grylls: Then I’ll trade with you tomorrow after visiting the orichalcon cave. Is it operated similarly to a crystal orb?","└ Cheonggu Princess: I don’t know which crystal orb you mean, but it should be similar. I can also use orichalcon to prevent it from overheating, so I’ll modify it for you.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you!","└ Cheonggu Princess: If you’re grateful, what should you do?","└ Wild Grylls: Chae-U is invincible, and Kone is a god.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Kyaa! Look at that wit! Absolutely splendid!","└ He’s seriously going to wear himself out doing this. Lmao.","└ At this point, isn’t he genuinely becoming a Cheonggu fan? Lmao.","└ Seems like he’s already been completely Cheonggu-fied. O_O","***","I used the collective intelligence of the Gallery to discuss how I should renovate my shelter.","The first task was to narrow the cave entrance.","I planned to use bricks for this, just as I had when constructing the oven.","’And the dwarf agreed to make the iron door.’","Incidentally, it would be an iron door made with orichalcon mixed into it.","The dwarf said he would modify it so that, just as orichalcon absorbed mana, it could also absorb physical impacts.","Of course, he explained that its impact-absorption rate would be far lower than that of a mineral called adamantium.","’Do I seriously have to go mining for it?’","Mining—the unavoidable chore in that blocky game.","Just thinking that I might have to do it made me dizzy.","However, the Forest of Four Seasons was a place where I had no choice but to do whatever became necessary.","I wrote my plans in my notebook and looked around.","’Fortunately, they only stole the fasting pills. If they’d stolen the elixirs...’","I needed to hide the important items in an obscure corner where they would be difficult to find.","As I continued making plans to renovate the shelter one feature at a time, evening eventually arrived.","I headed up to the river to collect the fish caught in the traps and cooked food in the oven.","I began preparing to bring today’s particularly grueling routine to an end.","Oh, and I fed Namu-Ppareumbo with the fasting pills that remained.","I had brought them as emergency rations, so there was enough to last until tomorrow morning.","’I wonder if the gorillas will come tomorrow.’","Even if they did, I had no intention of going down without a fight.","As I circulated my breathing technique, I recalled the leader gorilla I had fought earlier that day.","Normally, no distracting thoughts should enter one’s mind while practicing an internal energy cultivation technique.","Strangely, however, I felt as though I could concentrate even better this way.","My breathing continued unconsciously while the battle against the leader gorilla replayed inside my head.","’I couldn’t even see the attack that struck my ribs.’","It had been the price of letting my guard down, but I genuinely hadn’t seen the leader gorilla’s final attack.","It had come from outside my field of vision.","I needed to keep that in mind.","It would be nice if I could glimpse the future like in a certain pirate manga, but something like that was probably still beyond me.","I continued visualizing the battle little by little before eventually focusing solely on the breathing technique.","\"Phew...\"","I finished circulating the technique and slowly opened my eyes.","Tomorrow would mark exactly two weeks since I had fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","It felt as though well over a month had passed, yet it had only been two weeks.","That probably meant I had been living every day in a frenzy.","It was also because I had considered every minute and second precious and tried to use my time as efficiently as possible.","’Still, it’s surprisingly manageable.’","The owlbear, the saber-toothed tiger, the orichalcon guardian, and finally, the leader gorilla.","Every one of them had been difficult to face, but I had somehow endured.","Of course, I couldn’t deny that Namu-Ppareumbo’s assistance had played the largest role.","Still, what mattered was that I had survived.","I would continue surviving, no matter what.","\"No matter what.\"","I would escape this hell.","***","The next day arrived.","As soon as dawn broke, I began my daily routine.","My shelter had been raided yesterday, but that didn’t mean I could postpone the things I needed to do.","Moreover, I planned to renovate the shelter today, so I needed to move quickly.","\"Ppareumbo, this is the last one.\"","\"...\"","\"I’ll find more somehow, so survive on grass for the time being.\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo’s final fasting pill.","He stared at it with a sorrowful expression before placing it in his mouth.","He looked rather pitiful, but I had mixed feelings when I remembered that I was the one paying tribute to him.","Still, every tribute I gave this creature increased my chances of survival, so it was well worth it.","’The Heavenly Demon said it would take time to make more fasting pills.’","I had heard that fasting pills were made using expensive medicinal herbs.","She said they would take at least a week to prepare. I wasn’t sure whether Namu-Ppareumbo could hold out until then.","If necessary, I would have no choice but to explore and gather medicinal herbs myself.","Since there was an entire colony of mature Mandrakes, a field of medicinal herbs likely existed somewhere too.","’Let’s see... Should I narrow the cave entrance this much?’","I began working on narrowing the entrance.","The owlbear had widened it when it forcibly squeezed inside.","Narrow terrain provided a natural advantage for me.","’Exploring will probably be difficult today. I should only visit the orichalcon cave.’","There was no telling when the gorillas might attack again.","Of course, now that we had clearly demonstrated that this was our territory, there was also a chance they wouldn’t return.","More importantly, Namu-Ppareumbo was here.","Unless they came as an entire horde...","Rustle—rustle—","I was examining the cave entrance when a rustling sound reached my ears.","Wondering if it could possibly be what I feared, I turned my head.","The rustling gradually grew louder.","\"...\"","Without saying a word, I armed myself as the sound drew closer.","Namu-Ppareumbo seemed to sense something as well and climbed onto my back. Wonmo also approached my side.","Eventually, the rustling became considerably louder.","\"...Huff.\"","A gorilla emerged.","It was every bit as massive as the leader gorilla, but everything about it—from its posture to its appearance—was different.","The gorillas flanking it supported themselves with both arms against the ground, while the one leading them stood upright on two legs.","More importantly...","\"Clothes?\"","It was wearing clothes.","They were old and tattered, practically no different from rags, but they were unmistakably clothes.","They were yellowed with grime, and the dye had faded until the fabric was nearly white, though traces of black could still be seen here and there.","Then there was its appearance.","Five distinct claw marks ran across its left eye.","Compared to its healthy eye, the injured one had turned cloudy white, making it easy to guess that it was blind.","It wasn’t merely unusual. There was something extraordinary about it.","That was my impression of the newly arrived gorilla.","’Did it inherit those clothes from a human?’","That was certainly how it appeared.","Judging by how old and tattered the clothes were, they looked as though they had been worn for at least ten years.","Normally, that would mean they were a deceased person’s belongings...","But did a gorilla even understand such a concept?","’And they’re carrying spears too? What the hell are they?’","As if that weren’t enough, the gorillas flanking their leader were carrying spears rather than clubs.","They were crudely crafted wooden spears, but they were still spears.","Their evolution was approaching the level of humans.","I assumed a defensive stance as I watched them.","Squeeze!","A powerful pressure gripped my shoulder.","Ppareumbo had seized it with one hand.","I turned my head and looked at Namu-Ppareumbo.","He was frowning slightly.","Since he normally maintained an expressionless face, such a clear display of emotion was highly unusual.","’Could those scars around its eye be...?’","The pieces of the puzzle were gradually clicking into place.","The gorilla I presumed to be the leader glanced to one side and jerked its head.","One of the spear-wielding gorillas then headed somewhere.","It soon returned carrying something and handed it to the leader.","Whoosh!","The leader threw the object toward me.","It didn’t feel like a declaration of war. It seemed more like it was simply giving the object to me.","Thud!","The object landed on the ground shortly afterward.","I stared at it.","It was a long, yellow fruit.","Not just one, but an entire bunch.","\"...Bananas?\"","The gorilla leader had thrown me a bunch of bananas.","At first, I had no idea what it meant.","But considering what had happened yesterday, I interpreted it this way:","I apologize for what happened yesterday. In exchange, I offer you these bananas.","In other words, it was a peace offering.","I stared blankly at the gorilla leader.","And then...","\"Ddui-bbu-chi.\"","The gorilla spoke a human \"language.\"","I couldn’t even begin to understand what it had said, but it had undoubtedly spoken.","A gorilla capable only of bestial cries couldn’t produce \"words\" like that.","’...Fuck. This really is Planet of the Apes .’","A rough voice shouting \"NO!\" echoed inside my head."]},{"title":"Chapter 111","paragraphs":["Welcome To (3)","Language.","The alpha and omega of civilization.","If human standards were applied directly to animals, one could argue that animals possessed no language.","But what if communication itself was considered a language?","Could one truly say that animals had none?","Their linguistic systems were simply less complex and less segmented than those of humans.","However, the greatest difference between humans and animals was intelligence, and that gap was clearly reflected in their use of language.","That difference gave rise to many things.","Even when humans encountered a foreign language, they could understand it to some extent as long as they made an effort to learn it.","Animals could not.","Language wasn’t something that merely needed to be memorized. Its true value could only be realized through complete comprehension.","In that sense, one could say that animals had failed to grasp the ultimate essence of language.","And right now, all that common sense came crashing down through the mouth of the gorilla chief.","Was this what it felt like to have the entire universe unfold inside one’s head?","Human words had emerged from the chief’s mouth—a language completely removed from an animal’s cries.","Could the person who had taught the gorillas martial arts have taught them language as well?","However, separate from the act of teaching them language, the important point was that they had acquired human methods of communication.","The chief had given me bananas as an apology and even bowed politely.","It undoubtedly possessed intelligence comparable to that of a human.","’Now that I look closely, it has a lot of wrinkles too.’","Its face was far more wrinkled than those of the other gorillas, giving it an air of considerable age and experience.","Then who in the world was the person who had taught it language?","After thinking for a moment, I decided to pick up the bananas first.","Judging by its polite manner and the overall atmosphere, it had clearly offered them as an apology.","Even if it launched a surprise attack, I had Namu-Ppareumbo with me, so I wasn’t worried.","\"Ni chou narira?\"","\"...What the hell are you saying?\"","When I picked up the bananas, the gorilla chief spoke again.","However, I didn’t know any of this world’s languages, so I couldn’t understand it.","’Judging by the intonation, it sounds somewhat similar to Chinese...’","This world had a place called the Central Plains, a nation resembling those found in martial arts stories.","If it was anything like the martial worlds I knew, it wouldn’t be strange for its people to speak a language resembling Chinese.","That didn’t change the fact that I had no idea what the words meant.","This was precisely when I needed the Gallery.","I opened the Gallery and began recording a video. I planned to upload it.","\"Could you... say that again?\"","I made a circular gesture with my hand to indicate that I wanted it to repeat itself.","I had unconsciously spoken politely, but I didn’t bother worrying about that.","Fortunately, it seemed to understand my gesture.","The chief stared at me before repeating the same words.","\"Ni chou narira?\"","\"Just a moment, please.\"","I immediately uploaded the recorded video to the Gallery.","I desperately hoped it was the language of the Central Plains.","If so, the Heavenly Demon could translate it immediately.","***","Title: Emergeeeency!!! The Gorilla Can Speak!!!","Wild Grylls","(Video of the gorilla chief speaking a human language)","I’m starting to get really scared. Does anyone know what it’s saying?","Gorillas in the Forest of Four Seasons can speak human languages. Can anyone translate this?","└ Heavenly Demon: ??? Why is a gorilla speaking the language of the Central Plains? Is this truly happening?","└ Wild Grylls: I’d broadcast it live if I could, but that isn’t possible right now. This is really happening.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm... I do not know where that gorilla learned it, but it is indeed speaking the language of the Central Plains. It is even using an archaic form of the language.","└ Wild Grylls: An archaic form?","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady means that it speaks as the elders do.","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t you an old fossil yourself?","└ Heavenly Demon: Did this lady not say that she only recently entered the prime of her youth?","└ SwordMaster: How can you say that while talking like some ancient relic? ;;","└ Allfather: Oh. My. God. By Aragorn, what am I looking at?","└ Wild Grylls: A video of a gorilla speaking a human language.","└ Allfather: Oh. Fuck. This must be an omen of the world’s destruction.","└ Wild Grylls: Are you okay? ;;","└ Allfather: I shall go relieve my urges for a moment.","└ Wild Grylls: Dude... ;;","└ Wait, can that gorilla seriously speak?","└ Monsters capable of human speech appear occasionally. Orc shamans and goblin sorcerers, for example.","└ Sure, but have you ever seen a gorilla speaking a human language?","└ Of course not. Lmao. What the hell is that? Lmao.","└ It even seems to have learned the language of the Central Plains. Lmao.","└ Who the hell taught it?","└ Judging by the way it speaks, that dialect is ancient as hell. It sounds like something people would’ve used during the Righteous-Blood War.","└ When did the Righteous-Blood War happen?","└ About sixty years ago, I think.","└ Why is it wearing clothes too? Lmao.","└ Looks like it’s wearing a dead person’s clothes.","└ Gorilla fashion. Lmao.","***","Countless comments appeared in less than a minute.","Most people said it was unbelievable or accused me of using ventriloquism.","They offered all sorts of wild theories, but this was the reality in front of me.","’Anyway, it asked where I came from, right?’","It was time to answer.","If I kept it waiting, I might ruin its first impression of me.","However, I didn’t know a single word that it could understand.","[Heavenly Demon: Do you wish for this lady to teach you what to say?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? How did you know?]","[Heavenly Demon: Considering the situation, that much is easy to deduce. However, although the Gallery can convey written words, it cannot transmit spoken language. Unless this lady knew your native tongue, it would likely be difficult.]","[Wild Grylls: Then could you show me how to write \"Republic of Korea\" in the language of the Central Plains?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is easily done. Wait a moment.]","While the Heavenly Demon wrote down the words, I attempted to converse with the gorilla chief.","Of course, the chief merely reacted as though it had no idea what I was saying, so I accomplished nothing.","It had only been an attempt to buy time, so I waited patiently.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon. Heavenly Demon. Could you help me?]","[Heavenly Demon: (Photo of \"Republic of Korea\" written in the language of the Central Plains on a sheet of paper) Will this suffice?]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you!]","[Heavenly Demon: Ask whenever you require assistance. From what this lady can see, you will continue to need her.]","I copied the characters from the Heavenly Demon’s photograph onto the ground.","I would have preferred to write them in the notebook inside the cave, but I didn’t know what might happen while I went to retrieve it.","When I began writing on the ground, the gorilla chief shifted its gaze toward the characters.","It tilted its head before looking back up at me and speaking.","\"Buchidao.\"","I recorded it and immediately sent the video to the Heavenly Demon.","According to her, it had answered, \"I don’t know.\"","Naturally, it couldn’t have known.","The Republic of Korea was a country from another world.","\"Yao. Shabi?\"","\"Bu.\"","\"Kai. Zama. Jubeo?\"","\"Junja tungpeo.\"","The chief then began conversing with one of the spear-wielding gorillas beside it.","Judging by their behavior, the spear-wielders seemed to be something like its personal guards.","Unlike the gorilla chief, who spoke fluently, the guards spoke in short, broken phrases.","I recorded their conversation and sent it to the Heavenly Demon.","[Heavenly Demon: That ape is asking whether they may kill you. It says you are the enemy who slew its kin.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Heavenly Demon: The chief says there is no need. Finding the bodies of their kin takes priority.]","The bodies of their kin.","They seemed to be referring to the gorillas I had killed yesterday.","Still, perhaps an ape remained an ape even after learning a language, because they openly discussed killing me while I stood right in front of them.","Or perhaps they had deliberately spoken where I could hear them.","I waited for their response.","\"Ssŭchi dorenma?\"","According to the Heavenly Demon, it was asking where its dead kin were.","Since they were the bastards who had stolen my food, I didn’t want to tell them so readily.","Moreover, if I conceded too easily, they might look down on me. I needed to proceed cautiously.","Scritch—scritch—","I wrote some characters on the ground.","They roughly meant:","What if I don’t want to tell you?","The chief carefully examined what I had written before responding.","\"Hwiurulseda.\"","According to the translation, it meant:","There will be blood.","I could tell from its half-threatening tone even before receiving the translation.","’It can even use figurative expressions?’","The figurative expression was surprising enough, but the fact that it could convey nuance through its tone was even more astonishing.","Just how intelligent was this creature?","I narrowed my eyes and stared back at the chief’s ferocious gaze before glancing at the gorillas beside it.","’Assuming the chief is as strong as Namu-Ppareumbo...’","There were approximately five other gorillas, including the guards.","We were at a numerical disadvantage.","If we fought, we would inevitably lose.","It was best to avoid battles with such poor odds whenever possible.","In particular, the fact that the chief had offered me bananas meant that it was willing to resolve the situation peacefully.","’Let’s avoid fighting.’","I imposed a condition.","I would show them where their kin were buried, but they had to leave immediately afterward.","When I wrote the condition on the ground, the chief nodded.","I didn’t know whether it would honor its promise, but reaching an agreement was still the best choice available.","\"They’re here.\"","When I showed them where the gorillas had been buried, the chief jerked its head.","One of the gorillas—an ordinary soldier rather than a personal guard—stepped forward and began digging.","It dug with its bare hands.","However, given a gorilla’s physical capabilities, it excavated the ground as rapidly as a mechanical digger.","Before long, it began pulling out the buried corpses one by one.","Since I had only buried them yesterday, they were still intact, without any signs of decomposition.","’Will this satisfy them?’","I watched the gorillas carry away the bodies before glancing at the chief.","It remained standing in place, silently observing until the other gorillas disappeared into the forest.","Once every one of its subordinates had vanished, the chief addressed me.","\"Shincha.\"","\"Huh?\"","\"Shishin pangeol laotera.\"","As expected, I had no idea what it was saying.","However, I always kept the Gallery open.","I sent the recording to the Heavenly Demon.","[Heavenly Demon: It says that it is time to discuss a personal matter.]","[Wild Grylls: A personal matter?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is not a particularly good sign. In the murim, when someone distinguishes between public and personal affairs, a fight usually follows.]","Was I going to have to fight this creature?","I slowly retreated.","The chief saw my reaction and spoke impassively.","\"Chinpalli lyushi eomeon kwoeo.\"","\"...\"","\"Sunzŭ shi billa. Ni shie jeungpandeo.\"","Invading your territory was our fault.","My grandson was discourteous. Your actions were justified.","\"Keoshi baenzhu join shien shin. Haio sso kong.\"","However, this Sovereign is the leader of the troop—and the boy’s grandfather.","The moment I heard the translation this Sovereign , I couldn’t help but stare dumbfounded.","The Heavenly Demon seemed equally astonished, immediately revealing her feelings after translating it.","[Heavenly Demon: How arrogant. A mere ape dares to call itself \"this Sovereign.\" Who in the world taught it that?]","[Wild Grylls: Maybe the person who taught it used that expression?]","[Heavenly Demon: Whoever it was taught the creature improperly. None but the greatest under heaven may refer to themselves by that title.]","More importantly, the chief’s aura was becoming increasingly ominous.","Even its personal guards gradually retreated, creating the unmistakable atmosphere of an imminent fight.","I slowly circulated the mana within my body and infused the Heavenly Demon’s sword with aura.","Unless I took it by surprise, defeating the chief seemed impossible.","\"Ssuai.\"","Therefore...","\"Na joi ikeubeo.\"","I shall take one of your arms.","The instant the Heavenly Demon finished translating, I charged.","Aura shimmered around the Heavenly Demon’s sword like a heat haze.","No—it had far surpassed the level of an ordinary heat haze.","Flames.","The sword’s aura surged like raging flames.","If I struck the gorilla chief with it, its body would be cleaved in two.","Don’t call me a coward.","This was the best I could do.","What wouldn’t I do to survive?","This was a place where the one who survived was the strong one.","’Good. I caught it completely off guard!’","The chief didn’t react even when the sword entered striking distance.","Perhaps it had failed to respond in time.","This was my chance.","If I continued forward and cleaved through its torso—","That never happened.","Instead, an unbelievable sight unfolded before my eyes.","Aura blazed like fire around the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","It was a strike capable of effortlessly slicing through an animal’s flesh and bones with the slightest contact.","Yet the gorilla chief casually caught it.","Not with one hand.","With only three fingers—its thumb, index finger, and middle finger.","As I stared in disbelief, the chief spoke with a serene expression.","\"Hao chil reo.\"","I didn’t know what it meant.","Even so, I was now certain of one thing.","The gorilla chief was far stronger than I had ever imagined."]},{"title":"Chapter 112","paragraphs":["Welcome To (4)","If I had to choose the most difficult opponent among all the creatures I had fought to the death, it would undoubtedly be the saber-toothed tiger.","A tiger’s natural ferocity. Its terrifying size. Its absurd regenerative ability.","Without Namu-Ppareumbo’s timely assistance, I would have died several times over.","That ordeal had allowed me to achieve tremendous growth. Without the saber-toothed tiger, I probably couldn’t have defeated the guardian either.","I had encountered all sorts of bizarre creatures since then, but I had never been defeated.","Whenever a beast that seemed likely to beat me appeared, I fled immediately rather than fighting it.","Fwoosh!","Aura surged around the Heavenly Demon’s sword like blazing flames.","I stared blankly at the gorilla chief holding the sword between its fingers.","Even though I had swung with all my strength, it had caught the blade effortlessly.","I might have understood if it had caught it with its entire hand.","But it had used only its fingers.","The fundamental strength I had gained from eating the eel and the additional strength I had acquired through cultivating internal energy—","Even with all of that combined, I had been stopped by three fingers.","\"Urgh...!\"","I couldn’t even pull the sword free.","No matter how much strength I exerted, it wouldn’t budge.","While I desperately struggled, the chief remained perfectly calm.","It was silently demonstrating just how vast the gap between us was.","There was a reason it had confidently declared that it would take one of my arms.","Release!","\"Whoa!\"","While I was desperately pulling on the sword, the chief suddenly relaxed its grip.","The resulting recoil nearly sent me tumbling backward in an embarrassing heap.","I barely regained my balance and faced the chief again.","It had even folded its massive arms across its chest.","\"Bugou.\"","I had no time to access the Gallery in this situation.","Still, one thing was obvious.","It was looking down on me.","Realizing that, I decided to attack more carefully.","\"Kyuu! Kyuu!\"","At that moment, Wonmo, who had remained still until now, suddenly charged into the fight.","Apparently, he had identified the chief as an enemy.","Just as I was about to order Wonmo to stay back, someone else intervened first.","\"Kyuu?\"","\"...\"","It was Namu-Ppareumbo, who had climbed down from my back at some point.","Ppareumbo stepped in front of Wonmo and gestured for him to retreat.","Wonmo initially looked confused before turning his head toward me.","\"Wonmo, do as Ppareumbo says.\"","\"Kyuu...\"","Only then did Wonmo retreat.","Ppareumbo went so far as to push him all the way into the cave.","Afterward, Namu-Ppareumbo didn’t climb back onto my back. Instead, he moved some distance away and began watching.","Observing from there would make it easier for him to intervene than if he were clinging to my back.","’Looks like he understands the situation.’","The chief’s personal guards were also standing still and watching.","This meant that it was a fight between the chief and me.","Ppareumbo seemed to have understood that as well.","Or perhaps, as always, he intended to intervene if I found myself in danger.","It seemed I could trust him a little.","I gripped my sword and shield and glared at the chief.","It remained motionless with its arms folded.","It didn’t even have a prominent nose, yet it still managed to look unbearably arrogant.","\"Hmph!\"","Then I would make it pay for letting its guard down.","I kicked off the ground and thrust my sword.","The attack came without warning.","Moreover, it was a thrust rather than a slash.","It utilized the exceptional sharpness of the Heavenly Demon’s sword to its absolute limit.","If it chose to block the attack as it had before, it would be severely injured.","Swoosh!","My sword pierced the chief directly in the abdomen.","At least, that was how it looked.","’What?’","But the sensation was strange.","I was certain I had stabbed it, yet it didn’t feel as though I had pierced anything.","It felt like thrusting into empty air.","The discrepancy between what I saw and what I felt was deeply unsettling.","Shimmer—","Shortly after that thought crossed my mind, a change occurred in the chief.","Its figure wavered like a mirage before vanishing entirely.","Startled, I hurriedly pulled back my sword and looked around.","’Where is it—?!’","A chill!","An ominous instinct sent a chill through the back of my head.","I had only lived in the Forest of Four Seasons for two weeks, but I had already learned something important.","I must never ignore an ominous feeling—my instincts.","This time, I chose to trust them.","Slash!","I spun around and swung my sword horizontally.","The flame-like aura swept violently through the air.","\"Hmm.\"","The chief was standing behind me.","Unlike before, its arms were no longer folded.","Apparently, it had attempted to ambush me but failed.","I didn’t let the opportunity pass.","It was still underestimating me.","\"Huaah!\"","With a fierce shout, I slashed, thrust, and slashed again.","The chief must have been surprised by my ferocity because it made no attempt to counterattack and focused solely on evading.","Slash!","Again.","I had definitely cut it, yet I felt no resistance.","At the same time, the chief’s figure faded like a mirage.","What in the world was this technique?","Could Namu-Ppareumbo use it as well?","I hurriedly turned around, remembering to slash with my sword as a precaution.","Slash!","The gorilla wasn’t behind me.","There was nothing but empty air.","At that exact moment, the back of my head began to tingle.","It had completely fooled me.","However, I couldn’t simply turn around and slash again.","That would be impossible unless my waist could rotate a full three hundred and sixty degrees.","Therefore, I chose the next-best option.","’I have to block with my shield!’","I twisted my waist back into its original position and raised my shield.","Fortunately, my decision seemed correct because the chief’s fist was heading directly toward it.","Just how powerful was that fist?","It belonged to a creature that had effortlessly caught my sword.","I might be sent flying backward, so I should also prepare to break my fall—","\"...\"","Yet contrary to all my expectations, the chief’s attack was anticlimactic.","No impact traveled through the shield.","It merely felt as though the chief had gently placed its fist against it.","The chief pressed its fist against my shield.","That was all.","Confused, I looked into its eyes.","Its expression was perfectly serene.","’Why?’","Before that question could even fade—","Thump!","A strange sensation traveled through the shield.","Crack!","A sound like a snapping branch reached my ears.","At the same time, the shield slipped downward.","Even though I was gripping it firmly, it fell limply from my grasp.","Wondering what had happened, I lowered my gaze toward the shield.","Then I realized why the shield had fallen.","It hadn’t disobeyed my will.","Dangle—dangle—","My arm had broken, leaving it incapable of carrying out my commands.","I stared blankly at the arm hanging limply by my side.","But only for a moment.","The pain that my adrenaline had barely suppressed came surging in.","\"Aaaaaaargh!\"","The agony of a broken bone was beyond imagination.","Hadn’t I suffered from broken ribs only yesterday?","I even dropped my sword as I grabbed my dangling arm.","It felt as though someone were stabbing needles directly into my brain.","’H-How? It only touched its fist against my shield...!’","Its body dispersing like a mirage, and now this attack—","Everything about it defied comprehension.","The chief’s abilities completely surpassed my common sense.","\"Urgh...! Haaah...!\"","\"...\"","While I gritted my teeth and endured the pain, the chief silently stared at me.","Its expression seemed to ask:","Do you wish to continue?","I answered through my actions.","Swoop—","I picked up the Heavenly Demon’s sword from the ground.","One arm was broken, but the other remained intact.","I wrung out every last bit of mana I possessed and concentrated it into the sword.","Hummm—","Perhaps I had instinctively sensed the danger.","The aura that had previously billowed like flames gradually began condensing.","I couldn’t die here.","My desperate desire to survive pushed my concentration to its absolute limit.","Just as the flame-like aura began assuming a definite shape, the chief moved.","At first, it merely appeared to bend its knees slightly.","I reacted the instant I saw the movement, but—","Swoosh!","Before I could even register what had happened, the chief was standing directly before me.","Its speed equaled Namu-Ppareumbo’s—perhaps even surpassed it.","I slowly looked up at the chief standing proudly on two legs.","Had I ever been overwhelmed so completely before?","Its presence erased even the faintest desire to resist.","The feeling resembled what I had experienced while confronting the saber-toothed tiger, yet it was also fundamentally different.","Swoosh—","The chief pulled its right arm back.","Its hand wasn’t clenched into a fist.","It appeared to be preparing a palm strike.","The instant that palm struck me directly, I would die.","I had to move my body somehow if I wanted to survive.","Yet perhaps because I had already been utterly overwhelmed, my legs refused to move.","’I can’t die like this...!’","I struggled desperately.","I even bit my tongue as I forced myself to move.","Fortunately, that desperate resistance seemed to work, and I barely managed to move my legs.","Next came my arm.","Under the illusion that time itself had slowed, I tried to raise it.","Whoosh!","The problem was that the chief could also act within that fleeting moment.","The arm it had drawn back shot forward like a bullet.","Its enormous gorilla palm completely filled my vision.","Just as I resigned myself to dying—","Baaaaang!","The chief’s palm swept past the side of my face.","The explosive burst of air left my ears ringing, while my hair whipped violently in the wind.","Craaaaaash!","My one relatively functional ear allowed me to guess what had happened behind me.","The noise wasn’t merely something collapsing.","It sounded as though everything had been completely obliterated.","I desperately hoped the cave hadn’t been behind me.","\"...\"","I froze in place.","Only my eyes could move.","Slowly, I shifted my trembling gaze toward the chief.","For some reason, it was smiling.","The chief lowered the hand that had passed beside my face and placed it on my shoulder.","Even though it had merely rested its hand there, it felt unbearably heavy.","Pat, pat—","The chief patted my shoulder several times as though telling me to relax.","It had truthfully said that it would take one of my arms.","But it had never said that it would take my life.","The chief removed its hand from my shoulder and spoke in the language of the Central Plains.","\"Wai wonni.\"","Welcome to the Forest of Four Seasons.","\"Shinshou.\"","Youngster.","For some reason, I felt certain that was what it was saying.","\"Zheoba.\"","The chief turned around and issued an order to its personal guards.","The spear-wielding guards merely glanced at me once before following it.","I remained rooted in place until the chief and its party disappeared.","\"Phew...\"","Only after they had been gone for some time did I finally manage to exhale.","I paid no attention to my broken arm dangling at my side.","More precisely, I was incapable of doing so.","My pounding heart felt as though it might burst at any moment.","It was like someone was forcibly pressing down upon my entire body.","The saber-toothed tiger had inspired an instinctive, primal fear.","The chief’s pressure, however, had felt almost deliberately manufactured.","’Who in the world...?’","At the same time, I became curious about the person who had taught the chief martial arts.","Just who was its master to have trained a gorilla into such an extraordinary expert?","I gradually organized my chaotic thoughts and came back to my senses.","My immediate priority was treating my broken arm.","Leaving it in this condition could result in severe lasting complications.","’Will an elixir even heal this...?’","I was carefully holding my arm to prevent the broken bones from twisting when I turned around and froze.","The chief had launched a palm strike beside my face.","I had clearly heard something being destroyed behind me.","I had assumed that a tree had simply fallen, but the reality far exceeded my expectations.","A \"road\" had appeared.","The area had originally been filled with densely packed trees.","But a single palm strike from the chief had sent trees crashing down or torn them out by their roots.","The unexpected road left me feeling faint.","’...Even Sun Wukong couldn’t do something like this.’","Then again, Sun Wukong wasn’t a gorilla. He was a monkey with a tail.","Whatever.","’Can I really survive here?’","Either way, my resolve had been shaken."]},{"title":"Chapter 113","paragraphs":["Welcome To (5)","I barely managed to immobilize my dangling arm before returning to the cave.","When I arrived, I found Wonmo pacing back and forth.","It seemed he had been beside himself with worry while I was gone.","\"Kyuu! Kyuu!\"","Wonmo gave me an enthusiastic welcome when he saw me return injured.","I would have loved to hug him with both arms, but that was rather difficult with one arm in this state.","\"Wonmo, wait just a moment. Let me fix my arm first.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","Wonmo answered energetically and took a small step back. Good little Wonmo was such a good listener.","I chuckled and carefully lowered my arm. First, I needed to remove the shield.","I had suffered plenty of injuries before, but this was my first time breaking an arm, so I wasn’t sure what to do.","’What if I pour the elixir on it without knowing what I’m doing and the bone heals crooked?’","That was my greatest concern.","My ribs hadn’t been shattered as badly as my arm.","It seemed best to immobilize it with a splint first.","Using my good arm, I found a suitable plank of wood.","All I had to do was cut one of the logs I had split for the campfire down to an appropriate size.","’And buy some cloth from the Gallery.’","Then I simply had to place the splint against my arm and tie it in place. The problem was that doing so with only one usable arm was difficult.","\"Hey, Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","Hold this for me, will you? My arm’s in a bit of a state.\"","I asked Namu-Ppareumbo for help. He might not be able to tie it, but he should at least be able to hold the cloth.","Namu-Ppareumbo stared silently at me before holding the cloth as I had asked.","With that, I managed to fashion a splint using the piece of wood and cloth.","This was only a temporary measure, however. Pouring elixir on it would be the real treatment.","Title: My Arm Got Wrecked","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an arm in a splint)","Fought the leader gorilla and got my arm wrecked. Good thing the leader gorilla spared me. Otherwise, I’d be dead, lol.","Anyway, can I just pour elixir over my arm like this? I was worried the bone might heal out of alignment, so I only immobilized it with a splint for now.","└ Heavenly Demon: Was the monkey strong?","└ Wild Grylls: Absurdly strong. My arm broke even though I blocked it with my shield. It didn’t even punch the shield. It just placed its fist against it.","└ Heavenly Demon: Your arm broke merely from it touching the shield?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It literally just tapped it.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think it can even use Penetrating Force. Its cultivation must be remarkably advanced. I did not anticipate this.","└ Wild Grylls: And when I swung my sword at it, its body vanished like a mirage before it reappeared directly behind me.","└ Heavenly Demon: Even Shifting Form and Position? How astonishing. It appears the creature showed you mercy.","└ SwordMaster: You’re really lucky to be alive. If that gorilla had gone all out, you would’ve died in less than a second.","└ Wild Grylls: I even launched a surprise attack, but it stopped my sword with nothing but its fingers. That was when I knew it was over.","└ SwordMaster: How many fingers did it use?","└ Wild Grylls: Three.","└ SwordMaster: It must have used three because it was you, Mr. Grylls. It probably would’ve used only one against most people.","└ Wild Grylls: It probably also sensed the power of the sword the Heavenly Demon gave me.","└ What kind of gorilla uses Penetrating Force and Shifting Form and Position? I won’t believe it until I see it myself;;","└ It can speak a human language, so why wouldn’t it be possible?","└ Honestly, this sounds like a lie. You might as well say it can fire palm blasts.","└ Wild Grylls: I don’t know about palm blasts, but it did destroy the entire forest. I’ll show you later.","└ What the hell? Did it actually fire a palm blast? Lol.","└ Not even the monkeys from mythology were like that, lol.","└ Monkeys appear in mythology?","└ It’s a story from the Central Plains. A monkey became a mystical creature by imitating human behavior.","└ Oh. Sounds interesting.","└ Starlight Princess: Is your arm completely broken?","└ Wild Grylls: Yes. It’s dangling loosely. I can pour elixir on it as it is, right? I was worried the bone might heal incorrectly, so I immobilized it with a splint first.","└ Starlight Princess: You made the right choice. Bones actually do heal out of alignment fairly often. Parts of the torso are strongly affected just by drinking elixir, but that isn’t the case with the limbs.","└ Wild Grylls: Would it heal quickly if I cut my arm open with a knife and poured the elixir inside?","└ Starlight Princess: I’ll just give you a syringe. I used to be ill, so I had to use syringes frequently.","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Is there anything you want in return? I don’t think I’ll be able to go outside today, but I should be able to give it to you tomorrow.","└ Starlight Princess: Just stay alive and in one piece. You’re really starting to seem like you could drop dead at any moment.","└ Wild Grylls: Yes, ma’am.","└ But his life really is hanging by a thread, isn’t it?","└ Honestly, I don’t think he’ll last a month.","└ Hasn’t it only been exactly two weeks?","└ I wonder what’ll appear after the gorilla, lol.","└ Good thing the gorilla showed him mercy. Otherwise, everything could’ve ended today, lol.","└ PraiseTheSun: Should I try raising a gorilla too? I wonder whether I could teach it martial arts.","└ Wild Grylls: Try teaching it to speak first. I’m curious whether it’s possible too.","└ PraiseTheSun: Wouldn’t simple sign language be possible? A chimpanzee I raised before could do it.","└ Wild Grylls: You raised a chimpanzee?;;","└ PraiseTheSun: Yeah. But it eventually died because of its limited lifespan. I doted on that little guy.","└ Upvote if you think that chimp lived better than you, lol.","└ Lol, they say that even if you become a slave, you should become a nobleman’s slave~","└ I’d rather become a chimpanzee, lol.","└ My intelligence is lower than a chimp’s. Could you raise me?","└ Then share some of your intelligence with me. You’re no different from a chimpanzee or monkey anyway.","└ Instead of becoming my pet, just become my slave. I’ll take good care of you.","└ You bastards, lol.","While the people in the Gallery continued their chatter, I received the syringe from Starlight Princess.","[Starlight Princess: I gave you a new one just in case, so you can use it without worrying.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I just fill this with elixir and inject it into my arm, right?]","[Starlight Princess: Yes. Please use it carefully.]","The syringe looked both similar to and different from the ones I knew.","Its basic shape was identical, but its material and size were completely different.","It was especially large. The barrel was thick, though the needle was relatively small.","\"If even the needle had been huge... Ugh.\"","I filled the syringe with elixir and checked whether it flowed properly.","Golden liquid trickled from the tip of the needle. This should be enough.","I then inserted the needle into the spot where my arm had broken and slowly injected the elixir.","’I look like some drug addict shooting up.’","The elixir’s distinctive cooling sensation spread through my arm, and the pain gradually subsided.","I could even feel the bones knitting together, so it seemed to have mostly healed.","Nevertheless, I planned to keep the splint on for the rest of the day if possible.","I had heard that broken bones could leave some fairly serious aftereffects.","’At least I survived.’","I took a sip of elixir and stared up at the ceiling.","Despite the Forest of Four Seasons’ notoriety, I had thought it was surprisingly easy to survive here. That had been a grave miscalculation.","I simply hadn’t encountered an irregular existence like the leader gorilla until now.","Even the saber-toothed tiger would be nothing more than a house cat before that gorilla.","’So there are creatures as powerful as that gorilla?’","Just how strong were they?","The thought frightened me a little.","After all, I didn’t even have to travel far to find those monstrous crabs and crayfish that looked as though they had stepped straight out of a kaiju movie.","However, their habitats were different, and their enormous size made them easy to avoid.","The real problem was creatures like the leader gorilla—small enough to be difficult to spot and living nearby.","As I brooded over the situation, my gaze suddenly fell upon Namu-Ppareumbo.","He had merely watched without intervening even though I had nearly died.","Had he refrained because the gorilla’s royal guards would have joined the fight the moment he interfered?","Or had he already known that the leader gorilla would show me mercy?","I wasn’t sure of the details, but it was obvious that Namu-Ppareumbo had some sort of history with the leader gorilla.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo.\"","\"Can you use that Shifting Form and Position thing too? You know, where you disappear and then reappear somewhere else.\"","Nod—","Namu-Ppareumbo answered by nodding.","Seeing that, I nodded as well. Offering tribute to this guy had definitely been the right decision.","’Come to think of it...’","After Namu-Ppareumbo, my gaze fell upon the bananas.","It was the bunch of bananas the leader gorilla had thrown to me as an apology.","To be precise, it was three clusters of bananas bound together, practically an entire set.","This would be enough to keep me from worrying about food for a while. Or I could eat them as snacks.","’Let’s try one.’","I was feeling gloomy, so I might as well eat something sweet.","I plucked off a banana.","I didn’t take only one for myself. I also picked one each for Namu-Ppareumbo and Wonmo.","\"Here. Eat up.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","\"...\"","My animal companions began eating the bananas in their own ways.","Wonmo, who had an insatiable weakness for sweets, practically buried his face in his banana, while Namu-Ppareumbo simply stared at his.","He probably felt reluctant to eat a banana given to him by his enemy. Still, judging by the way he peeled it, he didn’t seem completely opposed to the idea.","’It’s been a long time since I ate a banana.’","I struggled to peel it with one hand.","I wanted to use my left hand, but I intended to rest it just to be safe.","Munch, munch—","\"...Oh?\"","The moment I took a bite, a honey-like sweetness filled my mouth.","It even possessed the distinctive fragrance of a banana. It was literally a banana as sweet as honey.","No wonder Wonmo had buried his entire face in his. It was a flavor that filled you with joy.","’Can a banana really have such a high sugar content?’","These bananas had grown while absorbing an abundance of mana. Even Southeast Asian bananas probably weren’t this sweet.","They were enormous too. A single banana was as large as my forearm.","I devoured the banana ravenously, gradually calming my troubled mind.","’He really did give me something good.’","Of course, it was still far inferior to the fasting pills.","At first, I had even thought he was telling me to take these and get lost.","But considering how delicious they were, it seemed he had done his best in his own way.","How could he possibly obtain something as nutritious as a fasting pill in this place?","Simple medicinal herbs were one thing, but fasting pills were man-made food created by combining various herbs.","\"Nom, nom, nom.\"","Wonmo even ate all the banana peels. They were delicious, but I worried they might give him diarrhea.","I leaned against the cave wall and glanced at my broken arm.","No matter how many times I thought about it, it was astonishing. The gorilla had merely placed its fist against my shield, yet my arm had broken.","Would I ever be able to perform a feat like that?","It seemed difficult to learn something like that solely through posts on the Gallery.","’Wait. Come to think of it...’","It had happened just before the leader gorilla delivered its final strike.","When my survival instincts had surged and my concentration had reached its absolute limit.","I remembered how the aura that had billowed like flames gradually condensed and began taking shape.","’I need to practice before I forget that feeling.’","The sensation still lingered within me. The impact it had left was simply that profound.","I immediately brought over the Heavenly Demon’s sword and manifested my aura.","When I infused it with a small amount of mana, aura rose from it like a heat haze.","If I infused it with just a little more power, it surged like flames.","’Let’s slowly recall what I felt back then.’","The sensation of that formless energy crushing my entire body.","How I had even bitten my tongue in my desperate attempt to escape that pressure.","Although I hadn’t completed it, merely grasping the first clue was enough.","Woooong—woong—woooong—","Nevertheless, it was still difficult. The aura refused to condense properly.","Even so, I occasionally saw parts of the flame-like aura diminish.","It wasn’t because I had stopped supplying it with mana. If anything, I was forcibly pumping more and more mana into it, yet its volume still decreased.","It hadn’t taken on a complete form, but even this alone was remarkable progress.","’The problem is that there’s so much aura that it’s difficult to control.’","I would eventually achieve results if I continued practicing slowly.","I put down the sword and accessed the Gallery.","The moment I logged in, I saw everyone talking about me.","They were saying that a talking gorilla was obviously fiction and that I had made the whole thing up.","’This is why I recorded it, you bastards.’","So I uploaded all the footage of the gorilla speaking to the Gallery.","The Heavenly Demon had translated everything it said, but far too many people still refused to believe me.","’They probably don’t have things like video editing or AI here.’","Then again, if they did, that would be fascinating in its own way.","I quietly checked the Gallery’s comments.","└ What kind of fabricated translation is this?","└ Damn.","└ Bull.","└ Shit.","\"...\"","Or maybe not.","Perhaps people were the same everywhere."]},{"title":"Chapter 114","paragraphs":["Mining (1)","Title: Come See a Talking Gorilla","Wild Grylls","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the royal guards and leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla speaking)","(Video of the leader gorilla threatening me)","Too many people refused to believe me, so I’m uploading these.","Watch them and decide for yourselves whether I’m lying.","└ Heavenly Demon: It is fascinating no matter how many times I see it. Even its manner of speech sounds like something from ancient times.","└ SwordMaster: I don’t know the language of the Central Plains very well. What is it saying?","└ Heavenly Demon: It says SwordMaster is a liar and that only the Heavenly Demon is great.","└ SwordMaster: There you go, lying every time you open your mouth again;;","└ What’s with the fake translation?","└ F—","└ U—","└ Cker.","└ What the hell is this? Lmao.","└ Look at that teamwork, lol.","└ Allfather: By Aragon! Not only the leader, but even the gorillas beside it can speak. This will send shock waves through academia...!","└ Professor, won’t those gorillas pose a threat to us?","└ Allfather: That is unlikely. It might be a different story if they developed the Forest of Four Seasons into a civilization of their own.","└ A civilization in the Forest of Four Seasons, damn.","└ I heard those bastards are strong, lol. They even know how to use tools.","└ Once they start farming, the second human race will be complete.","└ Then should we classify them as beastmen? What exactly are they?","└ Wouldn’t we have to classify them as beastmen?","└ Suspiciously: It’s hard to call them beastmen. Their limb proportions aren’t right.","└ Allfather: The commenter above is correct. To be classified as beastmen, they must possess bodily proportions similar to humans.","└ Clever Main: By the way, do you know that guy’s name? If they have a language, they must have names too.","└ Wouldn’t whoever taught it to speak have given it a name? Does Grylls know?","└ Looks like he went off to do something else. He isn’t replying to any comments.","└ Clever Main: Then we’ll have to name it ourselves. How about Sun Wukong-plus-one?","└ What the hell is Sun Wukong-plus-one? Lol.","└ Clever Main: Sun Wukong is the name of a monkey from the mythology of the Central Plains. That guy isn’t a monkey but a gorilla, so he’s Sun Wukong-plus-one. Isn’t it fucking brilliant?","└ Holy shit, are you a genius? Your IQ must be over 150!","└ Clever Main: I am pretty smart, lol.","└ And yet a guy like you wastes his time on the Gallery, lol.","It was the Gallery, all right. Toss them one juicy topic, and they would happily entertain themselves.","Some of their speculation was occasionally meaningful, so browsing through it was quite useful.","’If everyone thinks they speak in an archaic manner, someone from the old days must have taught them.’","The most noteworthy detail was the leader gorilla’s archaic speech.","Languages naturally changed over time.","Even without looking far back, there were plenty of differences between the Korean spoken fifty years ago and the Korean spoken today.","Moreover, I had heard that the Jeonghyeol War, which occurred approximately sixty years ago, had brought significant changes to the language of the Central Plains.","In other words, the leader gorilla was speaking the language as it would have been spoken by someone from that era.","’All sorts of things really have happened.’","From the Immortal King to the Jeonghyeol War.","Such was human history. Roughly half of it inevitably ended up being marked by war and bloodshed.","People beating and fighting one another day after day was practically normal.","’It’s the same here.’","The wilderness was no different. It was a place where battles for survival took place every single day.","Hadn’t the leader gorilla nearly killed me just moments ago?","I was in no position to criticize anyone. As I had repeatedly said, I had more than enough problems of my own.","I considered how I should spend the rest of the day.","The leader gorilla had completely disrupted my plans, so I needed to revise them.","’Should I... build the door and wall?’","One slap from the leader gorilla would bring down any door or wall I constructed.","Even in The Three Little Pigs , the house built from bricks had remained standing.","The leader gorilla, however, rendered all of that meaningless.","’At least it apologized, so it probably won’t invade my territory again.’","Still, I had no idea when another creature as powerful as the leader gorilla might appear.","That meant any structure I painstakingly built could collapse with a single flick.","And it might not stop at the structures. The entire cave could collapse just like my heart.","’Let’s give up on the door and wall. I’ll only install CCTV cameras.’","Thanks to that realization, I could abandon the idea without hesitation. I should consider myself lucky to have realized it early.","If I had finished building everything only for the leader gorilla to appear and destroy it, my despair would have been twice as great.","That didn’t mean I could simply stand by and let someone steal my possessions from right under my nose.","Losing the fasting pills would be manageable, but if someone stole the elixir, even my life would be endangered.","’Should I hide the important items underground?’","I could dig into the floor and cleverly conceal the spot beneath the tiger hide.","As an additional precaution, I should place charcoal inside for its moisture-absorbing properties.","To do that, I would need to dig through a portion of the cave’s solid floor.","’Will a pickaxe be enough?’","The cave floor contained some soil, but most of it was stone.","It would probably be difficult to excavate unless I used a hammer or pickaxe.","Besides, I couldn’t use my left arm immediately, so for now, I only intended to inspect the area.","\"This should be a decent place to hide them.\"","I found a relatively soft spot and marked it.","I could begin modifying it once I decided that my left arm had fully recovered—probably sometime after lunch.","\"Chomp! Chomp, chomp!\"","\"Good grief, Wonmo.\"","You can’t eat that many bananas. You’ll give yourself diarrhea.","Just how delicious did he find them to be that he was even eating the peels? He had already eaten four bananas by himself.","In the end, I had no choice but to hide the bananas somewhere else too. Wonmo flailed in protest, but it couldn’t be helped.","’Does that... more or less settle everything?’","It seemed I had finished organizing everything that needed attention.","I planned to start digging into the floor around lunchtime.","It was currently approximately eleven in the morning.","Since the leader gorilla had visited early in the morning, I still had plenty of time.","’I should light the oven first. Then I’ll head up to the river and check the fish trap.’","My left hand might be in a splint, but I still had work to do.","I stood up.","Then I began wondering what I should feed Namu-Ppareumbo.","He had only eaten fasting pills until now, so I had no idea what his staple diet was.","\"Namu-Ppareumbo, what do you eat? We don’t have any fasting pills left.\"","Namu-Ppareumbo raised a claw and pointed somewhere.","I turned toward the direction he indicated.","Splash! Splash!","He was pointing at the metal bucket containing the fish.","Was he saying that he ate fish?","When I looked at him questioningly, he nodded.","’Come to think of it, didn’t he try to steal my fish when we first met?’","I still remembered it vividly.","He had slowly crept toward the fish to steal one, only to be caught red-handed.","I couldn’t even describe how dumbfounded I had been at the time. Of course, in hindsight, Namu-Ppareumbo had been showing me mercy.","’Considering both the gorillas and Namu-Ppareumbo like fish...’","Was fish something like gukbap to them?","Delicious gukbap, the so-called commoner’s meal—even though it had recently become expensive enough to make that label sound ridiculous.","It seemed quite likely, since catching fish would be difficult for both the gorillas and Namu-Ppareumbo.","After all, a Golden Poison Frog was sitting right beside the water. Without a fish trap, fishing would be dangerous.","\"All right. I’ll give you fish for the time being. You eat it raw like Wonmo, right?\"","\"...\"","He nodded again.","With this, I wouldn’t have to worry about his meals for a while.","I carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and brought Wonmo along with me.","When we eventually reached the river, I found two fish caught in the trap.","’Three in the morning and two at noon. Not bad.’","I still had plenty in reserve. There should have been three or four left.","Now that I also had to account for Namu-Ppareumbo’s meals, I needed to conserve them.","If necessary, we would have to eat smoked meat instead.","’The time is gradually coming when I’ll have to earn everything for myself.’","With one unexpected incident occurring after another, it seemed my reliance on the Gallery was gradually decreasing.","No. I had only survived this long because the Gallery existed in the first place.","As I cleaned the fish, I removed the inner cores from their entrails.","Slide—","\"Hmm?\"","However, the moment I removed one of the inner cores, Namu-Ppareumbo extended his hand beside me.","The gesture made it look as though he wanted me to give it to him.","I alternated my gaze between Namu-Ppareumbo’s face and his outstretched hand before asking uncertainly,","\"You want the inner core?\"","He answered with a nod.","I was slightly dumbfounded but soon gave it some thought.","To be honest, I had an abundance of inner cores.","Every time I cleaned a fish, another inner core was added to my stockpile.","It might actually be better to give one to Namu-Ppareumbo every now and then.","\"Here. Take it.\"","\"...\"","When I handed him the round inner core, Namu-Ppareumbo immediately placed it in his mouth.","Apparently, he ate them as a substitute for fasting pills.","However, they must not have tasted as good as the fasting pills because he frowned slightly.","Even so, one should be enough for a meal. After all, it probably contained far more mana than a fasting pill.","’But he eats inner cores like ordinary food?’","That was fascinating in its own way.","Just how strong was this guy?","I continued stealing glances at Namu-Ppareumbo as I finished preparing the fish.","My left arm was slightly uncomfortable, but cleaning the fish and placing them in the oven wasn’t difficult.","’I’m glad the gorillas didn’t destroy the oven.’","Now that I had filled my stomach, it was time to circulate my inner cultivation technique.","Under normal circumstances, I would have begun consuming the inner cores today, but I postponed it because of the condition of my arm.","I would probably start eating them around the evening. The day I became stronger wasn’t far away.","’My arm... seems to have mostly healed.’","The arm into which I had injected the elixir appeared to be almost completely healed.","Of course, I had no intention of going out to explore. I planned to remain holed up at home all day.","I tapped my left arm in several places before nodding. It felt sturdier than before.","’Let’s start by digging into the cave floor.’","I needed somewhere to hide the elixir and my other valuables.","The gorillas probably wouldn’t invade again, but there was always a chance something might happen.","Since they were highly intelligent, there were bound to be a few with thieving tendencies.","I purchased a suitably sized pickaxe from the Gallery.","’When I think about it, I learned all sorts of things in the military.’","I had learned how to use both a shovel and a pickaxe during my military service.","Back then, I had grumbled about when I would ever need such skills, but now they were proving extremely useful.","Life really was unpredictable.","I let out a hollow laugh and moved into position.","’Swing it in a full circle to build centrifugal force. And instead of relying on my strength, let the weight of the pickaxe itself do the work.’","If I recklessly swung it with brute force, I would only injure my back and hands.","I had learned that lesson the hard way in the military.","Granted, the injury had allowed me to take it easy for a while, but they hadn’t shown me any mercy afterward.","Distracted by those pointless thoughts, I swung the pickaxe in a full circle.","Then I added a little force and brought it down upon my chosen spot.","Clang! Clang! Clank!","Worried that the floor might not break easily, I even infused the pickaxe with aura as I began digging.","Fortunately, the cave floor wasn’t particularly hard, so it broke apart easily.","’Since I’m putting an entire box inside, I should dig fairly deep.’","Not only did it need to be deep, but it also needed to be wide.","I might eventually have to store various supplies there in addition to my valuables.","I enthusiastically swung the pickaxe to a steady rhythm. Little by little, the floor began to give way.","Clang! Clank! Clank!","However, at some point, it stopped breaking so easily.","It seemed I had reached a different type of rock.","Still, it would eventually break if I kept at it.","With that thought, I continued patiently.","Clang!","\"No.\"","Clank!","\"Why!\"","CLAAAAANG!","\"WON’T YOU BREAK?!\"","In the end, I lost my temper and hurled the pickaxe away.","Just how hard was this rock that even an aura-infused pickaxe couldn’t break it?","Irritated, I stared at the hole, which was only about half as deep as I had intended.","A pile of loose stones surrounded it, so I cleared them away one by one with my hands.","Sparkle! Sparkle!","Once I removed the rubble, a stone with a striking green glow was revealed beneath it.","No. This was closer to an ore than an ordinary stone.","I could tell because I had seen orichalcum before.","\"What the hell is this now?\"","As if everything else weren’t enough, now I couldn’t even dig into the ground.","It felt as though God himself were deliberately screwing me over.","Setting that aside, what kind of ore was so hard that even my pickaxe couldn’t break it?","I immediately took a photograph and uploaded it to the Gallery.","Title: Does Anyone Know What This Is?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a green, glowing mineral)","I was digging into the ground to make a place to store my valuables, and this crap showed up.","What the hell is it? Is it that mithril stuff someone mentioned before?","It’s so fucking hard that my hands are killing me.","└ Passing Dwarf: Uh... I think that really is mithril.","└ Wild Grylls: ?","It was real?"]},{"title":"Chapter 115","paragraphs":["Mining (2)","There was a saying:","Try digging in the ground all day and see if you find even a single ten-won coin.","It meant that instead of dreaming about making money through pointless schemes, you should find yourself a proper job.","In reality, however, you could uncover all sorts of things by digging, and the greatest prize of all was oil.","The moment you struck oil, becoming rich was only a matter of time.","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. I think that really is mithril.","└ Wild Grylls: ?","But I didn’t need money.","I needed something immediately useful more than I needed wealth.","Even if oil had erupted from the ground, I was in a situation where a single lump of steel would have been more valuable.","Naturally, I couldn’t help feeling bewildered by the sudden appearance of mithril, which was said to be even rarer than steel.","’You find something bizarre every time you dig into the ground in this damn forest, don’t you?’","I had no idea how this place was structured.","As if having an orichalcum cave nearby weren’t enough, now mithril had appeared when I dug into the ground.","Of course, I needed to verify rigorously whether this truly was mithril.","Moreover, all kinds of theories had begun flying around the Gallery, so I needed to be cautious.","└ You’re just going to run off and get drunk again after saying that, lol.","└ Passing Dwarf: You caught me, lol.","└ What do you mean, \"caught me,\" you dwarven bastard? Lmao.","└ A race that drinks whenever they get a break, lol.","└ That’s mithril? Isn’t it too bright for mithril?","└ It isn’t even mixed with rock. It looks like a solid mass of pure mithril.","└ The entire orichalcum cave was made of orichalcum, so it isn’t impossible.","└ Be precise. It would be impossible anywhere outside the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ Ah, I think I understand. Just as all the animals grew larger, the minerals must have grown too! That’s why it looks like that even before being refined!","└ That sounds pretty convincing. Then why are the gorillas normal-sized?","└ Dunno.","└ Passing Dwarf: Whatever. Break off a small piece and send it to me. I’ll examine it for you.","One comment among the countless replies caught my attention.","Was this truly mithril in its natural, unrefined state?","Not only mithril, but most minerals were found mixed with rock.","Pure substances were obtained by placing the ore inside a furnace and processing it through a method known as smelting.","What I had discovered, however, appeared to be a pure material that required no smelting whatsoever. That was why it was difficult to believe.","There were exceptions, such as diamonds, but mithril was not normally one of them.","’Everyone seems willing to accept it because I’ve already discovered an orichalcum cave, though.’","Orichalcum was originally a mineral as well. Nevertheless, I had discovered a cave made entirely of orichalcum.","There was no reason mithril couldn’t be the same.","The only problem was that this one happened to be beneath my home.","Either way, I needed to give at least a small piece to the dwarf.","I stared at the green-glowing mithril.","’A guardian isn’t suddenly going to rise out of the ground, is it?’","If that happened, the entire cave—including the floor—would collapse.","My heart would collapse along with it.","Unlike the orichalcum cave, however, there wasn’t any empty space beneath this ore.","Moreover, there was an even greater problem.","’Why won’t this damn thing break?’","Mining it was incredibly difficult.","No matter how many times I struck it with the pickaxe, I couldn’t leave even a single scratch.","If I remembered correctly, mithril was supposed to possess strength similar to steel while being far lighter.","It might have been different if it were mixed with ordinary rock, but most mithril was notoriously difficult to mine.","Clang! Clang! Clank!","Still, what else could I do?","I had no choice but to keep mining.","They said no tree could withstand ten swings of an axe, and mithril should be no different.","More importantly, I had aura.","I continued mining while infusing the pickaxe with aura.","Clang! Scrape!","After some time, I finally managed to extract a tiny piece of mithril.","I had been mining for so long that sweat streamed down my body.","’I only extracted a little, but the pickaxe is already almost completely blunt.’","Even though I had used aura, I couldn’t prevent the pickaxe from being damaged.","Aura might enhance a tool’s performance, but it wasn’t omnipotent.","Using aura didn’t increase the durability of the weapon itself.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword was sturdy only because it had been forged from something called Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron.","I examined the thumb-sized piece of green ore before accessing the Gallery.","If possible, I also wanted to get a high-quality pickaxe from the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls: I managed to mine this, so please examine it for me.]","[Passing Dwarf: Okay.]","[Wild Grylls: If you say you’re going drinking again, I’m never giving you anything else.]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s too harsh;; Fine, I understand. It’s easy to examine, so I’ll let you know soon.]","Since the dwarf said he would post his findings, I inspected the remaining mithril ore.","I wasn’t sure whether I should even call it ore, but for now, that was what I would call it.","Unlike orichalcum, mithril could be fashioned into weapons and all kinds of equipment.","It would undoubtedly be of immense help to me.","Before that, however, there was something I needed to do.","’I should give some to the Heavenly Demon and PraiseTheSun.’","If this truly was mithril, there were two people I wanted to repay immediately.","The Heavenly Demon had given me an absurdly overpowered weapon, while PraiseTheSun had continuously provided me with shields.","I had believed that even a fully mature Mandrake wouldn’t be enough to repay their kindness.","’And I broke the shield PraiseTheSun gave me.’","Like orichalcum, mithril was a mineral that was difficult to obtain even with money.","Wouldn’t PraiseTheSun, who loved rare things, be delighted to receive it?","’First, I should determine how far this deposit extends.’","If the entire cave floor was made of mithril, that would create its own set of problems.","I couldn’t simply leave the mithril untouched, but I couldn’t destroy the entire cave floor either.","After considering the matter, I decided to proceed with my original plan.","I still needed a hidden storage space, so I could simply continue digging in the same spot.","’Even this much is enormous.’","I wasn’t asking for an entire suit of armor.","I only needed some spare tools.","I vigorously swung the pickaxe to create the storage space.","’Damn it. Should I just ask him to make me a mithril pickaxe?’","After five minutes of mining, I was already sick of it.","I wiped away the sweat and accessed the Gallery.","The dwarf should have finished examining it by now.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hey, hey! Read this quickly. It’s urgent.]","[Passing Dwarf: You’re always gone at times like this, damn it. This is really fucking urgent, so hurry up and read this.]","The moment I entered the Gallery, I saw the dwarf’s messages, which sounded rather urgent.","They had arrived only a minute ago.","I stared at them in confusion.","’Is it a different mineral rather than mithril?’","This was the same dwarf who had drunkenly responded far too late with, \"Yeah, that’s orichalcum.\"","It was strange for someone like him to send messages in such a frantic manner.","[Wild Grylls: Yeah;; Why are you in such a hurry?]","[Passing Dwarf: This really is mithril. But it’s completely different from what I expected.]","[Wild Grylls: What’s different about it?]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s practically a solid mass of pure mithril that barely needs any refining;;]","A solid mass?","I tilted my head when I read that. Wasn’t that a good thing?","[Wild Grylls: What’s wrong? Is it not mithril? Or are you upset because you can’t go drinking?]","[Passing Dwarf: I’m being serious, so stop making jokes about alcohol.]","[Wild Grylls: Isn’t this good? It means we can skip all the annoying steps.]","[Passing Dwarf: Do you have absolutely no idea what you’ve discovered?]","[Wild Grylls: Nope. No idea whatsoever. Isn’t it just something good?]","[Passing Dwarf: Good grief. Fuck, is your head an anvil or did someone smash it with a hammer?;;]","[Wild Grylls: Stop insulting me and explain. I came from another world, so I don’t know any of this.]","[Passing Dwarf: Fine. I’ll explain it while assuming your head really is an anvil.]","Passing Dwarf’s explanation went as follows.","Minerals were ordinarily found inside rock, and their purity could be increased through the refining process.","The same applied to mithril.","Moreover, mithril occurred less frequently and in smaller quantities than other ores, so its higher value was unavoidable.","Even if what I had discovered had been ordinary mithril ore, the sheer size of the deposit would already have been absurd.","[Wild Grylls: Are you worried you’ll get caught browsing the Gallery?]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s a separate issue. This is going to make my real life a huuuuge pain in the ass.]","If he needed permission from his superiors, mithril must ordinarily require a fairly complicated refining process.","Well, it was supposed to be a rare mineral, so that much made sense.","Fortunately, mine was a solid mass of mithril, so simply melting it would be enough.","[Passing Dwarf: The so-called mithril weapons out there are actually all alloys. There isn’t a single tool in the world made entirely from pure mithril. Not even the wealthiest people in Setan could do something like that.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. But you’re saying I can?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. If it had been ordinary ore, I was going to send it back.]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Why? Didn’t you say you were a dwarf?]","[Passing Dwarf: I am a dwarf, but ordinary mithril has to undergo a special refining process. The furnace required for it can only be used with permission from the higher-ups.]","[Passing Dwarf: How did you mine this? More importantly, are you sure you actually mined it? Considering mithril’s hardness, I could only understand this if you said you found a loose piece lying around.]","[Wild Grylls: What are you talking about? It was hard, but it broke apart like stone.]","[Passing Dwarf: What are you talking about? The piece you gave me is a solid mass. Solid mithril. It’s basically a lump of metal.]","What was this guy talking about now?","I furrowed my brow.","The mithril vein was certainly hard, but based on my experience, it definitely wasn’t as tough as metal.","If it had been, I wouldn’t have been able to mine it with a pickaxe at all.","It was rock that could be broken with enough effort.","That was the mithril I was currently mining.","[Wild Grylls: That’s strange. I mined it just like ordinary stone. Isn’t that normal?]","[Passing Dwarf: Don’t talk nonsense. You’d have trouble cutting it even with a saw, so how could you possibly—;;]","[Wild Grylls: No, I’m serious;; I’ll record a video and show you. Before that, give me a pickaxe.]","[Passing Dwarf: I have no idea what kind of nonsense you’re spouting, but fine. I’ll give you one. I made it as a spare for myself, so it should be good.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh, and make me a mithril pickaxe. Digging this stuff is difficult.]","[Passing Dwarf: Holy shit, lol. The first pure-mithril tool in the world is going to be a pickaxe? Lmao.]","[Wild Grylls: I’m serious. It’ll make mining easier, won’t it?]","[Passing Dwarf: It would make things slightly easier, but the difference wouldn’t be dramatic;;]","Reality really was different from a game.","In games, tools made from the same material made mining that material far easier.","Still, I had an abundance of mithril, so there was no harm in owning one mithril pickaxe.","Even if the visible deposit was all there was, it wouldn’t be a problem. A pickaxe could be used anywhere.","’Will this help me mine it more easily?’","I examined the pickaxe I had received from the dwarf.","At a glance, it looked like an ordinary pickaxe.","However, its handle was slightly short. It had probably been made according to dwarven proportions.","Clang! Clank!","Even so, it performed far better than my previous pickaxe.","It had a satisfying weight and excellent durability. Thanks to it, I managed to mine a considerable amount of mithril.","Eventually, I turned a fist-sized chunk of mithril over in my hands and frowned in confusion.","’This is strange. It definitely feels more like stone.’","Not only was its texture stone-like, but it also lacked the distinctive solidity of metal.","I tilted my head before sending the mithril to the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls: (Video of me mining mithril) Look. It breaks apart like stone.]","[Passing Dwarf: That should be impossible. What the hell is going on? The piece you gave me is a lump of metal;;]","[Wild Grylls: You’re actually good at this, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: Hey, no matter what, don’t insult my pride like that. I might not look it, but I’m a master metallurgist.]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry. I apologize. Anyway, I showed you the evidence.]","[Passing Dwarf: Fuck, lol. I feel like everything I know is falling apart. Don’t you sense anything strange about it?]","I was just about to answer, Not at all.","Slide—","A fragment of mithril lying on the ground moved slightly.","’...What?’","For a moment, I thought my eyes had deceived me.","But then an astonishing scene unfolded, immediately proving otherwise.","Slide—scrape—","The mithril fragments scattered around during the mining process began moving little by little.","Where were they going?","Toward the mithril vein, which continued to shine brilliantly.","I left the Gallery window open and stared blankly at the sight.","Tap—","Before long, the fragments merged with the mithril vein.","They became one again as though they had never broken away.","I witnessed the entire process clearly with my own two eyes.","It looked almost as though the vein were forcibly gathering up pieces of its severed flesh.","’...No way.’","Half doubtful, I placed my hand upon the mithril vein.","There was something I needed to test.","The first rule of auctions and private trades: living creatures could not be traded.","The second rule: to trade an object, every side of that object had to be visible.","There was no need to concern myself with the rules after that. They weren’t particularly important.","The reason I specifically recalled the first and second rules was simple.","’You have to pass the first rule before the second rule is applied.’","That was how the system’s algorithm worked.","If something failed to pass the first rule, trading it was impossible from the outset.","If it weren’t, I wouldn’t still be trapped here. The first rule couldn’t be circumvented through tricks.","In other words—","[Living creatures cannot be traded.]","This proved that the mithril vein was alive like a living creature.","In this insane forest, even the minerals were alive and breathing."]},{"title":"Chapter 116","paragraphs":["Mining (3)","What was life?","It was a remarkably profound question.","A being promised death at the very moment it was granted life.","A being that raced toward death and therefore struggled to leave behind biological or spiritual descendants of its own.","A subject worthy of deep philosophical and scientific study, as well as a creation of God.","Life itself was the very embodiment of mystery.","That raised another question: What standards distinguished living things from nonliving things?","Scholars had established various criteria for defining life, but those criteria were ultimately subjective.","Distinguishing life in a completely objective sense was practically impossible.","The Gallery system was probably no different. Its creator’s subjective views must have been reflected in it.","The problem was that I had been able to trade other objects without difficulty until now.","Before my eyes lay mithril, displaying its brilliant splendor.","For some unknown reason, the Gallery had classified this mithril as a living creature.","I stared at the mithril and sank into thought.","A single question filled my mind.","’Why?’","Minerals detached from the vein could be traded.","However, the entire vein couldn’t be traded because it had been classified as a living creature.","’Does it have a core inside it like the guardian?’","If so, this was dangerous.","It meant the mithril vein might become active like the guardian.","I couldn’t be certain because it was buried underground, but I couldn’t help feeling uneasy.","The Gallery had classified it as a living creature, so I needed to exercise caution.","’Considering it stayed still even after I hit it so many times...’","The guardian had reacted the moment I used mana.","This thing, however, hadn’t responded even when I struck it with mana-infused attacks.","What kind of ecology did this vein possess?","It was difficult to understand.","In the end, all I knew was that the vein was alive.","What if it didn’t assume a definite form like the guardian and instead remained amorphous like a slime from some game?","What if one day, while I was sleeping, it suddenly sprouted upward in the shape of spikes?","What would happen then?","I would suffer a critical injury at the very least.","The human body was fragile.","The moment one of those spikes pierced my head, I would bid farewell to this world.","As long as such a danger existed, I couldn’t ignore a living mineral vein beneath my home.","’Should I ask the dwarf first?’","A living mineral vein.","The dwarf was the only person I could ask about something like this.","If even he didn’t know, I planned to post a question in the Gallery.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. Emergency. Emergency. Let me ask you something.]","[Passing Dwarf: What is it?]","[Wild Grylls: Are there such things as living... mineral veins?]","[Passing Dwarf: What kind of nonsense is that? What score did you get in language class at school?]","[Wild Grylls: My parents died, so I focused more on working than school. I barely met the attendance requirements.]","[Passing Dwarf: Ah, fuck. If you say it like that, you make me sound like an asshole;;]","[Wild Grylls: Then be serious and answer me.]","[Passing Dwarf: What do you mean, a mineral is alive? Are you talking about the mithril?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. After hearing what you said, I observed it for a while. The fragments lying nearby wriggled around before reattaching themselves to the vein. I tried trading the vein just in case, but all I got was a notification saying living creatures couldn’t be traded.]","[Passing Dwarf: I don’t know. Just ask the Gallery. I can tell you aren’t talking nonsense, but I honestly have no idea, lol.]","Even the dwarf, an expert, gave up trying to understand it.","In the end, I decided to ask the Gallery.","Surely someone would know.","Just in case, I recorded the entire process. I also broke off a few fragments.","This was possible because I could take photographs and videos of the Gallery window itself.","Title: Can Minerals Be Alive?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the mithril vein)","(Video showing the notification that appeared when I tried trading the mithril)","(Video of the fragments wriggling toward the vein and reattaching themselves)","It’s exactly as shown in the videos. Passing Dwarf identified it as mithril.","But he said mithril isn’t supposed to be alive.","Has anyone ever seen anything like this?","What the hell is it, and why is this happening?","└ Heavenly Demon: It crawls like an earthworm. It appears to be struggling to survive.","└ SwordMaster: Doesn’t it look like it’s trying to increase the size of its body?","└ What the fuck am I looking at?","└ I never thought I’d live to see mithril fragments crawling like earthworms;;","└ Even for the Forest of Four Seasons, does this make any sense?","└ Could there be some kind of core embedded inside it?","└ Forget that. Grylls, give me some mithril. I’ll put it to good use.","└ Come to think of it, that really was mithril, lol.","└ Everyone was so shocked that they focused on the video instead of the mithril, lol.","└ This bastard assessed the situation quickly, lol.","└ Allfather: The Gallery classified it as a living creature... That is effectively the same as saying the mineral possesses an ego.","└ Wild Grylls: An ego?","└ Allfather: Yes. The Gallery appears to prohibit the trading of anything it determines possesses an ego. That is the conclusion I reached through many years of research.","└ Then are you saying plants don’t have egos? Medicinal herbs and trees can be traded just fine.","└ Allfather: Possessing an ego means being capable of thought. It means learning through thought and developing even further.","└ You sound like one of those people who claims cancer is alive. Why doesn’t cancer count?","└ Allfather: Who told you that?","└ I read it in an old book.","└ Allfather: It seems you’re the one without an ego. Judging by how you refuse to think for yourself and entrust your sense of self to others, that is. Would you care to entrust that head of yours to me through a trade? As it happens, I have a friend for it.","└ Allfather: In any case, it isn’t completely unheard of for an inanimate object to develop an ego. Have you ever heard of an ego weapon? It is a weapon that possesses a consciousness of its own.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Ah! I know about those too! The Hero’s Holy Sword is also a weapon with an ego!","└ Allfather: An excellent example. However, even I have never seen an unprocessed mineral possess an ego... You should exercise caution. It may give birth to a guardian.","└ A mithril guardian? That’s fucking insane, lol.","└ Would he even be able to defeat it?","└ Mithril alone is already difficult enough. If a guardian emerges, Grylls will probably just die.","└ That’s genuinely horrifying;;","└ Wild Grylls: Then there must be a specific part responsible for the mithril’s ego, right?","└ Allfather: That is most likely the case.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: In the Holy Sword’s case, it’s the jewel embedded in the center of its hilt!","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t ask you.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: Okay...!","└ Wild Grylls: I’m sorry. I’m anxious, so I spoke too harshly.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero: It’s all right! I’ve been called much worse! Someone even called me a fucking bitch before!","└ Wild Grylls: ;;","└ Wild Grylls: Anyway, you’re saying this mineral vein possesses an ego, correct? An ego capable of thinking and making decisions for itself.","I suddenly felt sorry for the head moderator, but I decided to move on.","Such were the hardships of being a moderator.","I stared at the mithril vein, which was presumed to possess an ego.","How was I supposed to make this thing move?","I was afraid that an accident might occur if I continued mining.","\"Ahem. Hello, my friend?\"","\"...?\"","\"If you can hear me, could you move your body out of the way?\"","So I made the suggestion as politely as possible.","It might have made me look like an idiot, but I was completely serious.","Of course, the mineral vein didn’t move.","It didn’t have ears, after all. Not every living creature had them.","Would a jellyfish listen if you spoke to it in a human language?","Absolutely not.","\"Haa... This won’t do.\"","I couldn’t leave it like this.","I made a decision for the greater good.","Even if I had to tear apart the entire rear section of the cave, I would mine out all the mithril.","I would rather defuse the bomb myself than sleep with it beneath me.","’If neither of us had ever become aware of the other, it probably would’ve remained still.’","Ignorance was bliss.","It felt as though I had unnecessarily awakened something that had been sleeping.","Still, what else could I do?","It had already happened.","As a precaution, I placed Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and began mining.","Crack! Thud!","Instead of mining the mithril directly, I carefully chipped away at the rock surrounding it.","I needed to see just how large this mithril deposit was.","Fortunately, it seemed to exist only inside the cave.","’Games really are completely different from reality.’","In a certain blocky world, you could dig all the way down to lava with nothing more than an iron pickaxe.","It seemed only superhumans could become protagonists.","I was merely an ordinary human dropped into the Forest of Four Seasons by some god’s prank.","I felt like sighing, but mining took priority.","Crack! Thud!","How much time had passed?","Once I had dug down to a depth roughly equal to my height, the vein’s overall shape gradually began to emerge.","\"Oh, for fuck’s sake. Seriously?\"","I took it back.","What I had seen was merely the tip of the iceberg.","No matter how much I dug, I couldn’t find the end.","Just how far did this vein extend?","It was impossible to estimate.","’This is driving me insane.’","At this rate, I would have to tear apart not only the rear section but the entire cave.","Still, I needed to sleep inside the cave.","More than anything, I wanted to rest.","With a troubled heart, I stared at the glittering mithril vein.","’Was it Gyeongju? I heard people find artifacts just by digging in their yards there.’","Meanwhile, finding mithril had given me nothing but a headache.","Worse still, this was a mineral that might eventually produce a guardian.","An orichalcum guardian was horrifying enough, but a mithril guardian?","’I don’t have a choice. I’ll have to mine all of it.’","I changed my plan.","I would mine the mithril and locate the source of its life.","I didn’t know whether it would truly become a guardian, but I couldn’t ignore the worst-case scenario.","Clang! Clank! Clank!","And so I continued mining diligently.","My hands gradually began to go numb, but I endured it.","If I failed to eliminate this thing, my life might be in danger.","It was mining with my life on the line.","Fortunately, I had the pickaxe the dwarf had given me.","I stored the detached mithril fragments and chunks inside my spatial bag.","\"Huff... Haa...\"","After swinging the pickaxe for an hour, I was the first to give out.","Meanwhile, the mithril vein continued displaying its unyielding form.","Strangely, it seemed to grow harder the more I struck it.","More precisely, it became tougher the deeper I dug.","’I’ll have to make sure the dwarf crafts that mithril pickaxe for me.’","Either that, or I needed to complete my Aura Blade.","Unfortunately, I wasn’t making any progress with it.","Still, I had to do as much as I possibly could.","Didn’t they say that small gains eventually accumulated into a mountain?","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, I’ll give you a lump of mithril, so please have a weapon made from it. Consider it repayment for the sword you gave me.]","[Heavenly Demon: There is no need for this. Your kindness may well be your greatest weakness.]","[Wild Grylls: The sword you gave me has saved my life several times. Without it, I would’ve died long ago. So please accept this.]","[Heavenly Demon: Refusing would also be discourteous. I shall accept it with gratitude.]","I used my break to give the Heavenly Demon a lump of mithril.","[Wild Grylls: Mithril isn’t some trivial trinket, so you’ll accept it, right?]","[PraiseTheSun: Not even the king of a nation could call mithril a trivial trinket;;]","[Wild Grylls: Then please accept it. It’s repayment for all the shields you’ve given me.]","[PraiseTheSun: You already gave me a fully mature Mandrake. I thought that was more than enough.]","[Wild Grylls: So you don’t want it?]","[PraiseTheSun: No one dislikes free gifts. Thanks. I’ll use it to make an accessory.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","I also gave a lump of mithril to PraiseTheSun, who had gifted me the shields.","Afterward, I resumed mining.","It was an endless battle.","However, even by evening, I had failed to extract all of it.","’I’ll have no choice but to sleep as far away from it as possible.’","My hands were numb after swinging a pickaxe all day.","I massaged my tingling palms and accessed the Gallery.","There were approximately thirty minutes left until dinner, so I planned to browse the Gallery until then.","’The dwarf sent me a message.’","I had given the dwarf more mithril whenever I extracted some.","I had also repeatedly insisted that he make me a pure-mithril pickaxe.","Since he had messaged me, I assumed he had either completed it or was currently crafting it.","[Passing Dwarf: Hey. We’re fucked.]","However, the message I received was nothing like what I had expected.","It was short and concise, yet perfectly summarized the situation he was facing.","Instead of feeling anxious, I was confused and immediately replied.","[Wild Grylls: What happened?]","[Passing Dwarf: The mithril won’t melt.]","[Wild Grylls: ? What are you talking about?]","[Passing Dwarf: No matter what I do, it won’t melt, so I can’t pour it into a mold. I can’t even break it.]","The dwarf then continued.","[Passing Dwarf: I examined it and found that it contains an excessive amount of mana. I’d need a specially constructed furnace to melt it. So I think I’ll have to send it back.]","[Wild Grylls: You aren’t saying I’ll have to melt it and make the equipment myself, are you?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. That’s exactly what I’m saying.]","[Wild Grylls: F—]","[Passing Dwarf: Still, anything made from it will be insanely powerful, lol.]","In other words, my workload had increased yet again."]},{"title":"Chapter 117","paragraphs":["Mining (4)","One obstacle after another. That was the perfect way to describe how I felt right now.","After all the trouble I had gone through to mine the mithril, even the dwarf told me he couldn’t melt it.","The moment I heard that, a crushing sense of futility washed over me, but I barely managed to pull myself together.","I had no idea what was so special about this damned mithril, but I needed an explanation.","[Wild Grylls: Explain it in detail. Is it really just because it contains so much mana?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. It’s difficult to melt, and even if you do melt it, an ordinary furnace can’t withstand it.]","[Wild Grylls: Explain why. I don’t think I’ll be convinced otherwise. It’s not that I don’t trust you. It’s just the situation.]","[Passing Dwarf: I get what you mean. Most ordinary metals...]","I carefully read the dwarf’s explanation.","Most metals were buried underground, so they naturally absorbed mana from the earth.","Ordinary soil didn’t contain much mana, so there was no issue with putting metals mined from it into a furnace.","However, the deeper one dug—or in places like the Forest of Four Seasons, where the earth contained an abnormally high amount of mana—the situation was different.","Minerals mined from such places generally contained highly concentrated mana, so a special furnace was required.","He explained that using an ordinary furnace instead of a special one could cause an explosion.","[Passing Dwarf: It’s basically just a furnace that consumes an absurd amount of mana.]","[Wild Grylls: Can’t an individual own one?]","[Passing Dwarf: The furnace is bigger than an entire mansion, you human ;; It’s not something we use often in the first place, so the state manages it directly.]","[Wild Grylls: What kind of ridiculous inefficiency is that?]","[Passing Dwarf: Do you think our dwarven technology is a joke? Do you have any idea how cutting-edge that thing is?]","[Wild Grylls: A cutting-edge joke.]","[Passing Dwarf: Anything becomes a bomb if you forcibly compress it into a confined space and then let it burst. Naturally, the mithril gets blown away too.]","[Wild Grylls: What the hell is the special furnace made of, then?]","So there was nothing I could do about it. All I could do was sigh.","Building an ordinary furnace would already be enough to drive me insane, but now I needed a special furnace?","He had even said it was much bigger than an entire mansion, so constructing one was completely out of the question.","At this rate, the mithril I had worked so hard to mine would become a useless burden.","I needed to find some way to use it, but nothing came to mind.","[Passing Dwarf: Why don’t you try making something yourself? Since you’re in the Forest of Four Seasons, it should be no different from ordinary metal there.]","[Wild Grylls: Didn’t you say it could only be melted in a special furnace?]","[Passing Dwarf: That place is already overflowing with mana. So just give it a try.]","[Wild Grylls: I don’t know how to build a furnace.]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s a solid chunk of mithril, so just heat it in a forge and hammer it into shape. If you want to use a mold, build a furnace, melt the mithril, and pour it in.]","[Wild Grylls: Isn’t that contradictory? You just said I needed a special furnace.]","[Passing Dwarf: Is your brain actually an anvil? It explodes because the mana escapes when the material changes state. I was going to cast it because I wanted to finish quickly, but I noticed in time. If I’d realized any later or started hammering it, I’d be in the hospital right now.]","[Wild Grylls: Aha. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: This is seriously upsetting. I only tried to finish it quickly because I felt bad for you, yet you don’t appreciate my sincerity at all...]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry ;; Is there anything you want?]","[Passing Dwarf: Just give me one crab shell, hehe.]","[Wild Grylls: Damn it ;; Fine.]","He had taught me something valuable, so I was perfectly willing to give him one crab.","I ended my conversation with the dwarf and contacted the registered users to whom I had given mithril.","It was necessary, if only to prevent an unexpected accident.","[Heavenly Demon: Dost thou mean true silver? This lady still possesses it.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s a relief. Apparently, it might explode if you try to make equipment with it. Could you return it to me?]","[Heavenly Demon: Is it because true silver contains an immense amount of qi?]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? How did you know?]","[Heavenly Demon: It was simple. This lady wished to absorb it, but feared it might lose its essence, so I chose to wait.]","[Wild Grylls: If you return it, I’ll forge a sword for you myself.]","[Heavenly Demon: May this lady look forward to it?]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm... No? It might take a long time.]","[Heavenly Demon: I appreciate thy honesty. This lady shall wait without expecting too much. It matters not what weapon this lady uses.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Allfather: So you can’t even work it, let alone hammer it?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll ask.]","[Wild Grylls: He says engraving and cutting are fine.]","[Allfather: Then I’ll keep mine. I’m going to use it as a ring.]","[Wild Grylls: Be careful anyway.]","I received the mithril I had given to the Heavenly Demon.","Allfather decided to keep his.","When I asked the dwarf, he explained that there was only a risk of explosion when the material changed states.","There was no problem with carving it down while keeping it in the same state.","’Come to think of it, if that weren’t the case, carrying it around would be no different from carrying a bomb.’","Even if heat caused it to change shape, there was no need to worry. Why?","Because if it was hot enough to deform metal, a person would have died long before that became an issue.","After gathering all sorts of information, I closed the gallery.","’Thankfully, I don’t have to do everything myself.’","According to the dwarf, he could sharpen the blade for me.","He said all I needed to do was flatten the mithril into shape.","If that proved too difficult, I could obtain a mold and simply pour molten mithril into it.","’The downside is that I’d have to build a furnace.’","Besides, an ordinary mold might not withstand the temperature of molten metal.","In the worst case, even the furnace I had worked so hard to build could melt.","Each option had clear advantages and disadvantages, so I couldn’t help agonizing over the decision.","’Let’s eat first.’","Whatever happened, food was important. I could continue worrying about the mithril tomorrow.","When I went up to the river, I found two fish caught in the trap. Satisfactory.","I was about to clean them as usual when a thought occurred to me, and I stopped.","’Should I try cutting one with mithril?’","There were several mithril fragments that had broken off while I was mining. Some of them had sharp edges.","Just how sharp was mithril?","With that expectation in mind, I sliced open the fish’s belly.","Sliiice.","It felt similar to using a dagger.","That was all.","Although the edge hadn’t been sharpened, I couldn’t help feeling slightly disappointed.","’Would it be different if I used aura?’","So I channeled aura into it, and to my surprise...","Even though I used only a small amount of mana, the aura blazed like fire.","It was possible that I had simply grown stronger, so I channeled aura into my dagger as well, but there was a clear difference.","To make sure, I tried using aura with several other tools, but the result was the same.","Compared to the mithril, I had to pour far more mana into them before the aura displayed its full power.","’So that’s what it was.’","Its mana efficiency was incredible.","That alone explained everything.","This seemed to be what the dwarf had meant when he said its performance would be exceptional.","I could be certain precisely because it was mithril, not orichalcum.","’This will be a huge help in prolonged battles.’","Aside from my fight against the Orichalcum Guardian, I had never run out of mana before.","However, mana—or rather, aura itself—was an extremely inefficient technique to begin with.","It might be different if it took a defined shape like an Aura Blade, but mine burned like flames. Anyone could see how inefficient that was.","Perhaps this mithril could be even more efficient than the Heavenly Demon’s sword. It might even accelerate my training.","’So it isn’t completely useless.’","For someone like me, whose survival was paramount, efficiency was an important consideration.","This mithril drastically improved that efficiency, making it practically indispensable.","I would have to use it to make various tools.","Its performance was comparable to steel, yet it was much lighter. It was perfect.","’Mining it is still a problem, though.’","There was nothing I could do about that. I would simply have to work my aaaass off.","I finished dinner and cleaned everything up before going to bed.","I planned to leave the section I had dug out as it was and continue mining tomorrow.","’As for the elixir... I’ll keep it above my head.’","A thief might sneak in during the night and steal something.","Namu-Ppareumbo would probably wake up and stop them, but it was better to be prepared.","Once I had finished setting everything up, I logged into the gallery.","I didn’t have anything in particular to say. I was simply curious whether anything had happened.","’Tomorrow will mark exactly half a month.’","A lot had happened over the past fifteen days. Today, the leader ape had beaten the living daylights out of me.","Tomorrow, I planned to retrieve the orichalcum from the Orichalcum Cave and receive the crystal orb that would serve as a security camera.","While I was at it, I would also work on building a furnace. I could ask the dwarf about its structure.","’I have so much to do.’","Every time I finished one task, two more appeared. Whenever I finished those two, five more took their place.","Mithril, in particular, could only be processed within the Forest of Four Seasons.","With complicated feelings, I browsed through the gallery. I needed something to help me unwind.","[Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.]","While browsing the gallery, a particular title caught my eye.","At first, I thought it was an ordinary clickbait post, but then I realized it had been posted by a registered user.","’Who is that?’","I’ll Become a Duke. The username seemed vaguely familiar.","Curious, I opened the post.","Title: Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.","I’ll Become a Duke","(A photograph of a finely crafted pair of leather shoes)","(A photograph of the leather shoes remaining undamaged after water was poured over them)","(A photograph showing that the shoes could not easily be cut with a knife)","They were photographs of shoes.","Come to think of it, I had completely forgotten.","I had promised to give a mature Mandrake to anyone who provided me with a good pair of shoes.","The moment I made that offer, several people uploaded photographs of shoes, but I disliked most of them.","One of them had even tried to scam me, so I gave him a casual middle finger and left it at that.","Furthermore, the competition had died down after the dwarf—or rather, the dwarf’s friend—gave me a pair of shoes.","Everyone said that no matter how hard they tried, their efforts would be meaningless before the craftsmanship of a dwarven artisan.","I also liked the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend, so I had stopped paying attention to the matter.","’But this person...’","This registered user was different. Despite all the time that had passed, he had continued working on them.","Of course, if all he had to show for his efforts was a poor result, I would have ignored him.","└ There isn’t even a single scream, so they really must be sturdy, hahahaha.","└ Maybe he’s gritting his teeth and enduring it in silence, hahaha.","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A photograph revealing his masked face) I knew you would say that, so I filmed this too. I recorded it with a crystal orb.","└ Damn, look at how thorough he is, hahahaha.","└ What’s with the mask? It looks like something you’d wear to a ball. Is he a noble?","└ Who’s the person hitting him with the sledgehammer?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: My son.","└ Hahahahahahahahaha!","└ What a devoted son, damn, hahahahaha!","└ Even if he’s your son, he’s hitting you way too hard, hahahaha!","(A video of someone repeatedly striking the shoe wearer’s foot with a sledgehammer)","└ S-Sir ;; Y-You can stop now ;;","└ How many times is he going to hit him? Damn, hahahaha!","└ At this rate, his foot is going to be completely crushed ;;","If only that video hadn’t been there.","No matter how durable the shoes were, who would strike them with a sledgehammer while someone was still wearing them?","Then again, that made him even more trustworthy. Hadn’t he risked his own body to prove the quality of his product?","After staring at it in discomfort for a moment, I hurriedly left a comment before he injured himself any further.","There were no issues with the shoes’ performance, so I could safely proceed with the trade.","└ Wild Grylls: S-Sir, you don’t have to do that. You aren’t injured, are you?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A video of him removing his foot from the shoe after the sledgehammer test) Correct.","└ Wow. He’s thorough as hell. Now that’s proper product verification ;;","└ Who made those? I want a pair.","└ I’ll buy them!","└ Buy me a pair too!","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. You win. I think those are better than the pair my friend made ;;","└ The dwarf has declared defeat!","└ If even a dwarf admits defeat, they must be the real deal, hahaha.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll buy them. It’s already late, though. Can we make the exchange tomorrow?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: That is possible.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a private message.","I sent him a message because it seemed we needed to discuss the matter privately.","Despite his stiff way of speaking, he was passionate. I found myself liking him.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, I’ll Become a Duke. I saw the shoes. You need a mature Mandrake, correct?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: You don’t need anything else?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: I do not. I urgently need a mature Mandrake.]","He urgently needed a mature Mandrake. I could sense the desperation in his words.","Someone close to him was probably suffering from an illness.","Otherwise, he would have no reason to reject everything else and insist solely on the mature Mandrake.","’He seems trustworthy.’","Both the video and his messages suggested that he was someone I could trust.","After telling him I would send the mature Mandrake tomorrow, I closed the gallery window.","Tomorrow would be my fifteenth day—exactly half a month—and I also planned to consume the inner core.","Building the furnace and completing my trade with I’ll Become a Duke...","I had plenty to do.","’The Guardian won’t wake up while I’m asleep, will it?’","Fortunately, nothing like that happened.","\"Ah. What the hell? What is this now?\"","Except that the entire section I had worked so hard to mine had completely regenerated.","I didn’t want an unlimited supply, but it looked like I was going to be forced to enjoy one.","’Is it a planarian or something?’","Planarian mithril.","I had no idea what kind of horrifying hybrid this was.","This seemed to be what the dwarf meant when he said that its performance, at least, would be excellent.","I could be sure of that because it was mithril, not orichalcum.","’This will be a great help in prolonged battles.’","Aside from my battle against the Orichalcum Guardian, I had never run out of mana before.","However, mana—or rather, aura—was an extremely inefficient technique to begin with.","It might be different if it took on a defined shape like an Aura Blade, but mine burned like flames. Anyone could tell at a glance how inefficient it was.","It might even be more efficient than the Heavenly Demon’s sword. It could also help accelerate my training.","’So it isn’t completely useless.’","For someone like me, whose survival was paramount, efficiency was an important consideration.","This mithril drastically increased that efficiency, making it practically indispensable.","I would have to use it to make various tools.","It performed about as well as steel while being much lighter, making it perfect for the job.","’Mining it is still a problem, though.’","There was nothing I could do about that. I would just have to work haaaarder.","I finished dinner, then cleaned everything up before going to bed.","I planned to leave the rear section of the hole as it was and continue digging tomorrow.","’As for the elixir... I’ll keep it above my head.’","A thief might sneak in during the night and steal something.","Namu-Ppareumbo would probably wake up and stop them, but it was better to be prepared just in case.","Once I had finished setting everything up, I logged into the gallery.","I didn’t have anything in particular to say. I was simply curious whether anything had happened.","’Tomorrow will mark exactly half a month.’","A lot had happened over the past fifteen days. Today, the leader ape had beaten the living daylights out of me.","Tomorrow, I planned to retrieve the orichalcum from the Orichalcum Cave and receive the crystal orb that would serve as a security camera.","While I was at it, I should also work on building a furnace. I could ask the dwarf about its structure.","’I have so much to do.’","Whenever I finished one task, two more appeared. Whenever I finished those two, another five appeared.","Mithril, in particular, could only be processed within the Forest of Four Seasons.","With mixed feelings, I browsed through the gallery. I needed something to help me unwind.","[Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.]","As I browsed the gallery, one particular title caught my eye.","At first, I thought it was ordinary clickbait, but then I realized it had been posted by a registered user.","’Who is that?’","I’ll Become a Duke. The username seemed vaguely familiar.","Curious, I opened the post.","Title: Wild Grylls, your shoes are finished.","I’ll Become a Duke","(A photograph of a finely crafted pair of leather shoes)","(A photograph of the leather shoes remaining undamaged after water was poured over them)","(A photograph showing that the shoes could not easily be cut with a knife)","They were photographs of shoes.","Come to think of it, I had completely forgotten.","I had promised to give a mature Mandrake to anyone who gave me a good pair of shoes.","As soon as I made that offer, several people uploaded photographs of shoes, but I disliked most of them.","One of them had even tried to scam me, so I gave him a casual middle finger and left it at that.","Furthermore, the competition had died down after the dwarf—or rather, the dwarf’s friend—gave me a pair of shoes.","Everyone said that no matter how hard they tried, all their efforts would be meaningless before a dwarven artisan.","I also liked the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend, so I had stopped paying attention to the matter.","’But this person...’","This registered user was different. Despite how much time had passed, he had continued working on them.","Of course, if he had put in all that effort only to produce a disappointing result, I would have ignored him.","└ There wasn’t even a single scream. Those shoes must be seriously sturdy, hahaha.","└ Maybe he’s just gritting his teeth and enduring it in silence, hahaha.","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A photograph revealing his masked face) I knew you would say that, so I filmed this as well. I recorded it with a crystal orb.","└ Damn, look at how thorough he is, hahahaha.","└ What’s with the mask? It looks like something you’d wear to a ball. Is he a noble?","└ Who’s the person hitting him with the sledgehammer?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: My son.","└ Hahahahahahahahaha!","└ What a devoted son, damn, hahahahaha!","└ Even if he’s your son, he’s hitting you way too hard, hahahaha!","(A video of someone repeatedly striking the shoe wearer’s foot with a sledgehammer)","└ S-Sir ;; Y-You can stop now ;;","└ How many times is he going to hit him? Damn, hahahaha!","└ At this rate, his foot is going to be completely crushed ;;","If only it hadn’t been for that video.","No matter how durable the shoes were, who would strike them with a sledgehammer while someone was still wearing them?","Then again, that made him even more trustworthy. Hadn’t he put his own body on the line to prove the quality of his product?","After staring at it uneasily for a moment, I hurriedly left a comment before he injured himself any further.","There were no issues with the shoes’ performance, so I could safely proceed with the trade.","└ Wild Grylls: S-Sir, you don’t have to do that. You aren’t injured, are you?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: (A video of him taking his foot out of the shoe after the sledgehammer test) Correct.","└ Wow. He’s thorough as hell. Now that’s proper product verification ;;","└ Who made those? I want a pair.","└ I’ll buy them!","└ Buy me a pair too!","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey. You win. I think those are better than the pair my friend made ;;","└ The dwarf has declared defeat!","└ If even a dwarf admits defeat, they must be the real deal, hahaha.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll buy them. It’s already late, though. Can we make the exchange tomorrow?","└ I’ll Become a Duke: That is possible.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll send you a private message.","I sent him a message because it seemed we needed to discuss the matter privately.","Despite his stiff manner of speaking, he was clearly a passionate person, which made me like him.","[Wild Grylls: Hello, I’ll Become a Duke. I saw the shoes. You need a mature Mandrake, correct?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: You don’t need anything else?]","[I’ll Become a Duke: I do not. I urgently need a mature Mandrake.]","He urgently needed a mature Mandrake. I could sense the desperation in his words.","Someone close to him was probably suffering from an illness.","Otherwise, he would have no reason to reject everything else and insist solely on the mature Mandrake.","’He seems trustworthy.’","Both the video and his messages suggested that he was someone I could trust.","After telling him I would send the mature Mandrake tomorrow, I closed the gallery window.","Tomorrow would be my fifteenth day—exactly half a month—and I also planned to consume the inner core.","Building the furnace and completing my trade with I’ll Become a Duke...","I had plenty to do.","’The Guardian won’t wake up while I’m asleep, will it?’","Fortunately, nothing like that happened.","\"Ah. What the hell? What is this now?\"","Except that the entire section I had worked so hard to mine had completely regenerated.","I didn’t want an unlimited supply, but it looked like I was going to be forced to enjoy one.","’Is it a planarian or something?’","Planarian mithril.","I had no idea what kind of horrifying hybrid this was."]},{"title":"Chapter 118","paragraphs":["Alloy (1)","By now, I was tired of even saying, \"I’ve seen everything.\"","Everything in the Forest of Four Seasons was one enormous, unsolvable mystery.","It would be best to accept things quickly and move on. Hadn’t I recently encountered a talking gorilla?","I should probably just... go with the flow. While keeping meticulous records, of course.","’Why is everything here useless to me?’","What I needed were survival supplies, not resources like this.","Of course, I could use those resources to craft armor and various other tools.","However, that would take far too long, and I didn’t even have a furnace.","They were the very definition of a white elephant. I wasn’t even particularly good at knapping stone tools like a primitive man from the Paleolithic era.","’It’s not like I can sell this, either.’","I sighed. It seemed impossible to extract this mithril through ordinary mining.","Unless I carved out the entire floor around it, I had no choice but to leave it alone.","Still, if I looked at it positively, I had an unlimited supply of resources.","If I could build a furnace and acquire the necessary skills as a blacksmith, I couldn’t ask for anything more.","’The problem is that it’ll take years at the very least.’","I sighed again before turning around. Whatever the case, I still had work to do.","My daily routine began in the morning. By now, it had become familiar.","I went up to the river, caught fish, and ate my fill.","For some reason, only one fish had been caught today, which was slightly disappointing.","’Good thing I’ve stored some from the previous days.’","I still had plenty for now. However, it would become a problem if I continued catching only one fish a day.","After having breakfast with my animal companions, I got to work.","My first task was to send the mature Mandrake to I’ll Become a Duke.","After that, I planned to visit the Orichalcum Cave and retrieve some orichalcum.","I had originally intended to use the orichalcum to make a door, but that plan had been abandoned, so I no longer needed the mineral.","Still, I figured there was no harm in having a few pieces, so I planned to keep them in reserve.","’Let’s build the furnace after lunch.’","It looked like the task would require both brains and strength, so it would be better to take my time.","According to the dwarf, molten metal was nearly as hot as lava.","He also mentioned that mithril had a higher melting point, so it would be even hotter.","’I also need charcoal, right?’","Charcoal was essential for producing higher temperatures.","Since I needed enough heat to melt metal, I would require much greater firepower.","That alone made my prospects look bleak, but there was at least one fortunate aspect.","The furnace didn’t need to be very large. Since all it had to do was melt the ore, a small one would suffice.","Even so, I couldn’t afford to relax. I would be handling fire, the very definition of a double-edged sword.","’I’m glad I’ve been steadily collecting charcoal.’","Until now, I had only used it for laundry and as a deodorizer. I never imagined I would use it in a furnace.","Charcoal truly was divine and all-purpose. I would have to work on producing more of it in the future.","After completing my preparations, I set out to obtain the mature Mandrake and the orichalcum.","As always, I carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back and brought Wonmo, my adorable bodyguard, along with me.","Wham! Thud! Smack!","\"Gueek! Gueeek! Gweeeek!\"","First came the mature Mandrake.","By now, I was familiar with the capture method.","Though calling it a \"capture method\" was generous when all I did was beat it senseless. Not that it mattered.","After capturing the mature Mandrake, I headed toward the Orichalcum Cave.","Fortunately, I didn’t encounter any dangerous animals along the way.","It was partly because I was following a familiar route and partly because I remained thoroughly vigilant.","’Orichalcum acquired. But does this not need to be refined either?’","That thought occurred to me as I picked up several chunks of orichalcum scattered across the ground.","Perhaps it didn’t need to be processed separately, considering Princess Cheonggu and King Leor had used theirs as soon as they received it.","Then again, that might be a unique characteristic of orichalcum. I would have to ask the dwarf.","[Wild Grylls has registered an item for trade.]","[Wild Grylls: Here it is. I sincerely hope everything works out for you.]","[I’ll Become a Duke: Thank you very much! May the Goddess’s blessing be with you!]","After returning to the cave, I exchanged items with I’ll Become a Duke.","Judging by his mention of the Goddess’s blessing, perhaps he was from the Holy Kingdom.","’Come to think of it, the mature Mandrake can be traded without any problems.’","Had the system determined that mature Mandrakes lacked self-awareness?","They didn’t merely let out terrifying battle cries; they even operated as a colony.","It was truly strange, but I decided to accept it since the outcome benefited me. Thinking too deeply about it would only make my head hurt.","’These are nice. Sturdy too.’","Just as the video had shown, the shoes I received from I’ll Become a Duke prioritized durability.","They were so tough that they were even better than the shoes made by the dwarf’s friend.","However, that durability came at the expense of comfort and convenience.","’Still, these are perfect for me.’","I could wear the dwarf’s shoes when revisiting places I had already explored and I’ll Become a Duke’s shoes when exploring new areas.","That seemed like the best way to categorize them. Inside the cave, I could simply wear sneakers.","’I should get just one more pair.’","Since the two pairs served different purposes, I needed a spare as well.","With that in mind, I immediately posted in the gallery. People might assume the offer had already ended.","Title: Looking for One More Pair of Shoes","Wild Grylls","I safely received the shoes provided by Passing Dwarf and I’ll Become a Duke.","However, since I’ll likely use them for different purposes, I think I need one more pair as a backup.","As before, I’ll give a mature Mandrake to whoever provides a suitable spare pair.","└ Heavenly Demon: When dost thou intend to give this lady her sword?","└ Wild Grylls: I-I’ll give it to you soon!","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady was merely jesting. There is no need to hurry, so take thy time.","└ SwordMaster: You’re giving her a sword?","└ Heavenly Demon: He says he shall personally craft a sword of true silver for this lady.","└ SwordMaster: Damn it. I’m a little jealous of that. Even I’ve never used a sword made of mithril ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmph. Perhaps thou shouldst have been more generous.","└ SwordMaster: I gave him an elixir too, you know ;;","└ Wild Grylls: The Heavenly Demon gave me her own sword, so I’m giving her this one in return. Would you like one too, SwordMaster?","└ Heavenly Demon: That fool. So this was his intention all along.","└ SwordMaster: Honestly, I’m tempted, but I’m fine. Unlike a certain someone, I’m strong enough even with a cheap sword.","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady possesses a mace.","└ SwordMaster: You evil bitch.","└ Is Grylls making it himself? I thought he asked the dwarf to do it.","└ Passing Dwarf: That was the plan, but the mana concentration inside the mithril was too high, so I returned it. It’ll explode the moment it melts.","└ Is orichalcum safe?","└ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Orichalcum is safe because of its mana-absorbing properties. But that applies exclusively to orichalcum.","└ So Grylls was handing out bombs?","└ Looks like he was planning to assassinate them.","└ Wild Grylls: I didn’t know either ;; That’s why I have to make it myself.","└ Princess Cheonggu: I’m making good use of the orichalcum you gave me. The security recording orb I mentioned yesterday is ready, so just let me know whenever you want it.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. How do I view the recorded footage?]","[Princess Cheonggu: Tap it twice again to close its eye, then tap it three times. To watch the recording, press and hold it. One thing to keep in mind is that the recording will be deleted automatically once you watch it, so be careful!]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll be careful. And thank you.]","[Princess Cheonggu: If you’re grateful, what should you say?]","[Wild Grylls: I hope Chae-U wins next season!]","[Princess Cheonggu: Hehe. Very good.]","The moment I saw Princess Cheonggu’s comment, I sent her a private message.","I planned to give her orichalcum in return. The more of it she had, the better.","[Princess Cheonggu: If you tap the orb twice, it’ll open like an eye. Just think of it as watching whatever direction the eye is facing.]","I examined the security orb I had received from Princess Cheonggu.","It was mostly blackish-purple and about the size of my face.","’Am I supposed to hang it up like a block of fermented soybean paste?’","Installing it would be another chore. Still, I planned to remain inside the cave all day, so I had no immediate need for it.","After looking it over from various angles, I tapped the security orb twice.","Flash!","\"Whoa.\"","Just as Princess Cheonggu had explained, it opened like an eye. It resembled the eye of a reptile.","It looked terrifying. It practically radiated the message, I’m watching you.","Tap, tap, tap—","When I tapped it three times, the eye quietly closed. I then pressed and held it with my finger.","With a flash, a holographic screen appeared.","The hologram displayed my face as seen from above.","\"Wow.\"","No matter how I looked at it, my skin had improved. I couldn’t find a single blemish.","I stared at my face in the hologram for a while before closing it.","Now that I had confirmed how the security orb worked, it was time to begin training. I couldn’t afford to skip even a single day.","’Starting today, I’ll also be consuming the inner core.’","I planned to receive the second mnemonic verse from the Heavenly Demon.","The gist of the verse was not to surrender my body to the heavens, but to read their flow.","I was worried that it would contain expressions even more difficult than those in the first verse, but that was fine.","If I didn’t understand something, I could keep struggling with it until I did. I had never expected it to be easy.","’I’ll eat the inner core after lunch, once I’ve had time to digest.’","The fish also produced effects similar to those of a spiritual medicine.","If I consumed the inner core immediately after lunch, I might overdose.","Since I needed to avoid danger whenever possible, it would be better to wait until the meal had mostly been digested.","’I also need to catch a crab for the dwarf.’","It was going to be a busy day. I couldn’t postpone anything.","In that case, I should begin working right away. Once I finished lunch, I planned to start building the furnace.","The furnace didn’t need to be large. It only had to melt the mithril into molten metal.","However, I would have to obtain the necessary materials from the dwarf.","The most important component was heat-resistant stone. It needed to withstand temperatures exceeding a thousand degrees.","’The dwarf said he’d provide that.’","I had also heard that he would give me bellows to pump air into the furnace. He was genuinely supplying me with everything.","When I asked whether he was really fine with that, he said sharpening a mithril sword would be sufficient compensation.","Whenever he acted like this, I couldn’t help thinking how dwarven he was.","Flop! Flop!","When I went up to the river, I found two fish caught in the trap. That was a relief, at least.","I put them in the oven, ate my meal, and began making preparations.","Before that, however, there was something I needed to check—the mithril at the rear of the cave.","An endlessly regenerating supply of mithril was certainly useful, but there was something I wanted to know.","’How exactly does it regenerate?’","Its regenerative ability was remarkable, like that of a planarian.","Moreover, only the section I had mined yesterday had regenerated.","I also wondered where its core was located. At the same time, I was afraid it might awaken like the Guardian.","’I can’t let my guard down.’","I had mined quite a lot of mithril yesterday.","All I had to do now was melt it and pour it into a mold.","Once I decided that all my preparations were complete, I sent the dwarf a message.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. You there?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Did you catch the crab?]","[Wild Grylls: I’ll catch it after building the furnace. I also want your advice.]","[Passing Dwarf: Advice about what?]","[Wild Grylls: Mithril is an extremely rare mineral, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: Calling it rare doesn’t even begin to cover it. There are countless mines in the world, yet whenever someone finds mithril, it makes the newspapers. What do you think?]","[Wild Grylls: Is orichalcum the same?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Most of it ends up in Magic Towers, but it’s just as rare as mithril. For reference, the newspapers went wild when you discovered the Orichalcum Cave.]","So it was that significant.","Since I was stuck in here, I knew nothing about what was happening outside.","People occasionally mentioned something appearing in the newspapers, but I had never paid attention. I assumed they were just shitposting.","[Passing Dwarf: Why are you asking, anyway? Are you trying to rub it in my face?]","[Wild Grylls: No. I want an expert’s opinion.]","[Passing Dwarf: Hmm. Thou hast some discernment. What dost thou wish to ask, foolish mortal?]","[Wild Grylls: Ugh ;; Maybe I should just find another dwarf.]","[Passing Dwarf: You’ll hardly find another dwarf specializing in metallurgy who wastes his time on the gallery, hahaha.]","[Wild Grylls: Sigh. You know how I currently have both mithril and orichalcum?]","[Passing Dwarf: Are you bragging?]","[Wild Grylls: Let me finish talking. What do you think would happen if I melted them together and made a sword from the mixture?]","An alloy of one rare mineral and another.","That was what I wanted.","There was so much of both around me that I could practically trip over them, so they no longer felt particularly remarkable.","However, outsiders—especially dwarves—would react very differently.","[Passing Dwarf: An alloy? You want to combine mithril and orichalcum?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. Doesn’t that sound good?]","[Passing Dwarf: You’re talking about using caviar to make fried rice, hahahaha.]","The dwarf laughed as though the idea were utterly absurd.","But then—","[Passing Dwarf: Let’s try it immediately. Do you need anything? Tell me what you need. I’ll get all of it for you.]","[Wild Grylls: So it’s a good idea?]","[Passing Dwarf: My balls are trembling with excitement right now.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s fucking disgusting ::]","In the end, he was still a dwarf."]},{"title":"Chapter 119","paragraphs":["Alloy (2)","There was one thing men could never resist.","Something that looked utterly stupid but also incredibly fun. Pure entertainment that appealed directly to their instincts.","Most of those ideas were idiotic and frequently caused accidents, but one couldn’t always choose the safest path.","And what if the likelihood of success seemed extremely high? What if there were so many opportunities that even failure could simply be laughed off?","That was how an unstoppable bulldozer who feared no failure was born.","It was fun, and its performance was practically guaranteed. An endeavor that offered both romance and practicality.","There was no resisting it.","The dwarf cared more about the romance, while I cared more about the practical benefits. We made an excellent team.","[Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you heat-resistant bricks, so use them to build it. You’ll have to coat the outside with mud yourself.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. Is there anything else? Like a container for the molten metal.]","[Passing Dwarf: I’ll give you that too. But it’s damn heavy, so be careful. Even professionals often make mistakes while pouring molten metal.]","[Wild Grylls: How should I install the bellows?]","[Passing Dwarf: Since you’re only using the furnace to melt the metals, making a hole in the side should work. Just make the opening fairly long.]","One by one, I obtained the materials and instructions needed to build a makeshift furnace from the dwarf.","The dwarf provided most of the materials, but assembling them was my responsibility.","In truth, the assembly itself was much easier than building the oven.","I wasn’t going to refine the metals separately. All I had to do was melt them.","I stacked the bricks I had received from the dwarf into a square structure, then plastered the outside with mud.","I didn’t forget to leave an opening for the bellows.","The furnace was approximately fifty centimeters wide and long, while its height rose slightly above my knees.","However, it needed to become narrower toward the top, naturally, to retain as much heat as possible.","Lastly, I had the container for holding the mithril and orichalcum, along with the tongs needed to move it.","I thought that was everything, but the dwarf had given me something else as well.","[Wild Grylls: What’s this blue powder? It isn’t some kind of drug, is it?]","[Passing Dwarf: Snort it straight up your nose. It’ll send you to heaven.]","[Wild Grylls: Sorry ;; Do I add it to the molten metal?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. No one has ever made an alloy of mithril and orichalcum before, so I gave it to you just in case. Adding that powder should help them mix properly. Impurities might rise to the surface, so skim them off carefully.]","According to the dwarf, it was made from finely ground and processed mana stones.","He explained that it was useful when producing alloys.","I had no reason to reject something that could help, so I gladly accepted it.","’I received the mold too.’","Finally, I also received the mold. It came with a lid.","It seemed that the molten metal was supposed to be poured through a hole in the exact center of the lid.","Creak—","When I carefully opened it, I found the shape of a longsword carved into the mold.","Since it was a mold used by dwarves, there should be no risk of the molten metal melting through it.","I closed the lid again and listened to the dwarf’s precautions.","If the dwarf wanted, I planned to make more of the alloy, and I would also give him the crab soon.","[Passing Dwarf: I’m emphasizing this again—always be careful around molten metal. I’m serious.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay, okay. Got it.]","[Passing Dwarf: If you get hurt, I won’t get to touch the mithril-orichalcum alloy.]","[Wild Grylls: You bastard, hahaha.]","[Passing Dwarf: Seriously, if you spill the molten metal, just run as far away as possible. That’s your best option.]","[Wild Grylls: Because it might splash everywhere?]","[Passing Dwarf: That too, but mainly because even I don’t know what will happen.]","He also warned that the molten metal might splatter like hot oil, so I absolutely had to wear protective equipment.","I considered wearing a helmet, but decided against it because it would only obstruct my vision.","Instead, I received a pair of goggles from the dwarf. They were a spare pair he had.","One might argue that I was receiving far too much from him, but it was fine.","I couldn’t tell whether he was being sincere or joking. The fact that he was a dwarf made it even harder to tell.","In any case, all the preparations were complete. All that remained was to put the plan into action.","’He said an eight-to-two ratio would be best, right?’","It was the ratio recommended by the dwarf. Naturally, mithril accounted for the larger portion.","Orichalcum had a strong affinity for mana, but it wasn’t as durable as mithril.","Rattle—","I poured about half the charcoal I had accumulated into the makeshift furnace.","It was such a waste that it nearly brought tears to my eyes, but I was willing to sacrifice it for the sword.","’I should build a dedicated charcoal kiln too.’","After building one thing, I immediately found myself needing another.","Moreover, charcoal could be used almost anywhere. It was an exceptionally versatile material.","I stared at the charcoal inside the furnace, decided there was enough, and moved on to the next step.","’It really is as heavy as the dwarf said.’","It was a thick, wide container capable of withstanding extreme heat.","It was already heavy when lifted normally, but since I had to use the tongs for safety, it felt twice as heavy.","Hoping the minerals inside would melt properly, I placed the container inside the furnace.","’Now I just have to light the fire—’","Whoosh!","I threw a burning branch onto the pile of charcoal.","After a while, the charcoal began glowing red, and the heat gradually intensified.","\"Ah. Wait.\"","Now that I thought about it, I should have lit a fire at the bottom first and then added the charcoal. I had reversed the order.","I cursed my own stupidity, but what could I do? I had already thrown the burning branch in.","As the charcoal gradually heated up, I checked to make sure I hadn’t forgotten anything.","\"Ppareumbo, take Wonmo somewhere farther away.\"","\"....\"","\"Kkyuu?\"","Just in case, I asked Ppareumbo to take Wonmo away from the area.","Now it was time to concentrate.","As the furnace gradually heated up, I grasped the bellows with both hands.","It was common knowledge that fire burned more intensely when supplied with oxygen.","Fwoooosh—","I slowly pulled the bellows open, filling them with air.","Whoooom!","Then I pumped the air directly into the furnace.","Fwoooosh!","The flames inside the furnace became far fiercer than before. I could tell from the sound alone.","I worked the bellows vigorously, helping the charcoal produce even more heat.","Whoom! Whoooom!","The more air I pumped into the furnace, the more violently the flames raged.","But it still wasn’t enough.","I continued working the bellows until the flames began turning white.","From time to time, I added more charcoal to increase the intensity even further. Since this was my first attempt, I grew slightly anxious that I might fail.","Rooooar!","Eventually, all the charcoal ignited, producing a fierce blaze.","The flames seemed to fluctuate between yellow and white.","This should be enough.","I stopped working the bellows and wiped away my sweat.","Despite standing some distance away, I could feel the tremendous heat.","I was reluctant to approach, but I had no choice if I wanted to inspect the minerals.","Rooooar!","\"Ugh...\"","I frowned. Even moving slightly closer made the skin on my face sting.","Still, I needed to confirm whether the metals were melting properly. I endured the heat and inspected them.","’The container is intact... and the minerals seem to have shrunk.’","Their size had visibly decreased. The change in the orichalcum was especially noticeable.","Liquid streamed down the surface of the mithril as though it were sweating.","The minerals were melting.","My hard work was finally producing results.","’I should add more charcoal and keep working the bellows.’","Now that I had confirmed the minerals were melting, all that remained was to maintain the fire.","I continued pumping the bellows vigorously before gradually retreating from the heat.","I hadn’t been working for very long, yet the heat had caused sweat to pour from my body like rain.","’That dwarf did this every day?’","And I was only using a makeshift furnace. The dwarf must have worked in an even harsher environment.","No one’s work was ever easy, especially work connected to the very foundations of civilization.","Others had been enduring these hardships on my behalf, yet I had lived without appreciating them.","’I should sprinkle in some of this powder too.’","Following the dwarf’s instructions, I sprinkled in the blue powder.","The minerals were now about halfway melted and had become soft and sludgy.","I stirred them with the tongs to help them melt more evenly, then sent the dwarf a message.","[Wild Grylls: (A video of the melting minerals) They’re melting. I’m sweating like crazy ;;]","[Passing Dwarf: Tough, isn’t it?]","[Wild Grylls: How did you do this every day?]","[Passing Dwarf: It’s fine once you get used to it. An expert can even drink molten metal, hahaha.]","[Wild Grylls: Want a sip?]","[Passing Dwarf: I prefer booze to molten metal.]","Of course he did. I chuckled.","Since even the mithril was melting, it might not be a bad idea to keep him updated in real time.","[Passing Dwarf: Ah, right. You’ll need to quench it too. I completely forgot.]","[Wild Grylls: Quench it? I’ve heard of that, but do I really need to?]","[Passing Dwarf: Of course you do. It’s a weapon. I’ll give you some oil, so find a suitable metal container and fill it.]","[Wild Grylls: Why oil instead of water?]","[Passing Dwarf: If you use water and mess it up, the sword might break. Oil is better.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay.]","[Passing Dwarf: Don’t panic if it catches fire. That’s normal.]","An expert really was different. He even explained useful tips like these in detail.","However, regardless of how many tips he gave me, I was still the one who had to do everything.","After preparing the oil for quenching, I looked inside the furnace.","Bubble, bubble, bubble—","The mithril and orichalcum had completely melted and were beginning to boil.","Something resembling impurities floated on the surface, so I immediately skimmed it off.","How did I skim it off? By using yet another tool the dwarf had given me.","Perhaps because I had sprinkled in the blue powder, the impurities were easily filtered out, leaving behind pure molten metal.","’Now I just have to pour it into the mold.’","This was the most important moment.","I swallowed nervously and grasped the container with the tongs.","It had been heavy when empty, but with molten metal inside, it was considerably heavier.","Just in case, I circulated mana throughout my body and slowly carried it toward the mold.","Then I carefully tilted the container over the small hole in the center of the mold.","Trickle, trickle, trickle—","I was supposed to stop once the molten metal filled the hole. That was the method the dwarf had taught me.","However, I couldn’t pause midway through pouring. Molten metal cooled quickly.","Focusing completely, I carefully watched the hole.","I could feel the strain gradually building in my forearms, but I endured it.","Trickle, trickle—pour!","Now!","The moment the hole could no longer contain the molten metal, I immediately stopped.","A little molten metal remained in the container, but that didn’t matter. I had plenty of raw material anyway.","I set down the container and tilted the mold slightly.","The molten metal filling the hole spilled out.","This step was essential because the metal couldn’t be allowed to harden while completely blocking the hole.","\"Phew.\"","I exhaled. My first attempt had gone fairly well.","Now I only had to wait for the molten metal to harden somewhat.","[Wild Grylls: (A video of the mold filled with molten metal) I’m almost finished.]","[Passing Dwarf: Pant... Pant...]","[Wild Grylls: ;;]","Just how excited was he that he couldn’t even form words?","Chuckling, I waited for the molten metal to harden.","I had heard that it usually took around ten to fifteen minutes.","I could clean up while I waited. The furnace came first.","’I have no choice but to wait until the charcoal burns out.’","Most of the charcoal had already turned gray rather than black.","Even if I didn’t extinguish it myself, it would eventually go out on its own.","’I’ve been fairly fortunate despite all my misfortunes.’","I wiped the sweat streaming down my body with a towel.","If the minerals hadn’t come in solid chunks, I would have struggled far more than this.","I would also have to make a dagger and a spare sword later, so it seemed I still had plenty of hardship ahead of me.","’Has enough time passed?’","After waiting a while, I slowly opened the mold’s lid.","A beautifully shaped sword appeared before my eyes.","It was an alloy of green mithril and blackish-purple orichalcum.","’It’s surprisingly dull in color.’","I wouldn’t describe it as beautiful. It was simply... plain and gloomy.","It was neither green nor blackish-purple, but an ordinary silver. A particularly dark silver, at that.","I was slightly disappointed, but its appearance didn’t matter as long as it performed well.","I unconsciously reached for the sword, only to flinch and stop myself.","’That was close.’","I had assumed it had cooled, but I felt intense heat as soon as my hand approached it.","I tapped it several times with the tongs the dwarf had provided to check whether it had hardened, then carefully picked it up.","Now all I had to do was slowly lower it into the container of oil and quench it.","Hiss! Fwoosh!","Just as the dwarf had warned, the oil caught fire the moment I inserted the sword.","However, he had said there was little risk of an accident, so I remained calm and continued quenching it.","After repeating the process several times, the oil no longer caught fire.","And with that, my first sword was complete.","\"Phew.\"","I exhaled as I gazed at the sword, wisps of smoke still rising from it.","Seeing the finished product filled me with pride. It was a tool I had made with my own hands.","I would have liked to sharpen the blade myself, but I should leave that pleasure to the dwarf.","He had begged me to let him hold the sword, saying that he would be satisfied as long as he could sharpen its blade.","[Wild Grylls: (A photograph of the completed sword) It’s finished. It has cooled down. Want me to send it now?]","[Passing Dwarf: Please... just let me sharpen the blade....]","[Wild Grylls: I-I’ll send it over ;;]","He sounded so desperate that I couldn’t even bring myself to tease him.","I sent the longsword to the dwarf.","’I sweated a lot, but it wasn’t particularly difficult.’","After briefly rehydrating, I checked the time.","There was still plenty left. I could use it to complete my remaining tasks.","’Wonmo is... asleep.’","As it happened, Wonmo was taking a nap.","This seemed like a good opportunity to find the crab I had promised the dwarf.","I hung the security orb I had received from Princess Cheonggu above the cave entrance.","How did I hang it? Just like a block of fermented soybean paste. Of course, I made sure it wouldn’t sway.","\"Ppareumbo, I’ll be back soon.\"","\"....\"","After saying goodbye to Ppareumbo, I left the shelter.","***","Around the same time, Gareth—the dwarf to whom Grylls had sent the sword—was staring at it in awe.","\"Daaamn...!\"","He exclaimed in admiration as he gazed at the sword Grylls had given him.","The blade was still blunt, and the grip had yet to be finished. That unfinished sword now rested in Gareth’s hands.","However, something about it was different.","When Grylls had crafted it, the sword had been dull and gloomy.","Shiiimmer—","But that was no longer the case.","Gareth stared at the sword, which now gleamed a brilliant green.","Blackish-purple points of starlight were embedded across its luminous green surface.","It looked as though an entire green galaxy had been captured within the blade.","\"This is so fucking cool.\"","Gareth murmured in pure enchantment."]}]);
